  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, 1, 'Explain Mohammad Ali Jinnah’s Two-Nation Theory.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q1a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Event 1: In country ‘A’, people of various linguistic backgrounds lived. However, the ruling class chose one language for official state affairs. This led to protests by speakers of other languages. Eventually, the rulers were compelled to recognise all languages. Event 2: In a certain country, various political parties participated in a national election. Among them, Party A won about 99% of the seats in the National Assembly. In the Provincial Assembly election, Party A won all but 12 seats. However, when the ruling authorities hesitated to hand over power, the country erupted in turmoil.
a. How many seats did the United Front win in the 1954 election?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q1b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Event 1: In country ‘A’, people of various linguistic backgrounds lived. However, the ruling class chose one language for official state affairs. This led to protests by speakers of other languages. Eventually, the rulers were compelled to recognise all languages. Event 2: In a certain country, various political parties participated in a national election. Among them, Party A won about 99% of the seats in the National Assembly. In the Provincial Assembly election, Party A won all but 12 seats. However, when the ruling authorities hesitated to hand over power, the country erupted in turmoil.
b. How does the Language Movement strengthen national consciousness?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q1c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Event 1: In country ‘A’, people of various linguistic backgrounds lived. However, the ruling class chose one language for official state affairs. This led to protests by speakers of other languages. Eventually, the rulers were compelled to recognise all languages. Event 2: In a certain country, various political parties participated in a national election. Among them, Party A won about 99% of the seats in the National Assembly. In the Provincial Assembly election, Party A won all but 12 seats. However, when the ruling authorities hesitated to hand over power, the country erupted in turmoil.
c. Which historical event in former East Pakistan is referred to in Event 1? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Event 1: In country ‘A’, people of various linguistic backgrounds lived. However, the ruling class chose one language for official state affairs. This led to protests by speakers of other languages. Eventually, the rulers were compelled to recognise all languages. Event 2: In a certain country, various political parties participated in a national election. Among them, Party A won about 99% of the seats in the National Assembly. In the Provincial Assembly election, Party A won all but 12 seats. However, when the ruling authorities hesitated to hand over power, the country erupted in turmoil.
d. “The election mentioned in Event 2 resembles a pre-independence election in our history, which led us toward independence”—Evaluate this statement.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, 2, 'What were the reasons behind the Muslim League’s defeat in the 1954 election?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch1-p16-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch1', 16, 3, 'Rimi was attentively watching a television program. In one scene, a leader, with a strong voice, declared support for implementing a political decision at a gathering of students and teachers. The students protested with shouts of “No, no.”
