  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, 1, 'How do countries around the world manage to coexist peacefully?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q1a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, NULL, 'In 2012, all the union chairmen of ‘A’ upazila gathered and appointed the upazila chairman as the head of the council. They formulated policies to ensure justice, discipline, and security in every union and pledged to follow them. They started working to resolve disputes, develop the area, and provide fundamental rights for the people. As a result, peace and order were established, and people began to live safely. When a dispute arose between two unions, the upazila chairman of ‘A’ intervened and resolved it. Inspired by the success of ‘A’ upazila, other upazilas also became interested in adopting similar policies.
a. What is the League of Nations?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q1b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, NULL, 'In 2012, all the union chairmen of ‘A’ upazila gathered and appointed the upazila chairman as the head of the council. They formulated policies to ensure justice, discipline, and security in every union and pledged to follow them. They started working to resolve disputes, develop the area, and provide fundamental rights for the people. As a result, peace and order were established, and people began to live safely. When a dispute arose between two unions, the upazila chairman of ‘A’ intervened and resolved it. Inspired by the success of ‘A’ upazila, other upazilas also became interested in adopting similar policies.
b. Explain the UN’s fundamental principle: “All member states of the United Nations shall have equal rights and equal sovereignty.”'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q1c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, NULL, 'In 2012, all the union chairmen of ‘A’ upazila gathered and appointed the upazila chairman as the head of the council. They formulated policies to ensure justice, discipline, and security in every union and pledged to follow them. They started working to resolve disputes, develop the area, and provide fundamental rights for the people. As a result, peace and order were established, and people began to live safely. When a dispute arose between two unions, the upazila chairman of ‘A’ intervened and resolved it. Inspired by the success of ‘A’ upazila, other upazilas also became interested in adopting similar policies.
c. The process of resolving disputes between the two unions in the stem—which UN principle does it resemble? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, NULL, 'In 2012, all the union chairmen of ‘A’ upazila gathered and appointed the upazila chairman as the head of the council. They formulated policies to ensure justice, discipline, and security in every union and pledged to follow them. They started working to resolve disputes, develop the area, and provide fundamental rights for the people. As a result, peace and order were established, and people began to live safely. When a dispute arose between two unions, the upazila chairman of ‘A’ intervened and resolved it. Inspired by the success of ‘A’ upazila, other upazilas also became interested in adopting similar policies.
d. “The peace efforts of ‘A’ upazila are similar to the United Nations’ global peace initiatives”— Give your opinion.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, 2, 'How is it possible to solve major problems of various countries?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch11-p112-q2a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch11', 112, NULL, '[Picture: A Bangladeshi army doctor is providing medical care in the United Nations mission in Sierra Leone — the photo shows a uniformed doctor examining an elderly man with a stethoscope; caption: A Bangladeshi army doctor is providing medical care in the United Nations mission in Sierra Leone.]
