  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, 1, 'Why is the turmeric ceremony considered part of folk culture?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q1a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Rakin lives in the village of Patar char. Every year in late autumn, when the new rice is harvested, his family makes traditional cakes and puddings. They share these treats with neighbours. Last year, Rakin also went to watch a traditional play with his father. He enjoys life a lot. On the other hand, his cousin Abir lives in their flat in Comilla. His father is a doctor, and his mother is a school teacher. Both are very busy. Abir stays alone most of the time and eats sandwiches or burgers when he is hungry.
a. What is meant by the material elements of folk culture?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q1b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Rakin lives in the village of Patar char. Every year in late autumn, when the new rice is harvested, his family makes traditional cakes and puddings. They share these treats with neighbours. Last year, Rakin also went to watch a traditional play with his father. He enjoys life a lot. On the other hand, his cousin Abir lives in their flat in Comilla. His father is a doctor, and his mother is a school teacher. Both are very busy. Abir stays alone most of the time and eats sandwiches or burgers when he is hungry.
b. What is the culture of Bangladesh? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q1c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Rakin lives in the village of Patar char. Every year in late autumn, when the new rice is harvested, his family makes traditional cakes and puddings. They share these treats with neighbours. Last year, Rakin also went to watch a traditional play with his father. He enjoys life a lot. On the other hand, his cousin Abir lives in their flat in Comilla. His father is a doctor, and his mother is a school teacher. Both are very busy. Abir stays alone most of the time and eats sandwiches or burgers when he is hungry.
c. Which type of urban culture is reflected in the passage? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Rakin lives in the village of Patar char. Every year in late autumn, when the new rice is harvested, his family makes traditional cakes and puddings. They share these treats with neighbours. Last year, Rakin also went to watch a traditional play with his father. He enjoys life a lot. On the other hand, his cousin Abir lives in their flat in Comilla. His father is a doctor, and his mother is a school teacher. Both are very busy. Abir stays alone most of the time and eats sandwiches or burgers when he is hungry.
d. Do Rakin and Abir enjoy the same kind of entertainment? Give your opinion.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, 2, 'What is a totem? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q2a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Shanta and Antara study at the same university. Shanta belongs to a small ethnic community in the Mymensingh region. Antara visits Shanta’s home there and learns that Shanta’s father lives at her mother’s house. Roads in their area have improved. People from their community are now getting educated, which has brought changes in their food, clothing, etc.
a. What is Gopi dance?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q2b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Shanta and Antara study at the same university. Shanta belongs to a small ethnic community in the Mymensingh region. Antara visits Shanta’s home there and learns that Shanta’s father lives at her mother’s house. Roads in their area have improved. People from their community are now getting educated, which has brought changes in their food, clothing, etc.
