  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q2c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Shanta and Antara study at the same university. Shanta belongs to a small ethnic community in the Mymensingh region. Antara visits Shanta’s home there and learns that Shanta’s father lives at her mother’s house. Roads in their area have improved. People from their community are now getting educated, which has brought changes in their food, clothing, etc.
c. Which ethnic group does Shanta belong to? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q2d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Shanta and Antara study at the same university. Shanta belongs to a small ethnic community in the Mymensingh region. Antara visits Shanta’s home there and learns that Shanta’s father lives at her mother’s house. Roads in their area have improved. People from their community are now getting educated, which has brought changes in their food, clothing, etc.
d. Do you think other ethnic communities, like Shanta’s, have experienced lifestyle changes? Give reasons to support your answer.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch2-p28-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch2', 28, 3, 'Even though the roof of Mongpru’s house was damaged, he couldn’t repair it since it was the month of Poush. They believed repairing it would bring misfortune.
