a. Proper use of local raw materials
b. Achieving self-reliance
c. Employment generation
d. Capital growth'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, 1, 'How does poultry farming by rural women contribute to the national economy?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'Tamiz Uddin cultivates various crops like rice, wheat, mustard, and corn on his own land with his three sons. His wife and daughters-in-law help with harvesting. In his free time, he runs a grocery shop. His younger brother, Ramiz Uddin, works in a garment factory, and his wife is a government primary school teacher.
d. Does Tamiz Uddin’s family contribute to the national economy? Evaluate.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, 2, 'What is a cottage industry? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q2a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'Jarina Begum, a poor widow in a village, once bought bamboo and cane from the market. With her two daughters, she crafted items such as trays, baskets, and vases. Her son Tamjid sold them at the market. Later, with advice from his father’s friend, Tamjid took a loan from a bank. They established a factory to make cakes, biscuits, and other food products, earning a substantial profit.
a. What is the purpose of establishing export processing zones?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q2b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'Jarina Begum, a poor widow in a village, once bought bamboo and cane from the market. With her two daughters, she crafted items such as trays, baskets, and vases. Her son Tamjid sold them at the market. Later, with advice from his father’s friend, Tamjid took a loan from a bank. They established a factory to make cakes, biscuits, and other food products, earning a substantial profit.
b. What is meant by informal economic activity? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q2c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'Jarina Begum, a poor widow in a village, once bought bamboo and cane from the market. With her two daughters, she crafted items such as trays, baskets, and vases. Her son Tamjid sold them at the market. Later, with advice from his father’s friend, Tamjid took a loan from a bank. They established a factory to make cakes, biscuits, and other food products, earning a substantial profit.
c. Which industry category do Jarina Begum’s products fall into? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q2d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'Jarina Begum, a poor widow in a village, once bought bamboo and cane from the market. With her two daughters, she crafted items such as trays, baskets, and vases. Her son Tamjid sold them at the market. Later, with advice from his father’s friend, Tamjid took a loan from a bank. They established a factory to make cakes, biscuits, and other food products, earning a substantial profit.
d. Evaluate Tamjid’s contribution to the economic development of Bangladesh.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch4-p45-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch4', 45, 3, 'What is meant by the processing industry? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p47-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Write down the attributes of a good citizen and discuss them in groups in the classroom.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p49-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 49, NULL, 'Think about the barriers to good citizenship and write them down on your khatas. Then write the list on a poster and hang it in classroom.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p50-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 50, NULL, 'What kind of misdeeds will a good citizen abstain from doing? Work in groups and make a list for presentation in classroom.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p51-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 51, NULL, 'Make and present a work-plan about how you are going to carry out your duties and responsibilities to the country.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p52-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 52, 1, 'How many basic qualities must a good citizen possess?
a. One
b. Two
c. Three
d. Four'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p52-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 52, 2, 'To be an intelligent citizen—
i. One must study
ii. One must vote for their own people
iii. One must work for national development
Which of the following is correct?
a. i
b. i and ii
c. i and iii
d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p52-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 52, 3, 'Topu was riding a rickshaw when he saw a car hit a pedestrian and try to flee. Topu quickly, with the help of others, caught the driver and handed him over to the police, and took the injured pedestrian to the nearby hospital.
Which quality is mainly reflected in Topu’s behaviour?
a. Intelligence
b. Self-control
c. Conscience
d. Confidence'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p52-q4', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 52, 4, 'Topu was riding a rickshaw when he saw a car hit a pedestrian and try to flee. Topu quickly, with the help of others, caught the driver and handed him over to the police, and took the injured pedestrian to the nearby hospital.
From Topu’s actions, we can conclude—
i. Topu has the qualities of a good citizen
ii. He is a valuable asset to Bangladesh
iii. People like him can help build a developed nation
Which of the following is correct?
a. i and ii
b. i and iii
c. ii and iii
d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, 1, 'How does selfishness hinder becoming a good citizen?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q1a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Dialogue between Two Friends Samiha: Lazin, did you read the news about the rickshaw puller in the newspaper a few days ago? Lazin: Yes, I did. Even after finding a bag containing one lakh taka left behind by a passenger in his rickshaw, he didn’t take it. Instead, he found the passenger’s address and returned all the money. Samiha: People like that rickshaw puller are exactly what our country needs. Truly, his wisdom and awareness are commendable.
a. Who are good citizens?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q1b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Dialogue between Two Friends Samiha: Lazin, did you read the news about the rickshaw puller in the newspaper a few days ago? Lazin: Yes, I did. Even after finding a bag containing one lakh taka left behind by a passenger in his rickshaw, he didn’t take it. Instead, he found the passenger’s address and returned all the money. Samiha: People like that rickshaw puller are exactly what our country needs. Truly, his wisdom and awareness are commendable.
b. Explain: “Communalism is a major obstacle to becoming a good citizen.”'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q1c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Dialogue between Two Friends Samiha: Lazin, did you read the news about the rickshaw puller in the newspaper a few days ago? Lazin: Yes, I did. Even after finding a bag containing one lakh taka left behind by a passenger in his rickshaw, he didn’t take it. Instead, he found the passenger’s address and returned all the money. Samiha: People like that rickshaw puller are exactly what our country needs. Truly, his wisdom and awareness are commendable.
c. Which quality of a good citizen is shown by the rickshaw puller in the stem? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Dialogue between Two Friends Samiha: Lazin, did you read the news about the rickshaw puller in the newspaper a few days ago? Lazin: Yes, I did. Even after finding a bag containing one lakh taka left behind by a passenger in his rickshaw, he didn’t take it. Instead, he found the passenger’s address and returned all the money. Samiha: People like that rickshaw puller are exactly what our country needs. Truly, his wisdom and awareness are commendable.
d. “The quality shown by the rickshaw puller is enough to be a good citizen”—Do you agree? Give reasons for your answer.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, 2, 'Why are good citizens considered valuable assets of a country?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q2a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Mr. Sobhan and Mr. Shekhar are friends. Mr. Sobhan is a government officer. He recently conducted a peaceful voting process at a polling station. Mr. Shekhar is a prominent businessman and won the Best Taxpayer Award this year. Both are very conscious about their children’s education. Mr. Sobhan invites Mr. Shekhar’s family to Eid and other festivals. Mr. Shekhar also invites Mr. Sobhan’s family to the Puja and other Hindu festivals. Both families celebrate their respective religious traditions freely.
a. What is self- control?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q2b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Mr. Sobhan and Mr. Shekhar are friends. Mr. Sobhan is a government officer. He recently conducted a peaceful voting process at a polling station. Mr. Shekhar is a prominent businessman and won the Best Taxpayer Award this year. Both are very conscious about their children’s education. Mr. Sobhan invites Mr. Shekhar’s family to Eid and other festivals. Mr. Shekhar also invites Mr. Sobhan’s family to the Puja and other Hindu festivals. Both families celebrate their respective religious traditions freely.
b. Explain: “Indifference is an obstacle to becoming a good citizen.”'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q2c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Mr. Sobhan and Mr. Shekhar are friends. Mr. Sobhan is a government officer. He recently conducted a peaceful voting process at a polling station. Mr. Shekhar is a prominent businessman and won the Best Taxpayer Award this year. Both are very conscious about their children’s education. Mr. Sobhan invites Mr. Shekhar’s family to Eid and other festivals. Mr. Shekhar also invites Mr. Sobhan’s family to the Puja and other Hindu festivals. Both families celebrate their respective religious traditions freely.
c. By practising their rituals independently, which rights are the two families exercising? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q2d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, NULL, 'Mr. Sobhan and Mr. Shekhar are friends. Mr. Sobhan is a government officer. He recently conducted a peaceful voting process at a polling station. Mr. Shekhar is a prominent businessman and won the Best Taxpayer Award this year. Both are very conscious about their children’s education. Mr. Sobhan invites Mr. Shekhar’s family to Eid and other festivals. Mr. Shekhar also invites Mr. Sobhan’s family to the Puja and other Hindu festivals. Both families celebrate their respective religious traditions freely.
d. “Mr. Sobhan and Mr. Shekhar not only enjoy rights but also fulfil duties”—Evaluate this statement.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch5-p53-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch5', 53, 3, 'What is meant by the fundamental rights of a citizen?'),
