  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p55-t2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 55, NULL, 'What kinds of disasters occur due to adverse weather in Bangladesh? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p57-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'What is greenhouse gas? How these gases are contributing to the increase in temperature in Bangladesh? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p57-t2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'What can man do to keep climate normal? Analyse.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p61-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 61, NULL, 'Make a list of disasters that occur in Bangladesh.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p61-t2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 61, NULL, 'Write a report on the nature of various kinds of natural disasters and damages caused by them.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p61-t3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 61, NULL, 'What can you do in case of flood, river erosion and cyclone situation in your area?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p62-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 62, 1, 'In which season does river erosion usually occur in Bangladesh?
a. Summer
b. Monsoon
c. Winter
d. Spring'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p62-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 62, 2, 'What causes river erosion in our country?
i. Rivers don’t have straight paths
ii. Weak structure of riverbanks
iii. Too many trees on riverbanks
Which is correct?
a. i and ii
b. i and iii
c. ii and iii
d. i, ii, and ii'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p62-t1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 62, NULL, 'Make a chart to show the sectors facing damage due to climate change.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q1a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Zayan went out with his father. First, they visited the floating market on the Sandhya River. After speaking to a local person, they learned his home was submerged by the river. Now he works as a day labourer. Then they headed toward Kuakata. On the way, they saw many brick kilns. At Kuakata beach, Zayan was disturbed to see plastic bottles and food wrappers littered everywhere. He asked his father why people spoil such a beautiful beach and harm the environment. His father replied, “It’s not just these behaviours—many human actions are putting our country and world at risk.”
a. What is the weather?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q1b', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Zayan went out with his father. First, they visited the floating market on the Sandhya River. After speaking to a local person, they learned his home was submerged by the river. Now he works as a day labourer. Then they headed toward Kuakata. On the way, they saw many brick kilns. At Kuakata beach, Zayan was disturbed to see plastic bottles and food wrappers littered everywhere. He asked his father why people spoil such a beautiful beach and harm the environment. His father replied, “It’s not just these behaviours—many human actions are putting our country and world at risk.”
b. Explain the influence of monsoon winds on Bangladesh’s climate.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q1c', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Zayan went out with his father. First, they visited the floating market on the Sandhya River. After speaking to a local person, they learned his home was submerged by the river. Now he works as a day labourer. Then they headed toward Kuakata. On the way, they saw many brick kilns. At Kuakata beach, Zayan was disturbed to see plastic bottles and food wrappers littered everywhere. He asked his father why people spoil such a beautiful beach and harm the environment. His father replied, “It’s not just these behaviours—many human actions are putting our country and world at risk.”
c. What disaster did Zayan learn about at the first location? Explain.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q1d', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Zayan went out with his father. First, they visited the floating market on the Sandhya River. After speaking to a local person, they learned his home was submerged by the river. Now he works as a day labourer. Then they headed toward Kuakata. On the way, they saw many brick kilns. At Kuakata beach, Zayan was disturbed to see plastic bottles and food wrappers littered everywhere. He asked his father why people spoil such a beautiful beach and harm the environment. His father replied, “It’s not just these behaviours—many human actions are putting our country and world at risk.”
d. Evaluate how logical Zayan’s father’s statement is.'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q3', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, 3, 'Rupsa, a girl from Cox’s Bazar, was listening to the radio at home. After hearing a warning, she and her family became frightened and left home for the shelter.
What warning did Rupsa hear?
a. Cyclone
b. Earthquake
c. River erosion
d. Tornado'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p63-q4', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 63, 4, 'Rupsa, a girl from Cox’s Bazar, was listening to the radio at home. After hearing a warning, she and her family became frightened and left home for the shelter.
Why was Rupsa frightened?
i. The whole area could be flooded quickly
ii. Another tremor might follow the first
iii. Delay in reaching the shelter in time
Which is correct?
a. i and ii
b. i and iii
c. ii and iii
d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p64-q1', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 64, 1, 'Explain: “Cold waves disrupt public life.”'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p64-q2', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 64, 2, 'Why do riverbanks erode?'),
  ('class7-bgs-en-ch6-p64-q2a', 'class7-bgs-en', 'class7-bgs-en-ch6', 64, NULL, 'Arif was watching a TV report titled “Natural Disasters in Bangladesh.” The first part showed how agricultural land in the northern region is drying and cracking. The second part demonstrated how natural disasters impact life and the environment in the coastal region, which is frequently affected by disasters due to its location.
