i. Removing ignorance
ii. Offering cooperation
iii. Providing true help
Which of the following is correct?
a. i & ii
b. ii & iii
c. i & iii
d. i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q1', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, 1, 'Why did Father Charles think of forming a cooperative Credit Society?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, 2, 'Why did Father Charles not want to help people with cash handouts?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q2a', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, NULL, 'Stimulus: Anima, a resident of Pahartali, is deeply religious and has strong moral values. She teaches people to be frugal and self-reliant. She helps by collecting surplus income from local people and forming a cooperative society. This society provides loans on easy terms to its members during times of need.
a. What is full name of the organization CCULB?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q2b', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, NULL, 'Stimulus: Anima, a resident of Pahartali, is deeply religious and has strong moral values. She teaches people to be frugal and self-reliant. She helps by collecting surplus income from local people and forming a cooperative society. This society provides loans on easy terms to its members during times of need.
b. What kind of work does Caritas do for the people of Bangladesh?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q2c', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, NULL, 'Stimulus: Anima, a resident of Pahartali, is deeply religious and has strong moral values. She teaches people to be frugal and self-reliant. She helps by collecting surplus income from local people and forming a cooperative society. This society provides loans on easy terms to its members during times of need.
c. Works of which organization of Father Young inspired Anima?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch10-p96-q2d', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch10', 96, NULL, 'Stimulus: Anima, a resident of Pahartali, is deeply religious and has strong moral values. She teaches people to be frugal and self-reliant. She helps by collecting surplus income from local people and forming a cooperative society. This society provides loans on easy terms to its members during times of need.
