d. Heavenly angel.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p71-q2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 71, 2, 'How are people united in brotherhood?
a. through service
b. through love
c. through sharing
d. through faith'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p71-t4', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 71, NULL, 'Write what sort of apostolic work you can do in your family, school and local society.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q1a', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, NULL, 'Stimulus: Due to Father Rupom''s love for the Church and his hard work the Church grew spiritually. But one young man of the Church, Shimanto, without the knowledge of the priest, starts working against the Church and tries to lead other young man astray. Upon realizing this, the church secretary informs the priest and suggests expelling Shimanto from the congregation. But the priest says, “No need to expel him. Give him a chance.” Gradually, Shimanto realizes his mistakes and returns to the right path.
a. What is meant by holy?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q1b', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, NULL, 'Stimulus: Due to Father Rupom''s love for the Church and his hard work the Church grew spiritually. But one young man of the Church, Shimanto, without the knowledge of the priest, starts working against the Church and tries to lead other young man astray. Upon realizing this, the church secretary informs the priest and suggests expelling Shimanto from the congregation. But the priest says, “No need to expel him. Give him a chance.” Gradually, Shimanto realizes his mistakes and returns to the right path.
b. Why did the Son of God come to earth?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q1c', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, NULL, 'Stimulus: Due to Father Rupom''s love for the Church and his hard work the Church grew spiritually. But one young man of the Church, Shimanto, without the knowledge of the priest, starts working against the Church and tries to lead other young man astray. Upon realizing this, the church secretary informs the priest and suggests expelling Shimanto from the congregation. But the priest says, “No need to expel him. Give him a chance.” Gradually, Shimanto realizes his mistakes and returns to the right path.
c. Through which of the priest’s teachings did Shimanto return to the right path? Explain.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q1d', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, NULL, 'Stimulus: Due to Father Rupom''s love for the Church and his hard work the Church grew spiritually. But one young man of the Church, Shimanto, without the knowledge of the priest, starts working against the Church and tries to lead other young man astray. Upon realizing this, the church secretary informs the priest and suggests expelling Shimanto from the congregation. But the priest says, “No need to expel him. Give him a chance.” Gradually, Shimanto realizes his mistakes and returns to the right path.
d. What could be the result of Shimanto’s holy life, in your opinion? Give your opinion based on textbook information.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q3', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, 3, 'Stimulus: Two brothers, who are siblings, are in a severe conflict over land. Observing this, an elder from the village, Mr. Milon, sits with them to discuss and establish peace between the two.
Whose inspiration helped Mr. Milon to take up the above work?
a. Priest
b. Church
c. Holy Spirit
d. Jesus Christ'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p72-q4', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 72, 4, 'Stimulus: Two brothers, who are siblings, are in a severe conflict over land. Observing this, an elder from the village, Mr. Milon, sits with them to discuss and establish peace between the two.
Through Mr. Milon’s actions in society –
i. Harmony will be established
ii. Love will increase
iii. Mutual dependence will grow
Which of the following is correct?
a. i & ii
b. ii & iii
c. i & iii
d. i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q1', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, 1, 'How did the Church begin?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, 2, 'Why is the Church holy?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q2a', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, NULL, 'Stimulus: Mother Teresa was a European and a Christian. But her love is open for people of all nations and religions. She never considered religion, nation or nationality differently. With her sisters who followed her, she established "Missionaries of Charity", a religious congregation to serve the humanity. She founded "Nirmal Hriday" (home for the destitutes), "Shishu Bhavan" (orphanage for the children), "Naba Jibon Abash" (home for the retarded children), "Prem Nibash" (resident for the lepers), and many others to extend her services for the people. She lived in the community with her sisters giving them responsibility to look after the various programs and she herself remains as their model.
a. What is the inspiration of apostolic work?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q2b', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, NULL, 'Stimulus: Mother Teresa was a European and a Christian. But her love is open for people of all nations and religions. She never considered religion, nation or nationality differently. With her sisters who followed her, she established "Missionaries of Charity", a religious congregation to serve the humanity. She founded "Nirmal Hriday" (home for the destitutes), "Shishu Bhavan" (orphanage for the children), "Naba Jibon Abash" (home for the retarded children), "Prem Nibash" (resident for the lepers), and many others to extend her services for the people. She lived in the community with her sisters giving them responsibility to look after the various programs and she herself remains as their model.
b. Why is Church holy?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q2c', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, NULL, 'Stimulus: Mother Teresa was a European and a Christian. But her love is open for people of all nations and religions. She never considered religion, nation or nationality differently. With her sisters who followed her, she established "Missionaries of Charity", a religious congregation to serve the humanity. She founded "Nirmal Hriday" (home for the destitutes), "Shishu Bhavan" (orphanage for the children), "Naba Jibon Abash" (home for the retarded children), "Prem Nibash" (resident for the lepers), and many others to extend her services for the people. She lived in the community with her sisters giving them responsibility to look after the various programs and she herself remains as their model.
c. What teaching of the Church inspired Mother Teresa to do the above works?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q2d', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, NULL, 'Stimulus: Mother Teresa was a European and a Christian. But her love is open for people of all nations and religions. She never considered religion, nation or nationality differently. With her sisters who followed her, she established "Missionaries of Charity", a religious congregation to serve the humanity. She founded "Nirmal Hriday" (home for the destitutes), "Shishu Bhavan" (orphanage for the children), "Naba Jibon Abash" (home for the retarded children), "Prem Nibash" (resident for the lepers), and many others to extend her services for the people. She lived in the community with her sisters giving them responsibility to look after the various programs and she herself remains as their model.
d. ''Church of Christ and Missionaries of Charity'' both are universal. Evaluate in the light of the stimulus.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch8-p73-q3', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch8', 73, 3, 'In what sense do we call the Church apostolic?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p75-t1', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 75, NULL, 'Take paper and pen. Write down the scripture given below in your own paper and meditate one minute silently, what God wants to tell us. “Be kind to one another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, as God in Christ forgave you.”(Ephesians 4:32) Share with others if you have forgiven anybody or if you have been forgiven for any fault.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p75-t2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 75, NULL, 'Think personally What would you do if same situation happens in your life.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p75-t3', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 75, NULL, 'Everyone write in paper personally and present, what you would do if you were in the place of Sagor'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p76-t4', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 76, NULL, 'Discuss the questions given below in group: 1. Share with others in group, if you have forgiven anybody anytime any day. 2. How can you win the heart of someone and truly forgive against whom you have the attitude of revenge? 3. How does the prayer teach you to forgive? 4. How can Jesus teach you to forgive?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p77-t5', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 77, NULL, 'Discuss the questions given below and prepare a report in group: 1. What behavior would I do with Nomita if I were in the place of Anna? 2. How did they feel in heart if they had really forgiven Anna and Sagar?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p78-t6', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 78, NULL, 'A reunion program can be arranged. As a result everyone may have a chance to go to each other to beg pardon and to forgive, and everybody shall get experience of forgiveness in reality.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p83-q1', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 83, 1, '"Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing."- Who said?
a. Peter
b. Stephan
c. John
d. Jesus'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p83-q2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 83, 2, 'How can one become tolerant?
a. By being patient
b. By forgiving
c. By being considerate
d. By serving'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p84-q3', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 84, 3, 'Stimulus: Prafulla lives abroad, but his heart remains in the village. He constantly visualizes the green paddy fields and river water of his village and hears the chirping of birds. He is amaged of thinking about surrounding nature and atmosphere. He has got a degree on environment from abroad. So he thinks how the atmosphere of the village can be saved. He returns to village and inspires all about this. The people are also inspired.
Which characteristic is exposed in Prophullo?
a. Cooperation
b. Endurance
c. Patriotism
d. Self-control'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p84-q4', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 84, 4, 'Stimulus: Prafulla lives abroad, but his heart remains in the village. He constantly visualizes the green paddy fields and river water of his village and hears the chirping of birds. He is amaged of thinking about surrounding nature and atmosphere. He has got a degree on environment from abroad. So he thinks how the atmosphere of the village can be saved. He returns to village and inspires all about this. The people are also inspired.
Prophullo will not get from this work –
i. Exaltation
ii. Peace
iii. Divine power
Which of the following is correct?
a. i & ii
b. ii & iii
c. i & iii
d. i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q1', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, 1, 'What does it mean by patriotism?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q1a', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Niloy, Ayon and Oishi are classmates. They go to school and play together. They three are very faithful friends. One day Ayon borrows a book from Oishi. Oishi wants back her book just one day before the exam. But Ayon says, "There is no prove that I have taken your book". Oishi gets a great shock. She informs the matter to Niloy. Getting angry Niloy beats Ayon. Ayon realizes his fault and gives back the book. All sorrows of Oishi fade away. But Niloy cannot endure Ayon any way.
a. What does endurance bring in our work?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q1b', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Niloy, Ayon and Oishi are classmates. They go to school and play together. They three are very faithful friends. One day Ayon borrows a book from Oishi. Oishi wants back her book just one day before the exam. But Ayon says, "There is no prove that I have taken your book". Oishi gets a great shock. She informs the matter to Niloy. Getting angry Niloy beats Ayon. Ayon realizes his fault and gives back the book. All sorrows of Oishi fade away. But Niloy cannot endure Ayon any way.
b. Why has God forgiven us?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q1c', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Niloy, Ayon and Oishi are classmates. They go to school and play together. They three are very faithful friends. One day Ayon borrows a book from Oishi. Oishi wants back her book just one day before the exam. But Ayon says, "There is no prove that I have taken your book". Oishi gets a great shock. She informs the matter to Niloy. Getting angry Niloy beats Ayon. Ayon realizes his fault and gives back the book. All sorrows of Oishi fade away. But Niloy cannot endure Ayon any way.
c. Which character reveals in Oishi? Explain it.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q1d', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Niloy, Ayon and Oishi are classmates. They go to school and play together. They three are very faithful friends. One day Ayon borrows a book from Oishi. Oishi wants back her book just one day before the exam. But Ayon says, "There is no prove that I have taken your book". Oishi gets a great shock. She informs the matter to Niloy. Getting angry Niloy beats Ayon. Ayon realizes his fault and gives back the book. All sorrows of Oishi fade away. But Niloy cannot endure Ayon any way.
d. Describe the outcome of the work of Niloy.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q2', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, 2, 'What do we need to express ourselves?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q2a', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Sujon and Moitri were going to school by a bus. Driver was driving the bus accordingly. Sujon was anxious thinking that the school gate would be closed. He was looking at his watch frequently and becoming averse to the driver. Suddenly the running bus was stopped. Sujon and other passengers were scolding the driver and speaking ill altogether without realizing what was happening out side. Realizing the worse situation, Oishi asked "Sujon, Why are you scolding the driver? He has no fault. He stopped the bus to avoid an accident. Keep patient you all, don’t be angry. Our creator will convey us safely.
a. What is patriotism?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q2b', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Sujon and Moitri were going to school by a bus. Driver was driving the bus accordingly. Sujon was anxious thinking that the school gate would be closed. He was looking at his watch frequently and becoming averse to the driver. Suddenly the running bus was stopped. Sujon and other passengers were scolding the driver and speaking ill altogether without realizing what was happening out side. Realizing the worse situation, Oishi asked "Sujon, Why are you scolding the driver? He has no fault. He stopped the bus to avoid an accident. Keep patient you all, don’t be angry. Our creator will convey us safely.
b. Why should we admire the rulers?'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q2c', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Sujon and Moitri were going to school by a bus. Driver was driving the bus accordingly. Sujon was anxious thinking that the school gate would be closed. He was looking at his watch frequently and becoming averse to the driver. Suddenly the running bus was stopped. Sujon and other passengers were scolding the driver and speaking ill altogether without realizing what was happening out side. Realizing the worse situation, Oishi asked "Sujon, Why are you scolding the driver? He has no fault. He stopped the bus to avoid an accident. Keep patient you all, don’t be angry. Our creator will convey us safely.
c. Which character is expressed on Moitri? Explain it.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q2d', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, NULL, 'Stimulus: Sujon and Moitri were going to school by a bus. Driver was driving the bus accordingly. Sujon was anxious thinking that the school gate would be closed. He was looking at his watch frequently and becoming averse to the driver. Suddenly the running bus was stopped. Sujon and other passengers were scolding the driver and speaking ill altogether without realizing what was happening out side. Realizing the worse situation, Oishi asked "Sujon, Why are you scolding the driver? He has no fault. He stopped the bus to avoid an accident. Keep patient you all, don’t be angry. Our creator will convey us safely.
d. Evaluate the importance of practicing the character of Moitri in personal and social life.'),
  ('class7-christian-en-ch9-p85-q3', 'class7-christian-en', 'class7-christian-en-ch9', 85, 3, 'What does it mean by endurance?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p2-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 2, 1, 'Now answer these questions. 1. Do you speak English with your teacher? If you do, when and how often?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p2-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 2, 2, 'Now answer these questions. 2. Do you speak English with your friends and classmates? If so, how often?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p2-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 2, 3, 'Now answer these questions. 3. If you speak English outside the class, where do you speak it?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p2-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 2, 4, 'Now answer these questions. 4. Do you watch any English programmes on TV? What programmes do you watch?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 1, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 1. A: __________ you lend me your English book for a day? B: Sorry, I __________. I need to read it tonight.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q1-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 1, 'Make requests using the clues. 1. You want someone to help you with the washing.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 2, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 2. A: Could you give me 50 taka? B: Sorry, I __________. I have only 20 taka with me.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 2, 'Make requests using the clues. 2. You want someone to give you change for a one hundred taka note.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 3, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 3. A: __________ you give me your calculator, please? B: Yes, __________. __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q3-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 3, 'Make requests using the clues. 3. You want someone to wait a minute.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 4, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 4. A: __________ you get me a notebook and a ballpen from the stationer''s? B: Yes. Of course, I __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q4-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 4, 'Make requests using the clues. 4. You want someone to carry your bag.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 5, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 5. A: Can you put my box in the car, please? B: Yes, __________. I will.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p3-q5-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 3, 5, 'Make requests using the clues. 5. You want someone to call you a rickshaw.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 1, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 1. Would you read the shopping list? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 2, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 2. Will you go to the market, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 3, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 3. Will you buy me one litre of cooking oil, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 4, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 4. Would you buy me some rice? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 5, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 5. Would you need some money? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 6, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 6. Would you like some tea? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q7', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 7, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 7. Will you switch on the TV, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p5-q8', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 5, 8, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 8. Would you tell her to watch TV at 10 pm? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 1, 'Look at the picture and answer these questions. 1. What is it? [Picture: inside a bookshop - a shopkeeper behind a counter holds a book while talking to a girl customer with a shoulder bag; shelves full of books behind them and two books on the counter.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q1-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 1, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 1. 1. What do you mean by ''in stock'' and ''out of stock''?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 2, 'Look at the picture and answer these questions. 2. Where can you find it? [Picture: inside a bookshop - a shopkeeper behind a counter holds a book while talking to a girl customer with a shoulder bag; shelves full of books behind them and two books on the counter.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 2, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 1. 2. Who are talking in this conversation?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 3, 'Look at the picture and answer these questions. 3. Is there a bookshop near your house or school or in your upazilla/town? Tell us about it. [Picture: inside a bookshop - a shopkeeper behind a counter holds a book while talking to a girl customer with a shoulder bag; shelves full of books behind them and two books on the counter.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch1-p7-q3-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch1', 7, 3, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 1. 3. Where is the conversation taking place?'),
