  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p17-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 17, 1, 'Look at the picture and discuss the following questions. 1. Whom can you see in the picture? [Picture: a boy receiving a prize (a wrapped box) from a man at a school prize-giving ceremony, with other students watching.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p17-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 17, 2, 'Look at the picture and discuss the following questions. 2. What are they doing? [Picture: a boy receiving a prize (a wrapped box) from a man at a school prize-giving ceremony, with other students watching.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p19-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 19, 1, 'Say whether the following statements are true or false. If false, give the correct information. 1. Farabi and Flora are talking at school.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 1, 'Do you remember your first day at school? Write a short composition about it answering the questions below. 1. How old were you at that time?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 2, 'Say whether the following statements are true or false. If false, give the correct information. 2. Flora is talking about her school.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 2, 'Do you remember your first day at school? Write a short composition about it answering the questions below. 2. What is the name of the school you went to?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 3, 'Say whether the following statements are true or false. If false, give the correct information. 3. Flora first went to school at the age of 6.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q3-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 3, 'Do you remember your first day at school? Write a short composition about it answering the questions below. 3. What did you put on?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 4, 'Say whether the following statements are true or false. If false, give the correct information. 4. Her mother dressed her in her best clothes.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q4-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 4, 'Do you remember your first day at school? Write a short composition about it answering the questions below. 4. How did you feel before you started for the school?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 5, 'Say whether the following statements are true or false. If false, give the correct information. 5. Flora walked to school.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p20-q5-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 20, 5, 'Do you remember your first day at school? Write a short composition about it answering the questions below. 5. Who did you go with?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p21-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 21, 1, 'Choose the correct answer. 1. How long did it take Flora to reach the school? a. an hour b. half an hour c. less than half an hour d. one and a half hours'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p21-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 21, 2, 'Choose the correct answer. 2. Flora was a little bit afraid when she reached the school campus because a. the campus was full of students. b. it was the first time she went there. c. all the people there were unknown. d. the school was a long way from home.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p22-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 22, 3, 'Choose the correct answer. 3. The Head Teacher was pleased with Flora because she (Flora) a. looked very innocent. b. had a sweet voice. c. could answer the Head Teacher''s questions. d. was very smart.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p22-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 22, 4, 'Choose the correct answer. 4. Who took Flora to the class after admission? a. a teacher b. a peon c. her mother d. the Head Teacher'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p22-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 22, 5, 'Choose the correct answer. 5. Flora felt nervous in the class because a. it was a new place. b. the class teacher was very strict. c. she did not know any student in the class. d. the class did not welcome her.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p23-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 23, 1, 'Discuss and answer these questions. 1. What will you do if your parents do not want you to go on a picnic with your friends?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p23-q1-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 23, 1, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 1. Which is the correct statement? Farabi was a. standing up. b. looking down. c. looking happy.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p23-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 23, 2, 'Discuss and answer these questions. 2. What will you do if you miss the picnic bus?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p23-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 23, 2, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 2. Why was Farabi with his head down? Because a. he was unhappy. b. it was his habit. c. he had a headache.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p24-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 24, 3, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 3. His hair was ruffled. Here ''ruffled'' means a. brushed and tidy. b. clear and smooth. c. not brushed or combed.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p24-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 24, 4, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 4. Farabi didn''t want to talk to Flora because a. something sad happened to him. b. he stopped talking to his friend. c. he was unwell and sick.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p24-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 24, 5, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 5. "Please tell me what''s wrong," Flora insisted. Here ''insisted'' means a. scolded. b. demanded. c. shouted.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p24-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 24, 6, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 6. Your pain in the mind will be __________ if you talk about it with your friend. a. heavy b. less heavy c. more heavy'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p24-q7', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 24, 7, 'Read about what happened to Farabi yesterday and answer the following questions. Tick the best answer. 7. Which is the correct statement? a. Farabi was going to play in the Interclass Football Tournament. b. Farabi and Harun were not going to play in the Interclass Football Tournament. c. Farabi and Harun used to play in the Interclass Football Tournament.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p25-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 25, 1, 'Match the words / phrases with their meanings. 1. hurt Meanings: (a) an area in a desert where there are water, plants, etc. (b) remove something completely (c) cut words or designs on stone or wood (d) got physical pain when someone hits you or you fall (e) deep wet sand that works like a trap. If you walk on it, you will sink into it.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p25-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 25, 2, 'Match the words / phrases with their meanings. 2. oasis Meanings: (a) an area in a desert where there are water, plants, etc. (b) remove something completely (c) cut words or designs on stone or wood (d) got physical pain when someone hits you or you fall (e) deep wet sand that works like a trap. If you walk on it, you will sink into it.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p25-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 25, 3, 'Match the words / phrases with their meanings. 3. quicksand Meanings: (a) an area in a desert where there are water, plants, etc. (b) remove something completely (c) cut words or designs on stone or wood (d) got physical pain when someone hits you or you fall (e) deep wet sand that works like a trap. If you walk on it, you will sink into it.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p25-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 25, 4, 'Match the words / phrases with their meanings. 4. erase Meanings: (a) an area in a desert where there are water, plants, etc. (b) remove something completely (c) cut words or designs on stone or wood (d) got physical pain when someone hits you or you fall (e) deep wet sand that works like a trap. If you walk on it, you will sink into it.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch3-p25-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch3', 25, 5, 'Match the words / phrases with their meanings. 5. engrave Meanings: (a) an area in a desert where there are water, plants, etc. (b) remove something completely (c) cut words or designs on stone or wood (d) got physical pain when someone hits you or you fall (e) deep wet sand that works like a trap. If you walk on it, you will sink into it.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p27-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 27, 1, 'Listen to the teacher / audio about what Shahana says about herself and answer the following questions. Listening text: 4. Tick the best answer. 1. Ms Shahana Huda passed her SSC exam in a. 2000 b. 2001 c. 2002'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p27-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 27, 2, 'Listen to the teacher / audio about what Shahana says about herself and answer the following questions. Listening text: 4. Tick the best answer. 2. She passed her HSC exam in a. 2001 b. 2002 c. 2003'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p27-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 27, 3, 'Listen to the teacher / audio about what Shahana says about herself and answer the following questions. Listening text: 4. Tick the best answer. 3. She married a. before her HSC exam. b. after her BA exam. c. while she was studying at college.'),
