  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p28-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 28, 5, 'Listen to the teacher / audio about what Shahana says about herself and answer the following questions. Listening text: 4. Tick the best answer. 5. She took a break of one year a. to get training to become a teacher. b. to take care of her daughter. c. to take a BA degree.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p28-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 28, 6, 'Listen to the teacher / audio about what Shahana says about herself and answer the following questions. Listening text: 4. Tick the best answer. 6. Why did Shahana''s husband want her to work in an office? Because he thought a. teaching was not a job. b. teaching was less paid. c. people did not like teaching.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 1, 'Answer the following questions based on your reading of the passage: 1. What does generational naming refer to? Why do people name different generations?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q1-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 1, 'Vocabulary Test. Match the words with their correct definitions: 1. Rhetoric Correct Definitions: (a) A paradoxical situation where two opposite conditions exist simultaneously. (b) The use of language to persuade or influence, often in a manipulative way. (c) A system of government where power is held by one person with absolute authority. (d) Awareness or understanding of something, especially the state of one''s mind. (e) The feeling of being upset or annoyed, especially because of an inability to change or achieve something.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 2, 'Answer the following questions based on your reading of the passage: 2. Describe one unique characteristic or challenge of the current generation.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 2, 'Vocabulary Test. Match the words with their correct definitions: 2. Autocracy Correct Definitions: (a) A paradoxical situation where two opposite conditions exist simultaneously. (b) The use of language to persuade or influence, often in a manipulative way. (c) A system of government where power is held by one person with absolute authority. (d) Awareness or understanding of something, especially the state of one''s mind. (e) The feeling of being upset or annoyed, especially because of an inability to change or achieve something.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 3, 'Answer the following questions based on your reading of the passage: 3. What do you know about the legacy of generational struggles in Bangladesh? Write in brief.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q3-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 3, 'Vocabulary Test. Match the words with their correct definitions: 3. Consciousness Correct Definitions: (a) A paradoxical situation where two opposite conditions exist simultaneously. (b) The use of language to persuade or influence, often in a manipulative way. (c) A system of government where power is held by one person with absolute authority. (d) Awareness or understanding of something, especially the state of one''s mind. (e) The feeling of being upset or annoyed, especially because of an inability to change or achieve something.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p33-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 33, 4, 'Answer the following questions based on your reading of the passage: 4. Why is good governance important for meeting the needs of new generations?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 1, 'Fill in the Gaps. Fill in the blanks using the words from the list below: (Lost Generation, Gen Z, political, digital, connected) 1. The term "__________" refers to the generation affected by the aftermath of World War I and the Great Depression.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 2, 'Fill in the Gaps. Fill in the blanks using the words from the list below: (Lost Generation, Gen Z, political, digital, connected) 2. __________ is the first generation to grow up entirely in the digital age.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 3, 'Fill in the Gaps. Fill in the blanks using the words from the list below: (Lost Generation, Gen Z, political, digital, connected) 3. The 2018 road safety protests marked a shift in __________ awareness for Generation Z.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 4, 'Vocabulary Test. Match the words with their correct definitions: 4. Paradox Correct Definitions: (a) A paradoxical situation where two opposite conditions exist simultaneously. (b) The use of language to persuade or influence, often in a manipulative way. (c) A system of government where power is held by one person with absolute authority. (d) Awareness or understanding of something, especially the state of one''s mind. (e) The feeling of being upset or annoyed, especially because of an inability to change or achieve something.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q4-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 4, 'Fill in the Gaps. Fill in the blanks using the words from the list below: (Lost Generation, Gen Z, political, digital, connected) 4. The July Uprising of 2024 called for new methods to address the challenges of today''s __________ world.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 5, 'Vocabulary Test. Match the words with their correct definitions: 5. Frustration Correct Definitions: (a) A paradoxical situation where two opposite conditions exist simultaneously. (b) The use of language to persuade or influence, often in a manipulative way. (c) A system of government where power is held by one person with absolute authority. (d) Awareness or understanding of something, especially the state of one''s mind. (e) The feeling of being upset or annoyed, especially because of an inability to change or achieve something.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p34-q5-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 34, 5, 'Fill in the Gaps. Fill in the blanks using the words from the list below: (Lost Generation, Gen Z, political, digital, connected) 5. Gen Z experiences a paradox of being both hyperconnected yet often __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p35-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 35, 1, 'Read the poem silently and answer these questions: 1. Who asked the question, "Whose Child is This?" in the poem?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p35-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 35, 2, 'Read the poem silently and answer these questions: 2. How many times did he / she ask the question, "Whose child is this?"'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p35-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 35, 3, 'Read the poem silently and answer these questions: 3. Who answered the question in stanzas 1, 2, and 3?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p36-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 36, 1, 'Look at the shop and answer these questions. 1. What kinds of things do you find in the shop? [Picture: inside a shop with shelves of stationery, food items and clothes - a woman shopkeeper serves a girl student at the counter while a boy student stands nearby holding a book.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p36-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 36, 2, 'Look at the shop and answer these questions. 2. What are the students doing? [Picture: inside a shop with shelves of stationery, food items and clothes - a woman shopkeeper serves a girl student at the counter while a boy student stands nearby holding a book.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p36-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 36, 3, 'Look at the shop and answer these questions. 3. Who is the shopkeeper? [Picture: inside a shop with shelves of stationery, food items and clothes - a woman shopkeeper serves a girl student at the counter while a boy student stands nearby holding a book.]'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p37-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 37, 1, 'Read the text and answer the following questions. Questions 1. Do you go shopping? Where is the shop?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p37-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 37, 2, 'Read the text and answer the following questions. Questions 2. What do you usually buy?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p37-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 37, 3, 'Read the text and answer the following questions. Questions 3. Do you bargain? Why do you do that?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p37-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 37, 4, 'Read the text and answer the following questions. Questions 4. Do you know about a ''Fixed-price'' shop? Where is it? What does it sell?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p38-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 38, 1, 'Tick the best answers to the following multiple choice questions. 1. "The students are confused." The underlined words mean they a. can think clearly. b. cannot understand. c. are unable to speak.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p38-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 38, 2, 'Tick the best answers to the following multiple choice questions. 2. When you buy a thing from a Morality Shop, you a. pay the money to the office. b. pay the money later. c. keep the money in the shop.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p38-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 38, 3, 'Tick the best answers to the following multiple choice questions. 3. A person with a clear conscience a. usually does the wrong thing. b. always gets confused. c. always does the right thing.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 1, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 1. Joynul was angry with everybody because a. he was looking for work in his village and in the next village. b. he was hungry and Nazma could not cook food at the proper time. c. he did not find any work in his village and in the next village.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 2, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 2. Joynul shouted loudly at Nazma because a. she could not give him food in time. b. she had a bad headache. c. she forgot to cook food in time.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 3, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 3. It will take ages. The underlined words mean a. Nazma is suffering from old age. b. a very long time will be needed. c. Joynul is willing to wait long.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 4, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 4. Who should run the family? a. Joynul b. Nazma c. Joynul and Nazma'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 5, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 5. What can make a family happy? a. money and housework b. work that Nazma does at home c. work that Joynul does to earn money'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p41-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 41, 6, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 6. All members in a family should a. do their individual work separately. b. live together and support each other. c. earn and spend money equally.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p42-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 42, 1, 'Project work: Think of a family you know in your neighbourhood. Answer the following questions and write a short composition about the family. 1. How many members are there in the family?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p42-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 42, 2, 'Project work: Think of a family you know in your neighbourhood. Answer the following questions and write a short composition about the family. 2. Get each member''s name, age and work.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p42-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 42, 3, 'Project work: Think of a family you know in your neighbourhood. Answer the following questions and write a short composition about the family. 3. Do the family members share each other''s work? Describe who shares what, where and who with.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p42-q7', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 42, 7, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 7. What do you think Joynul should do from now? He should a. work harder to earn more money. b. not waste any time doing housework. c. help Nazma with her work when he can.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p42-q8', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 42, 8, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 8. Why does Joynul finally look at Nazma with deep admiration and gratitude? Because a. he is not sorry for what he has done to Nazma. b. he has understood the value of sharing work in the family. c. Nazma is willing to do all the housework in the family.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p44-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 44, 1, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 1. Dr Mahmud Hasan was born in a. a village. b. Mymensingh town. c. Dhaka.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p44-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 44, 2, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 2. What did Mr Hasan do during the Liberation War? a. He took part in the battle. b. He worked for the government. c. He set up a hospital.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p44-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 44, 3, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 3. The sufferings of the poor people a. made him work in a Red Crescent Hospital. b. changed his mind for working for the poor. c. made him join the Liberation War.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch4-p44-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch4', 44, 4, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 4. Dr Hasan went to his village a. before he gave up his job. b. after he gave up his job. c. before the war finished.'),
