  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 1, 'Now write sentences using the table about people in Paul''s family and your family. 1. Paul likes watching animals. I like watching animals too.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q1-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 1, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 1. Mr. Jabbar works with computers. Q: (like) Does Mr. Jabbar like working with computers? A: (Yes, love) Yes, he loves working with computers.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 2, 'Now write sentences using the table about people in Paul''s family and your family. 2. His sister hates spiders but my sister does not hate them.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q2-2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 2, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 2. Rabiul goes shopping at the weekend. Q: (like) Does Robiul like going shopping at the weekend? A: (No, hates) No, he hates going shopping at the weekend.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 3, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 3. The students watch cricket. Q: (like) __________? A: (Yes, like) __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p95-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 95, 4, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 4. Rezina goes to the doctor. Q: (Like) __________? A: (No, not like) __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p96-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 96, 5, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 5. Your sister watches films. Q: (Like) __________? A: (Yes, love) __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p96-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 96, 6, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 6. We waste our time. Q: (like) __________? A: (No, hate) __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch8-p96-q7', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch8', 96, 7, 'Use the clues to write questions and answers about likes/dislikes. 7. They donate money to the poor. Q: (like) __________? A: (Yes, love) __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p100-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 100, 1, 'Choose the right answer. 1. Which one of these is an example of climate change? a. a long day b. a windy day c. a hot summer day d. a sunny day'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p100-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 100, 2, 'Choose the right answer. 2. What does ''climbing'' mean in the statement "temperatures are climbing"? a. shifting b. going up c. being in crisis d. surviving'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p100-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 100, 3, 'Choose the right answer. 3. If things go on like this... In this sentence ''go on'' means a. to go places b. to change times c. to walk fast d. to continue'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p100-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 100, 4, 'Choose the right answer. 4. How did Samina and Arif react to what Anwar said about climate change? a. They showed no interest. b. They became afraid of going out alone. c. They wanted to know more about climate change. d. They agreed to attend a lecture on climate change.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p103-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 103, 1, 'Tick the best answer. 1. One outcome of climate change in Bangladesh is a. summers are becoming shorter. b. summers are becoming milder. c. the monsoon is becoming irregular. d. the cities are getting larger.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p103-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 103, 2, 'Tick the best answer. 2. The cyclone that hit Bangladesh in 2009 is called a. Hurricane. b. Sidr. c. Aila. d. Nargis.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p103-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 103, 3, 'Tick the best answer. 3. It is likely that 10.9 percent of Bangladesh will go under water if the sea level rises to a. 40 centimetres. b. 45 centimetres. c. 35 centimetres. d. 50 centimetres.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p103-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 103, 4, 'Tick the best answer. 4. The phrase ''coastal region'' means an area a. with deep forests. b. of dry lands. c. with a huge population. d. close to the sea.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p103-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 103, 5, 'Tick the best answer. 5. The phrase ''prolonged cold spells'' means a. long duration of cold waves. b. long gap between two winters. c. longer nights during winter. d. delay in doing something due to cold.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p104-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 104, 1, 'In small groups discuss these questions. 1. Which animals in Bangladesh are in danger of extinction? What do you think we should do to protect these animals?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p104-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 104, 2, 'In small groups discuss these questions. 2. What problems do you think deforestation can cause in Bangladesh?'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 1, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 1. If I have shorter showers I will B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q10', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 10, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 10. Batteries are highly toxic, if I need to use batteries I can B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 2, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 2. I can help keep cars off the road B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 3, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 3. When I leave a room I can save energy by B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 4, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 4. Putting on a jumper instead of the heater B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q5', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 5, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 5. Plastic bags harm wildlife, instead I can B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q6', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 6, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 6. I can dry my hair in the sun B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q7', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 7, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 7. I can reduce, reuse, and recycle B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q8', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 8, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 8. In my garden, I should plant B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p106-q9', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 106, 9, 'Match the sentence parts in A with those in B. 9. When I am shopping, I should B: (a) will keep me warm in winter. (b) the waste I make. (c) choose products with less packaging. (d) plants that are good for environment. (e) use rechargeable ones. (f) use bags made of jute or paper. (g) turning the light off. (h) help save water at home. (i) by walking to school and shops. (j) without using a hair dryer.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p107-q1', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 107, 1, 'Now write a few slogans for a poster using the following clues: 1. Don''t throw your wastes __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p107-q2', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 107, 2, 'Now write a few slogans for a poster using the following clues: 2. Do not use __________ bags while shopping.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p107-q3', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 107, 3, 'Now write a few slogans for a poster using the following clues: 3. You can not use too much water for __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-bn-ch9-p107-q4', 'class7-eft-bn', 'class7-eft-bn-ch9', 107, 4, 'Now write a few slogans for a poster using the following clues: 4. People must use __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p2-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 2, 1, 'Now answer these questions. 1. Do you speak English with your teacher? If you do, when and how often?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p2-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 2, 2, 'Now answer these questions. 2. Do you speak English with your friends and classmates? If so, how often?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p2-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 2, 3, 'Now answer these questions. 3. If you speak English outside the class, where do you speak it?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p2-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 2, 4, 'Now answer these questions. 4. Do you watch any English programmes on TV? What programmes do you watch?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 1, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 1. A: __________ you lend me your English book for a day? B: Sorry, I __________. I need to read it tonight.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q1-2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 1, 'Make requests using the clues. 1. You want someone to help you with the washing.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 2, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 2. A: Could you give me 50 taka? B: Sorry, I __________. I have only 20 taka with me.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q2-2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 2, 'Make requests using the clues. 2. You want someone to give you change for a one hundred taka note.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 3, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 3. A: __________ you give me your calculator, please? B: Yes, __________. __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q3-2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 3, 'Make requests using the clues. 3. You want someone to wait a minute.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 4, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 4. A: __________ you get me a notebook and a ballpen from the stationer''s? B: Yes. Of course, I __________.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q4-2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 4, 'Make requests using the clues. 4. You want someone to carry your bag.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q5', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 5, 'Complete these dialogues using suitable words. 5. A: Can you put my box in the car, please? B: Yes, __________. I will.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p3-q5-2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 3, 5, 'Make requests using the clues. 5. You want someone to call you a rickshaw.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 1, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 1. Would you read the shopping list? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 2, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 2. Will you go to the market, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 3, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 3. Will you buy me one litre of cooking oil, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 4, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 4. Would you buy me some rice? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q5', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 5, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 5. Would you need some money? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q6', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 6, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 6. Would you like some tea? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q7', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 7, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 7. Will you switch on the TV, please? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch1-p5-q8', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch1', 5, 8, 'Match the sentences in column A with suitable answers in column B. Some answers in B may match more than one question. 8. Would you tell her to watch TV at 10 pm? Column B: (a) Certainly, I''ll do it. (b) Why? Rina is watching. (c) No, thanks. I have enough with me. (d) Yes, I''ll. (e) Sorry, I can''t. I''ve left my glasses in the study. (f) Yes, I''d love to. (g) What for? (h) OK. How much?'),
