  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p42-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 42, 3, 'Project work: Think of a family you know in your neighbourhood. Answer the following questions and write a short composition about the family. 3. Do the family members share each other''s work? Describe who shares what, where and who with.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p42-q7', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 42, 7, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 7. What do you think Joynul should do from now? He should a. work harder to earn more money. b. not waste any time doing housework. c. help Nazma with her work when he can.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p42-q8', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 42, 8, 'Read the text again and tick the best answer. 8. Why does Joynul finally look at Nazma with deep admiration and gratitude? Because a. he is not sorry for what he has done to Nazma. b. he has understood the value of sharing work in the family. c. Nazma is willing to do all the housework in the family.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 1, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 1. Dr Mahmud Hasan was born in a. a village. b. Mymensingh town. c. Dhaka.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 2, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 2. What did Mr Hasan do during the Liberation War? a. He took part in the battle. b. He worked for the government. c. He set up a hospital.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 3, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 3. The sufferings of the poor people a. made him work in a Red Crescent Hospital. b. changed his mind for working for the poor. c. made him join the Liberation War.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 4, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 4. Dr Hasan went to his village a. before he gave up his job. b. after he gave up his job. c. before the war finished.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q5', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 5, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 5. Dr Hasan set up a healthcare centre a. with the money of the villagers. b. with government grants. c. with his own money.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p44-q6', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 44, 6, 'Listen to the teacher / audio and answer the following questions. Listening text: 5. 6. The health assistants give treatment to the sick people a. in and outside the centre. b. only in the doctor''s village. c. only in the neighbouring villages.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p46-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 46, 1, 'Ask and answer the questions. 1. Is the healthcare support free to all?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p46-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 46, 2, 'Ask and answer the questions. 2. Why is the doctor waiting for a torch bearer?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p46-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 46, 3, 'Ask and answer the questions. 3. Who will be in charge of the centre?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p46-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 46, 4, 'Ask and answer the questions. 4. Do you think the money he gets from the patients is enough to run the centre? Why do you think so?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p47-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'Read aloud the story about a hospital window and think about the questions. Q 1. Can you guess why they talk about all these things?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p47-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'Read aloud the story about a hospital window and think about the questions. Q 2. Can you guess what the man near the window talked about to his friend?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p47-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'Read aloud the story about a hospital window and think about the questions. Q 3. What would the listener feel and do if one day his friend could not sit up and talk?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch4-p47-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'Read aloud the story about a hospital window and think about the questions. Q 4. Can you guess what he saw?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch5-p49-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch5', 49, 1, 'Look at the picture. Ask and answer these questions. 1. Who is the woman? [Picture: a portrait of a woman wearing a headscarf and round glasses - Begum Rokeya.]'),
