  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p56-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 56, 2, 'Discuss in groups or pairs and answer these questions. 2. Why do you think he spends too much / too little / the right amount of time on his studies?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p56-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 56, 3, 'Discuss in groups or pairs and answer these questions. 3. What does Zishan study on Fridays?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p57-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 57, 1, 'Read the poem, discuss in groups / pairs and write answers to these questions: 1. Why does the poet think that we have no time to stand and stare?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p57-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 57, 2, 'Read the poem, discuss in groups / pairs and write answers to these questions: 2. Do you think people often do not have time to enjoy the beauty of nature? Give reasons.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p58-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 58, 1, 'Now read the paragraphs and match them with the pictures. 1. Young children play this game on the ground. The ground is marked by a set of joined squares. Each child throws a stone into a square, then hops (jumps on one leg) and jumps along the empty squares to pick up the stone again. They play this game in turn. Pictures: A. a girl sitting at a desk using a desktop computer; B. boys playing football on a field with a goal; C. a boy sitting on a sofa watching TV; D. two girls playing hopscotch on squares marked on the ground.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p58-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 58, 2, 'Now read the paragraphs and match them with the pictures. 2. Some children are often glued to computers. They download games to play on them. Some also share personal updates on Facebook by uploading posts and pictures. Pictures: A. a girl sitting at a desk using a desktop computer; B. boys playing football on a field with a goal; C. a boy sitting on a sofa watching TV; D. two girls playing hopscotch on squares marked on the ground.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p58-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 58, 3, 'Now read the paragraphs and match them with the pictures. 3. Children often watch football matches of both national and international teams on TV. Pictures: A. a girl sitting at a desk using a desktop computer; B. boys playing football on a field with a goal; C. a boy sitting on a sofa watching TV; D. two girls playing hopscotch on squares marked on the ground.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p58-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 58, 4, 'Now read the paragraphs and match them with the pictures. 4. Children often play football in the school playground. Pictures: A. a girl sitting at a desk using a desktop computer; B. boys playing football on a field with a goal; C. a boy sitting on a sofa watching TV; D. two girls playing hopscotch on squares marked on the ground.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p59-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 59, 1, 'Write answers to these questions. 1. What free-time / leisure activities do you do?'),
