  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p63-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 63, 1, 'Answer these questions. 1. Can you see the full moon from your house or yard?'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p63-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 63, 2, 'Answer these questions. 2. Discuss in pairs or groups and answer this question: What activities of the moon are noticed in the following stanza? Slowly silently, now the moon Walks the night in her silver shoon; This way, and that, she peers and sees Silver fruit upon silver trees. [Walter de la Mare]'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p64-q1', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 64, 1, 'Tick the best answer. 1. What made Jahid and Shima excited? a. the shining of the full moon b. meeting with their cousins c. sitting on the mats d. the delicious supper'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p64-q2', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 64, 2, 'Tick the best answer. 2. Everybody was feeling relaxed. This means everybody was a. wearing nice clothes b. talking and enjoying themselves c. having no work to do d. sitting under the full moon'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p64-q3', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 64, 3, 'Tick the best answer. 3. Zishan could not reply to Jahid''s question, "What sports do you take part in?" because a. he does not like sports. b. his school does not organize any sports. c. sports are not part of examinations. d. his parents don''t like sports.'),
  ('class7-eft-en-ch6-p64-q4', 'class7-eft-en', 'class7-eft-en-ch6', 64, 4, 'Tick the best answer. 4. Julie''s aunt''s funny jokes made everybody laugh their head off. Here "laugh their head off" means laughing a. slowly. b. moving their heads. c. loudly. d. with a headache.'),
