  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q13', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 8, 'Make the following sentences active: Was my book seen by anybody?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q14', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 9, 'Make the following sentences active: She was being laughed at.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q15', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 10, 'Make the following sentences active: The exam will be passed by Rimi.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q16', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 1, 'Choose the right option : The gallery was ______ in 1953. (a) suggested (b) told (c) built (d) permitted'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, NULL, 'Look at the picture and fill in the gaps in the following sentences in passive form with the given verbs in the bracket: [Image: A kitchen with a refrigerator, a stove with a kettle, a sink, shelves of plates, a dining table with chairs, and a stool.] A table is ______ in the middle (place).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, NULL, 'Look at the picture and fill in the gaps in the following sentences in passive form with the given verbs in the bracket: [Image: A kitchen with a refrigerator, a stove with a kettle, a sink, shelves of plates, a dining table with chairs, and a stool.] The chairs ______ properly (arrange).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, NULL, 'Look at the picture and fill in the gaps in the following sentences in passive form with the given verbs in the bracket: [Image: A kitchen with a refrigerator, a stove with a kettle, a sink, shelves of plates, a dining table with chairs, and a stool.] A lampshade ______ from the roof (hang).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, NULL, 'Look at the picture and fill in the gaps in the following sentences in passive form with the given verbs in the bracket: [Image: A kitchen with a refrigerator, a stove with a kettle, a sink, shelves of plates, a dining table with chairs, and a stool.] A large refrigerator ______ with the wall (attach).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 1, 'Make the following sentences active: The room is being painted.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 2, 'Make the following sentences active: Fruit juice will be served at the party.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 3, 'Make the following sentences active: I have been warned by my dad.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p162-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 162, 4, 'Make the following sentences active: This shirt must not be ironed.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p163-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 163, 2, 'Choose the right option : The company was ______ in 1980. (a) increased (b) founded (c) left (d) written'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p163-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 163, 3, 'Choose the right option : I was ______ to make a presentation at the conference. (a) suggested (b) increased (c) permitted (d) invited'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p163-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 163, 4, 'Choose the right option : The job was ______ to Jhumpa but she turned it down. (a) offered (b) permitted (c) left (d) written'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17-p163-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch17', 163, 5, 'Choose the right option : I was ______ that I wouldn''t need to bring my own slide projector. (a) told (b) increased (c) permitted (d) written'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18-p176-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18', 176, 1, 'Now write paragraphs on the given topics by answering the given questions : Topic: A Child and a Flower Questions : (a) Which two things are very innocent in this world? (b) Why do a child and a flower need care? (c) How does a flower motivate a cruel person? (d) How do a flower and a child make the atmosphere beautiful? (e) How is a child similar to a flower?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18-p176-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18', 176, 2, 'Now write paragraphs on the given topics by answering the given questions : Topic: Coffee and Tea Questions : (a) In which country did tea grow first? (b) Where did coffee grow first? (c) How do coffee and tea help in our daily life? (d) How do we drink coffee and tea? (e) How do we harvest tea and coffee?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18-p177-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18', 177, 3, 'Now write paragraphs on the given topics by answering the given questions : Topic: Your First Day at School Questions : (a) What is the most important day in your life? (b) When did you go there for the first time? (c) With whom did you go to school on the first day? (d) How did you go to school on the first day? (e) How did you feel on that day?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18-p177-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18', 177, 4, 'Now write paragraphs on the given topics by answering the given questions : Topic: Your Aunt Questions : (a) What is the name of your aunt? (b) How old is she? (c) Where does she live? (d) What does she do? (e) Why do you like your aunt?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18-p177-e3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch18', 177, 5, 'Now write paragraphs on the given topics by answering the given questions : Topic: Your Village Questions : (a) What is the name of your village? (b) Where is it situated? (c) How many people are there? (d) What is the occupation of the villagers? (e) How do you like your village?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p181-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 181, 1, 'Write a letter to your class teacher asking for one week’s leave:'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p182-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 182, 2, 'Write a letter of apology to your math teacher for disturbing others in the examination hall.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p183-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 183, 3, 'Write an e-mail to your headmaster praying for a full free-studentship:'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p184-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 184, 4, 'Write a complaint letter regarding irregular water supply in your locality.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p185-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 185, 5, 'Suppose, the British council has an advertisement in the national dailies to start an advanced English course for young learners. Write an email in 100 words to the course co-ordinator, requesting him to send you an application form:'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p186-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 186, 6, 'Write an application to the Manager of a bank to open a bank account.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p187-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 187, 7, 'Write an application to the Head teacher of your school, requesting him to organise an inter-class debate competition in the school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p188-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 188, 8, 'Write an application to the Head teacher, requesting him to contact the Bishwa Shahitto Kendro to provide the school library with more books.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p189-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 189, 9, 'Write an e-mail to the editor of a local newspaper informing him about the traffic jam you face daily:'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p190-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 190, 1, 'Now write the following : An application to the District Commissioner, complaining about the uncovered dustbins in your city.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p190-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 190, 2, 'Now write the following : An email to the editor of a newspaper, demanding better medical facilities in your village.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p190-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 190, 3, 'Now write the following : A letter to the chief engineer of your local power station complaining about irregular electric supply in your area.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19-p190-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch19', 190, 4, 'Now write the following : An application to your Headmaster requesting a transfer certificate.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch2-p12-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch2', 12, 1, 'Look at the underlined words in the following sentences. Guess what these words are called. Client : |want to open a savings account with your bank. Desk officer :How can! help you, sir?'),
