  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p20-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 20, 4, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : The waiter says, “ ______ I give you cold drinks, sir?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p20-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 20, 5, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : I am going home now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p20-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 20, NULL, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : I am going home now. Ok, I ______ you Sunday morning.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, NULL, 'Suppose you and your partner are playing the role of a palmist and a client. The dialogue will go like this. Use the verbs employ, earn, export, offer and import and complete the dialogue: Palmist : You will have a big business in future. Client : What kind of business? P : It will be a garment business'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, NULL, 'Now match these sentences with the predictions below: Sentences: 1. It''s Friday morning 2. I am back from my school 3. If you are not careful 4. On Fridays 5. The class teacher is coming to the class. Predictions: a. she will call our names b. shops will remain open. c. I will take some rest now. d. we will say our Jumma prayer. e. you will slip from the steep staircase.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, 1, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: Don’t worry; the student volunteers will manage discipline about the program.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, 2, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I am sure you ______ your visit to Rangamaati.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, 3, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I ______ you tonight and ______ you about the situation.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, 4, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I am very tired. I ______ to bed early tonight.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p21-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 21, 5, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: People are very angry about the problem. They ______ a compromising solution of the problem.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 1, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Nafisa’s school is closed today. She is reading a story book.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 2, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Asif : What are you doing now? Come and join us in a game if you are free. Maruf : Sorry, I can’t. I am taking my sister to a doctor. She is suffering from fever.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 3, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Please don’t interrupt me while I am talking over the phone.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 4, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Desk officer: Are you being served? Client: Yes, that young lady is helping me.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 5, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Teacher:Are you listening to me? Students: Yes ma’m, we are.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 1, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Take this umbrella. It ______ outside now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 2, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : “ ______ you still ______ in a bank?” “No, recently I have left it.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 3, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Please don’t disturb me. I ______ my homework.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p22-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 22, 4, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Please wait for a minute. I ______ soon.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 5, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : There are a few doctors in this clinic. Many patients (not) ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 1, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: I am going to visit my grandma this weekend. What about you?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 2, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Do you think our teacher is going to give us a good grade for this assignment?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 3, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Who of you are going to work as volunteers? Please raise your hands.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 4, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: When is your uncle coming back from his overseas study?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p23-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 23, 5, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: It is going to be a big problem if you do not pay attention to it now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p24-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 24, 1, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you decided to spend extra money? B: Well, I think I ______ to a restaurant for a good dinner but haven’t decided yet.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p24-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 24, 2, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you decided how you will spend the holiday? B: Not yet but I think I ______ to my village for a few days.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p24-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 24, 3, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: My cousins are coming from Italy this Friday. B: ______ you ______ to receive them at the airport?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p24-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 24, 5, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Our school has set up a new routine for our classes effective from this Saturday. B: Yes, we ______ to attend the first class much earlier.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p24-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 24, 6, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you collected your tickets for the concert? B: Not yet. But I think we ______ there on Friday if we can.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, NULL, 'Compare these two remarks: Why, do you think, is the form of the verb ''rain'' different in (a) and (b)? (a) It will rain tomorrow as soon as we get to the park. (b) According to the weather forecast it''s going to rain tomorrow. May be we shouldn''t go to the park.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, 1, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: The opposition has called a strike on Sunday. I ______ (not go) to attend my classes.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, 2, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: I ______ (carry) an umbrella if it rains.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, 3, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: The way all Kiwi wickets are falling, I think Tigers ______ (win) the match easily.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, 4, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: Son: Father, any plan for the weekend? Father: Our whole family has been invited to my colleague’s daughter’s wedding. So, we ______ (attend) the party.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p25-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 25, 5, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: It is not cold here. I ______ (wear) a jumper.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 1, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Please open your book. Have you (open) it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 2, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Wow! It’s a wonderful piece of drawing. Who ______ (draw) it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 3, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Excuse me, teacher. Could you please repeat what you ______ (say) just now?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 4, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: I am very worried about my homework. I ______ (not finish) it yet.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 5, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: There is a big museum in the city. ______ you ______ there?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p26-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 26, 6, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Please tell me what exactly you ______ done and what is yet to be done.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 1, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Teacher: We have only one day left for the science fair. Now let me know who ______ what. Zarif: I ______ the wall, sir.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 2, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Mother: There are only a few chocolates on the table. Who ______ the others? Mayisha: Mom, I ______ just one.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 3, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Teacher: Let’s brainstorm on the topic for a minute. Now Anika, tell me what ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 4, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Hanif: Wait, this math problem is not that easy. But I ______ something about it. Monoj: Ok, tell us what ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 5, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : ‘Three Idiots’ is an excellent movie. ______ you ______ it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p27-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 27, 1, 'Write some sentences about your activities you have done since morning. Show your sentences to your partner to check. You may start like this. First, I have said my morning prayer.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 1, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The sun (shine) when we went out.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 10, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: Who (talk) there when I knocked at the door? “I (call) my sister.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 2, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: When you came, I (write).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 3, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: My brother asked me, “Why didn’t you receive my call?” “I (sleep) then”.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 4, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: When the teacher came to the class, all students (stand) up.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 5, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The bus started while some passengers (get) on.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 6, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The boy took another piece of cake when the mother (not look).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 7, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The teacher asked his students,‘Why you (make) a noise in the class?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 8, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: We (have) dinner when electricity went off.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p28-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 28, 9, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The boy jumped off the train while it (move).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p29-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 29, 1, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: It ______ heavily outside when I ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p29-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 29, 2, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Where ______ when I ______ you?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p29-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 29, 3, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: When my elder ______ my father ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p29-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 29, 4, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Our grandma ______ with us when we ______ in our village.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3-p29-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch3', 29, 5, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Everybody ______ until the fire accident occurred.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 1, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : My name is Nazia Rahman. | am a student of a famous school. My two brothers are also students of the same school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 5, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: You work in a bank. How long you here?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 2, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Deena was a student of this school too. But her two sisters were not students of this school. They studied in another school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 3, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : The bus is very late. Passengers are being impatient.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 4, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Tahmid has got a lot of toys on his birthday. He is getting restless with them.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 5, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Samrin is ill. She has been absent from the school for a few days. Her parents have been very worried about her medical treatment.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 1, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: My teachers all very qualified and trained. | do not know who he .'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 2, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: Once his father an ordinary farmer.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 3, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: your mother a housewife?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p30-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 30, 4, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: You are asking the same questions repeatedly. You silly.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 1, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : During the final exam I worked until late night.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 10, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Nobody knew how he made it possible.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 2, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Many students attended their class late because of transport strike.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 3, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Our school’s annual cultural program went very well.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 4, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : A computer operator solved the problem at last.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 5, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Who typed the whole document?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 6, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : They have all sung the national anthem in the assembly session.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 7, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : During hartal days our classes were not held.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 8, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : My father cooked all meals when he had lived overseas.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p31-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 31, 9, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : It was decided that teachers would come to school this Friday for make up classes.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4-p33-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch4', 33, NULL, 'Look at the table below and fill in the gaps with the correct form of verb: Base Form / Past Simple / Past Participle: admire / admired / ______; ban / ______ / banned; burn / burnt / ______; claim / ______ / claimed; carry / ______ / carried; chew / ______ / ______; dare / ______ / ______; employ / employed / ______; excuse / excused / ______; frighten / ______ / frightened; guess / guessed / ______; hate / ______ / ______; invent / ______ / Invented; rely / relied / ______; scold / ______ / ______; shop / shopped / ______; share / ______ / shared; shave / ______ / shaved; skip / skipped / ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5-p51-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5', 51, NULL, 'Identify adjectives in the following passage: Muntaha is Bani’s best friend. Bani is a brilliant student. She borrowed three books from Muntaha. All the books are new. The books are interesting as well. Do all the above adjectives take the same position in the sentences? In some sentences, the adjective is used before a noun. But in other sentences, the adjective comes after the verb. The adjectives that come before a noun are called attributive adjectives and those coming after a verb are called predicative adjectives.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5-p52-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5', 52, NULL, 'Use the following adjectives in different positions. One is done for you: safe, interesting, new, old, unsafe, excellent, huge, quite, cold, yellow, nice, hot, enormous, furious, gorgeous, crazy, tiny Safe: We had a safe journey. (before a noun) Our journey was safe. (after a verb) I found him safe. (after an object)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5-p52-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5', 52, NULL, 'Match the following adjectives with the nouns they go with: Adjectives: gorgeous, terrifying, tiny, exhausted, soaked, huge, starving, freezing, furious, terrible, hilarious, deafening. Nouns: crowd, insect, experience, music, temperatures, dress, customer, clothes, meal, comedy show, refugee, runner.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5-p57-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch5', 57, NULL, 'Fill in the blanks with appropriate adjectives: Sirajum Munira is a ------ girl. Bondhon is her cousin. Both of them read in the same school. Bondhon is -------- than Munira.Bondhon has a very -----brother, named Tanbin. He is so cute. To Munira’s aunt, he is ------- ------- -------- baby in the world. Munira loves Tanbin so much. She is Tanbin’s --------- sister. She plays with him. She is ------- than Tanbin.Bondhon is -------- about Tanbin, so is Munira about him. When Tanbin cries, Bondhon calls his mother and Munira gives him ------ toys. Tanbin loves ----- toys. Tanbin’s father presents him with ----- toys too.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: A wagon train that was very long started out from Laksam.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The doctor sometimes stays up all night.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The trail through the mountains was fairly hazardous.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Bangladesh is a densely populated country.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The students are inside.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: She will go to Rajshahi tomorrow.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: He will join the party tonight.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Uncle came home yesterday.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Ahsanullah Master fought against the drug smugglers bravely.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p59-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Salma is studying hard for her examination.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p61-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 61, NULL, 'Use the following adverbs of time in the box to fill in the blanks: later, occasionally, yesterday, often, in 1932 I met Abdul Matin Siddiqui ______ . He was born ______ . He had his primary education in the mid- thirties of the last century. ______ he came to Dhaka. He wrote poems ______ . His elder brother ______ inspired him.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p62-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 62, NULL, 'Use the following adverbs of place in the box to fill in the blanks: outside, back, around, nearby, everywhere, inside, there, in John looked ______ but he couldn''t see the monkey. I searched ______ I could think of. I was going ______ to camp. John built a house ______ . He took the child ______ . I found the monkey ______ the camp. John reached ______ . The monkey was sitting beside a snake there. Suddenly an elephant stepped ______ .'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Look at the following picture and then complete the passage below it using the adverbs given in the box: [Image: Three men riding on a motorcycle; the man in the middle holds an LMG (light machine gun) between them and one of them holds a fish market bag.] It was 1971. We can -------- forget those days of war. Maya was -------- serious about his purpose. He had two other companions. They rode from Gendaria. Three sat on the bike keeping the LMG in between them. They were moving towards the pre decided spot -------- , though they were pretending to be feeble and helpless with their shabby wearing. One of them was holding a fish market bag. The bike was an old one. It was not moving -------- fast. Somehow they kept their ultimate goal of urgency in their pretension. One, two Pakistani military truck passed by --------. They were facing death --------; three Pakistani soldiers were taking tea --------. But they did not notice Maya''s bike --------. Even then they did not ride -------- . At Joykali Mandir crossing a street vendor handed over to them a small packet in the fish bag --------. One of them sitting on the bike opened the packet and got three ''grenades''. His pulse increased -------- . But Maya was -------- calm. He was in the middle. He was holding the arms -------- . He was trying to remember the directions -------- . He was observing his surroundings -------- . They were moving -------- then. They moved past Baitul Mukarram Mosque --------. In front of G.P.O. there were some Pakistani soldiers, they were five in number as Maya could count -------- . No sooner had their bike reached a spot opposite to the Pak soldiers than Maya got down from the bike and opened fire upon the Pakistani soldiers. One of the soldiers was saying, "Mukut aya......." (Meaning Muktis have come.) All the Pak soldiers were killed --------. Maya and others left the spot --------. Box: accurately, unusually, strongly, rapidly, secretly, hardly, suddenly, very, fearlessly, safely, then, there, well, faster, carefully, slowly, easily, quickly, quite.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: now'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fluently'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: soon'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: then'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: hardly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: politely'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: immediately'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: quietly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fairly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6-p63-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fast'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'Let us find some prepositions in pictures. Describe the positions of the girl in each of the following pictures by using appropriate prepositions. Some of them are done for you: [Image: Twelve small pictures of a girl in different positions: a girl standing at the door of a house; a girl standing between two pillars; a girl standing inside a box; a girl standing behind a sofa; a girl standing under a big table; a girl standing on a small table; a girl standing near a desk with a computer; a girl standing in front of a desk with a computer; a girl standing next to a desk with a computer; a girl standing before a curtained doorway; a girl standing before a blackboard with sums written on it; a girl sitting at a desk.] At home. ______ the two pillars. ______ the box. ______ the sofa. ______ the big table. ______ the small table. Near the desk. In front of the desk. Next to the desk. ______ home. ______ school. ______ work.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where is the bird?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where is the rainbow?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where are the flowers?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where are the boy and the girl?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p69-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] What is the boy showing the girl?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7-p71-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch7', 71, NULL, 'See the positions of the boy in the following pictures and match the sentences with the relevant pictures: [Image: Sixteen pictures labelled a to p: a. a boy standing between two trees; b. a boy upside down (doing a handstand) beside a tree; c. a boy standing in front of a tree; d. a boy riding on a horse; e. a bird sitting in a tree; f. a boy standing to the right of a tree; g. a bird flying above a tree; h. a boy standing beside a horse; i. a boy standing to the left of a tree; j. a boy in a swimming pool; k. a boy climbing at the bottom of a ladder; l. a boy standing behind a tree (partly hidden by the tree); m. a boy standing to the right of a tree; n. a boy standing out of (beside) a swimming pool; o. a boy standing at the top of a ladder; p. a boy standing under a tree.] Sentences: i. The boy is off the horse. ii. The bird is in the tree. iii. The boy is behind the tree. iv. The boy is in front of the tree. v. The boy is to the left of the tree. vi. The boy is between the two trees. vii. The boy is under the tree. viii. The bird is above the tree. ix. The boy is upside down. x. The boy is on the horse. xi. The boy is in the swimming pool. xii. The boy is out of the swimming pool. xiii. The boy is on the right side of the tree. xiv. The boy is at the bottom of the ladder. xv. The boy is at the top of the ladder. xvi. The boy is to the left of the tree.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p79-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 79, NULL, 'Ask and answer the questions in pair: What is the function of a ‘chain’? What does the word ‘link’ mean? A chain links things together. You have certainly learnt that ‘to link’ means to connect two or more things or ideas together.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p79-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 79, NULL, 'Read the following paragraph and answer the questions that follow: Somen Chanda was born in a village named Baliya in Narsingdi on 24 May, 1920. He was an avid reader from his boyhood and he passed the Entrance Examination in 1936 from Pogose School, Dhaka. Then, he was admitted to Dhaka Mitford Medical School, but he had to discontinue his studies because of ill health. Yet, his pen did not stop. His writings S reflect struggles of the general people. Thus his writings survive him q even today. The words in italics are linking words. What are the functions of these linking words?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p81-t1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 81, 1, 'Activity: Identify the linking words in the following passage: Bangladesh was in a good team spirit in the world cup cricket tournament 1999. Besides, all the players were in good form. In fact, they proved it in the field. Anyway, they defeated a big team like Pakistan.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p81-t2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 81, 2, 'Activity: Read the following paragraph and make it meaningful by using the linking words given in the box. The first one is done for you: A student needs to have lots of qualities. He should be very studious. He should participate in outdoor games and debating activities. He should be punctual. He should have moral qualities. He should be social. He can be successful if he has these qualities. Linking words: and, firstly, thus, secondly, next, then. A student needs to have lots of qualities. Firstly, he should be very studious.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p81-t3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 81, 3, 'Activity: Fill up the blanks picking up linkers from the box below. The first one is done for you: firstly, secondly, thirdly, fourthly, to begin with, moreover, to conclude, next Several reasons were given for the language movement of the students of this country in 1952. Firstly, they were motivated to establish Bangla as their mother tongue. ______ they were committed to the ideology of Bengali Nationalism. ______ they wanted to raise awareness among the common folks of Bangladesh. ______ they gave ultimatum to the Pakistani rulers. ______ they felt frustrated and guilty in living a carefree life in the eastern part of Pakistan.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t1', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, 4, 'Activity: Rewrite the following paragraph using linking words: Dipak is twelve years old. He does not go to school. His father does not send him to school. He does not believe in education. He considers education to be a wastage of time and energy. Dipak helps his father in the poultry farm. His mother also does not find any interest in sending her son to school for some hours. Dipak is being deprived of primary education.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t2', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Purnava is a student of Jahangirnagar University. Purnava takes part in debate competitions.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t3', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Ukhin Mong is a good teacher. He does not take classes every day.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t4', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: It is raining. Rajib is going to market.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t5', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Bangladesh is a third world country. The Government of Bangladesh distributes books among all the students of primary and secondary schools.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8-p82-t6', 'class7-english-grammar-bn', 'class7-english-grammar-bn-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Kamal was sick. He did not go to school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 1, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: Abus is quicker than a rickshaw. / Buses are quicker than rickshaws.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 4, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: Do you know the ______ who lives next door? ( man/men)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q11', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 5, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: The dentist pulled out the that was hurting. (tooth/teeth)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q12', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 6, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: The __ who was waiting here has gone home. (boy/boys)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q13', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 1, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: The children ready for school. (is getting/ are getting)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q14', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 2, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: My uncle in the army. (is/are)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q15', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 3, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: The flower sweet. (smell/smells)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q16', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 4, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: The chocolates we bought very expensive. (was/were)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q17', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 5, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: The letters you posted yesterday confidential. (was/were)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q18', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 6, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or a plural verb: The young man you met yesterday transferred to this 8 office recently. (has been/ have been)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 2, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: A tiger is a ferocious animal. / ______'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 3, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: A banker earns more money than a teacher. / ______'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 4, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: A laptop is an expensive piece of equipment. / ______'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 5, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: Astudent has to work hard. / ______'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 6, 'Rewrite these sentences using plural nouns. One is done for you: Agood book helps to pass time. / ______'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 1, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: The stops outside our house. (car / cars).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 2, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: The were waiting for me. (child/children)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p3-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 3, 3, 'Complete these sentences with a singular or plural noun: The are in the shelf. ( book/books)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p5-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 5, NULL, 'Now use personal pronouns in the following text: Maruf’s father is a businessman. has been in business for about 15 years. Currently in his farm, there are 20 people working full time. has three children who are going to school. Maruf is second child.The youngest and eldest are both daughters.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p5-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 5, NULL, 'Let us use pronouns in their possessive forms. Look at the examples : This is our school. Who is your brother? Do you know where my pen is? Look at the following sentences. ‘Yours’, ‘hers’, ‘his’ and ‘ours’ are also possessives. This is my book. That is yours. These toys are hers. This bicycle is his. This garden is ours. Now use possessives in the following sentences. After retirement Mr Kamal is living in own village. He lives with his wife who has also retired from job as a school teacher. children live in Bogra where they have own © families. children often ask them to visit them.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p6-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 6, NULL, 'Now look at the passage below and fill in the gaps with adjectives: My uncle is a ______ engineer. He works in a ______ company as a ______ engineer. He graduated in ______ engineering from BUET. He also studied abroad for his ______ qualification. Currently he is in charge of a ______ project.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p7-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 7, 1, 'Now use appropriate words in the blanks of the following sentences: My friend Tumpa is ______ in music. But she thinks cricket is an ______ game.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p7-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 7, 2, 'Now use appropriate words in the blanks of the following sentences: Moynamoti is an ______ place to visit but my uncle was ______ with the long journey there.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p7-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 7, 3, 'Now use appropriate words in the blanks of the following sentences: I felt really ______ to see my teacher in my uncle’s wedding; it was ______ too.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p7-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 7, 4, 'Now use appropriate words in the blanks of the following sentences: The film was quite ______ but I felt ______ to my favorite heroine there.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p7-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 7, 5, 'Now use appropriate words in the blanks of the following sentences: I was so ______ in the work that I could finish in due time. And my teacher thinks it is ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p10-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 10, NULL, 'Use the following prepositions in sentences of your own: with, on, in, to, up, over, for, at, of, by,'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch1-p10-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch1', 10, NULL, 'Complete the following text by using appropriate prepositions. My auntie lives ______ Mogbazar just ______ Holy Family Hospital. Her flat is ______ the 5th floor. She lives ______ her family there. She often visits her good friend and neighbour who lives just one floor up; the top floor ______ the building. My auntie has been living in her flat ______ the last three years.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p90-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 90, NULL, 'Find out the possessives: Whose child is this? “Whose child is this?” | asked one day Seeing a little one out at play. “Mine”, said the parent with a tender smile © “Mine to keep a little while To bathe his hands and comb his hair To tell him what he is to wear To prepare him that he may always be good And each day do the things he should” “Whose child is this?” | asked again As the door opened and someone came in “Mine,’said the teacher with the same tender smile “Mine,” to keep just for a little while To teach him how to be gentle and kind To train and direct his dear little mind To help him live by every rule And get the best he can from school” “Whose child is this?” | asked once more Just as the little one entered the door “Ours”, said the parent and the teacher as they smiled And each took the hand of the little child “Ours to love and train together Ours this blessed task forever.” [Anonymous]'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, NULL, 'Identify the possessives in the following story: Two sick men were given the same room in a hospital. One man could sit up in his bed for about an hour. His bed was next to the room’s only window. The other man spent all his time lying on his bed opposite the window. The men talked for hours almost every day. They talked about their wives and children, their homes, their jobs and almost about everything. Every afternoon the man in the bed by the window would sit up and talked to his roommate about all the things he could see outside the window. The man on the other bed eagerly waited for this speaking and listening time. His friend’s vivid descriptions of passing things seen through the window inspired him to live. The window overlooked a park with a lovely lake. Ducks and swans play on the water, while children float their paper boats. A wonderful view of the skyline can be seen in the distance. The man by the window told his friend all this in detail. The listener would close his eyes and see everything in his mind’s eye.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 1, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: This is a tiger. Its body has stripes. => The tiger’s body has stripes.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 2, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: There are spiders. Their webs catch insects.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 3, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: There is a book on the table. Its pictures are obscure.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 4, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: There is a cat. Its baby is called a kitten.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 5, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: There is one shark. Its teeth are sharp.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 6, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: There are sheep. Their fur keeps them warm.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch10-p94-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch10', 94, 7, 'Singular and plural possessive nouns: Bangladesh is a beautiful country. Its nature is green.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p95-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 95, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: What do you do in your spare time?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p95-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 95, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Write 3 sentences about your pastime.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p96-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 96, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: What class do you read in?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p96-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 96, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: What is the name of your school?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p96-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 96, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: What is the name of your country?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p97-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 97, 1, '[Image: A black-and-white photograph of a village house with a tin roof among trees (banana and coconut palms), a cow grazing nearby, and a winding path crossing an open field in front of the house.] Look at the following picture and talk about it: <3 > hall + ae or Aspe e 7 + eg | ye. wae As Es TEE Sa ne wee rf. , wy. oo me , mie 8, i > Si me ae 7 & ot ars a vy e a } ro : ot Sit Sy Fe PX < At - « co a ZS . eat a '' te aie ¢ Ye ——"" 7 y , ° ey pom iren” VA ke i mm ee ar Ht Ls q iittala es bite ie ee - E Sik ] ‘ - : apf bene = be'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p97-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 97, 2, '[Image: A black-and-white photograph of a village house with a tin roof among trees (banana and coconut palms), a cow grazing nearby, and a winding path crossing an open field in front of the house.] Write 10 sentences about what you see in the picture.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p98-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 98, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Can you write your name?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p98-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 98, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Can you ride a bicycle?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p98-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 98, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Can you swim?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p98-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 98, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Do you have a computer at your home?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p98-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 98, NULL, 'Ask and answer the following questions: Do you like to speak English?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p100-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 100, NULL, 'Read the following sentences in Column A and match them with the negative sentences in Column B. One is done for you: Column A: 1. The Royal Bengal Tigers are available in the Sundarbans. 2. Have you ever seen any Royal Bengal Tiger? 3. You can see tigers only in the zoo. 4. The tiger is a rare animal. 5. The Royal Bengal Tiger is a beautiful animal. Column B: 1. Haven''t you ever seen any Royal Bengal Tiger? 2. Isn''t the Royal Bengal Tiger a beautiful animal? 3. The tiger is not a common animal. 4. Nowhere but in the zoo you can see tigers. 5. The Royal Bengal Tigers are not rare in the Sundarbans.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p101-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 101, NULL, 'Match the sentences on the right column with those on the left. One is done for you: Left column: a) He is an honest man. b) Lions are available in the jungles of Africa. c) The old man cannot walk fast. d) That stranger is found nowhere. e) He is the best player in the team. f) A mouse is afraid of a rat. g) Manik never tells a lie. h) Always speak the truth. i) Only a bird can fly so high. j) None but the shopkeeper was waiting there. Right column: a) The old man can walk slowly. b) The stranger is not found anywhere. c) It is not that a mouse is not afraid of a rat. d) Lions are not unavailable in jungles of Africa. e) Manik always speaks the truth. f) Only the shop keeper was waiting there. g) Is he not an honest man? h) Nothing but a bird can fly so high. i) No other player in the team is as good as he. j) Never tell a lie.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p104-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 104, NULL, 'Write a dialogue between you and your friend to get some information to write a paragraph on ‘My Friend’.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p104-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 104, NULL, 'Write a paragraph on ‘My Friend’.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 1, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Ask your friend to switch on the light.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 10, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Tell your classmates to go to the stadium to watch a cricket match.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 2, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Ask for snacks in a restaurant.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 3, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Advise your younger brother to be attentive in study.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 4, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Request your mother to give something.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 5, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Ask somebody not to do something.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 6, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Teacher tells a student to go out of the room.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 7, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Somebody is very angry and asking someone to do something immediately.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 8, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : Ask somebody to remember something.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p107-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 107, 9, 'Read the situations below and write imperative sentences. Remember, a positive imperative begins with a main verb and a negative imperative begins with a negative auxiliary (do not / don’t) : A naughty boy is giving a threat to one of his friends.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p108-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 108, NULL, 'Read the passage below and fill in the gaps with the words in the box: Box: don''t, let''s, should, never, snatch. Rifat went to his village home in the Summer holiday. He enjoyed the time very much with his cousins there. They went to many places around the village. One of his cousins showed him a bird''s nest in a banyan tree. All of them were excited to see the nest and the baby birds. One of them ran to the tree and tried to climb on to catch the baby birds. Rifat said to him, "No, ----- do that. Don''t ----- away the kids from their mother." Nantu said, "But it is fun, ----- climb the tree and watch what the kids are doing." Rifat said, "We ----- not disturb them." Milon said, "Right, our teacher said, "----- torture the baby birds or any other animals around us for your pleasure. It is harmful for the environment."'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p108-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 108, 1, 'You went to your village to meet your relatives. You found that some village children cannot wash hands properly. Write how you will encourage them to wash their hands properly using imperative sentences.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p108-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 108, 2, 'Recall how your teachers gave instructions using imperative sentences and write at least five of them.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p108-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 108, 3, 'Does your mother/father advise/ forbid/ request you to do something using imperative sentences? Write at least 10 of them.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p108-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 108, 4, 'If/ you/ want/ a glass of water, how will you ask your younger brother/sister for it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Suppose you are for the first time on the beach of Cox’s Bazar. Describe how you express your wonder in exclamatory sentences.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: I wish I would be a King.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: The garden is very charming.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: We rejoice that our team won the match.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: I wish you good morning sir.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: The place is very dirty.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: Let curse befall the traitors of the country.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: This town is very peaceful.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p111-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 111, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences as exclamatory sentences: I am very desirous to meet you once more.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p112-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 112, 1, 'Write how you wish your friend for coming round soon from sickness.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p112-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 112, 2, 'Write a message wishing a happy new year to any of your close friends or relatives.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p112-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 112, 3, 'Pray for the welfare of your country.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p112-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 112, 4, 'Pray for somebody to be successful in business.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch11-p112-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch11', 112, 5, 'Pray for the Bangladesh cricket team to win the match and prepare three banners.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch12-p116-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch12', 116, 1, '[Image: A black-and-white photograph of a busy city street crowded with buses, cars and crowds of people, lined with multi-storey buildings carrying billboards and shop signs.] Look at the picture and describe what you see in the picture and write sentences on the structure there + to be + singular/plural subjects: 4 bh . — eric | LS Saeante i\ { = — ~ 5 See ee eee ee | Ty Mie ish peaeie- a | i t = = = Song [sill nT ihe ae sisi. Rae ae Yb ad hal isos a OP St hivS oe gt eee po hl ret TE, Oris x Sin- gee Papel s (ie aol ae oa ge One Sic oa tt eh WS a wa — LJ : Md : ead ~ ae /) ee a TAS aa an -. Te ae 4 Satay = i e > a Ra rs aa ; 5 act a - as 3 a x ae . ; = Ra) d é u ps ie / fee o> ae Le aan'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch12-p116-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch12', 116, 2, 'Now write a paragraph on‘A Street”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch12-p117-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch12', 117, NULL, 'Make sentences with the words in the following table: There | is | a bridge over the river; There | are | a tree in front of the house; There | was | some girls on the roof; There | were | many birds in the winter season in Bangladesh; There | must be | no snakes in the garden; There | have been/has been | mosquitoes in the jungle; There | shall/will be | some problem with her; There | ______ | nobody like you; There | ______ | no denying the fact that he killed the bird; There | ______ | no storm; There | ______ | no way to come out; There | ______ | many children to go to sleep without food.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p119-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 119, 1, 'Look at the pictures and say what things are there. One is done for you: [Image: Ten numbered pictures: 1. a cat sitting on a chair; 2. a boat crowded with people; 3. a bunch of flowers in a vase; 4. a boat on water; 5. a decorated vase; 6. a plastic water bottle; 7. two birds on a tree branch; 8. a water bottle; 9. a wooden chair; 10. a tree.] What is there in picture 1? - There is a cat on the chair.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p119-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 119, 2, 'Look at the pictures and say what things are there. One is done for you: [Image: Ten numbered pictures: 1. a cat sitting on a chair; 2. a boat crowded with people; 3. a bunch of flowers in a vase; 4. a boat on water; 5. a decorated vase; 6. a plastic water bottle; 7. two birds on a tree branch; 8. a water bottle; 9. a wooden chair; 10. a tree.] Is there any water in the bottle of picture 6? - No, there isn’t any water in the bottle.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p120-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 120, NULL, 'Look at the picture of a living room. Make a list of things in the room and also say what things are not in the room. [Image: A black-and-white photograph of a living room with a white sofa set, a rug, a wooden cabinet, framed pictures on the wall, a tall plant by a glass door, and windows with dark curtains.]'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p122-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 122, 1, 'Write a dialogue using ‘there isn’t’ and ‘there aren’t’ and act it out (group work). Some clues are given in the table below: There isn’t/aren’t any computer in this room; any bad smell here; any germs in the water; any mosquitoes in this room; any dust in this room; any water in the bottle.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, 2, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you:'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There are no tourists in this season.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q11', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is no electricity in the city.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q12', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, 3, 'Suppose,there is no tubewell for drinking water in your village. You have to go to the neighbouring village to collect drinking water. The people in the village are suffering from various kinds of diseases and problems. Describe all these problems to your friend. You can start this way: There isn’t any tubewell in our village.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There are many villages in our country. There aren’t many villages in our country.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is a biting dog in the house.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is an old tree beside the river.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There are no snakes in the jungle.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is no police man in the street.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There are no beggars on the station.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is no cleaner in the hotel.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch13-p123-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch13', 123, NULL, 'Rewrite the following sentences using ‘isn’t/ aren’t’. One is done for you: There is no room service in this hotel.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p125-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 125, NULL, 'Read the passage below and identify ‘to+ infinitives’ and ‘bare infinitives’: A crow was thirsty. He was flying around to find water. The day was very hot. Water was not available anywhere. Suddenly the crow found a pitcher. He thought there might be water in the pitcher. But the water was at the bottom of the pitcher. The crow was wondering how to drink the water. As he began to look around, he saw some pebbles lying on the ground nearby. Seeing this, he thought of a way to use the pebbles to reach the water at the bottom of the pitcher. Then the crow picked up the pebbles with his beak and dropped them in the pitcher to make the water rise. Soon the water level was high enough for the crow to reach. Thus he was able to drink enough water to quench his thirst.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p127-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 127, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: Eliza recommended ---------- (eat) in a low cost restaurant while we''re in Hong Kong.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: I demand ---------- (talk) to the manager of the hotel immediately.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: I began (learn) French when I was a young boy.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q11', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: We thanked him for (come) to the party.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q12', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: He keeps (lie) to everybody.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q13', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: Would you mind (open) the window please?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q14', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: John has at last given up (smoke).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q15', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: Mary doesn''t like (be) late for school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q16', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: (Read) novels is his favourite pastime.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q17', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: Don''t start (sing) until you are asked to.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q18', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: Do you remember (write) to him?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q19', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Complete with right form of verbs: Jack can''t stand (ride) a bus. What kind of verbs are these? -----------------------'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: My grandmother recalled --------- (see) a plane for the very first time when she was six.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: She claims ------- (be) related to George Washington, but I don''t believe her.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: This broken bicycle needs -------- (fix) before someone can ride it.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: I can''t think of ------- (drive) such a big car when gas prices are so high, not to mention what it does to the environment.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: She managed -------- (communicate) with them, even though she didn''t speak their language.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: Don''t hesitate ------- (ask) for help if you don''t understand the directions.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: The course lasts ten days and involves --------- (hike) more than fifty miles through rugged mountainous terrain.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p128-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 128, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verbs: She refused --------- (speak) to me after our fight. What kind of verbs are these? ------------------------------'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, 3, 'Write the past participles of the following verbs. An example is given for you: Verb / Present participle / Past participle: sleep / sleeping / slept; publish / ______ / ______; go / ______ / ______; find / ______ / ______; arrest / ______ / ______; swim / ______ / ______; develop / ______ / ______; pick / ______ / ______; fall / ______ / ______; say / ______ / ______; give / ______ / ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: This story is--------(go) to be published in the magazine.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: It’s -------- outside (rain).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: I found the girl in the garden ------- (sleep) alone.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: The thief was ------ (catch) by the people.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: Mr. Mamun is in his living room ------ (watch) television.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch14-p129-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch14', 129, NULL, 'Fill in the gaps with the right form of verb: This news will be ------ (publish) in The Daily Star.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch15-p131-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch15', 131, NULL, 'Read the following passage and rewrite it using capital letters where necessary: mahmuda is an intelligent girl. she reads in class 7. the name of her school is kushumpur high school. her favourite subject is english. She has one sister, named lubna. they live in kushumpur, a village in bogra.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch15-p135-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch15', 135, NULL, 'Rewrite the following passage using capital letters and appropriate punctuation marks: rip van winkle stopped by a place where there had been a school and asked the crowd that had gathered where is schooner, the school master somebody said oh schooner he went to war in sixty three and never came back and van ammel asked rip van winkle he died eighteen years back said another voice in the crowd rip van winkle thought he was going mad had he slept all these years on the mountain finally rip van winkle asked does anyone here remember rip van winkle a very old woman said yes he was my lazy son he went up the mountains twenty one years back but never returned His dog came back without him rip van winkle was overjoyed he said mother it is me rip van winkle dont you recognize me oh my son it is really you where have you been all this while mother and son hugged each other. rip van winkle had indeed slept for twenty-one years.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p138-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 138, 1, 'Now rewrite the following in indirect speech: Maria said to her mother, ‘I have got 10 out of 10 in mathematics class test. I am very happy. My teacher became very happy. I''ll do my homework regularly. Then I’ll get good marks in every subject.’ Mom said to Maria, ‘Practice makes a man perfect’.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: I say, “I want to sleep.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: Meena said, “I am very busy now.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: He says, “I like mangoes”.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: You said, “I will meet my teacher.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: They said, “We are starting now.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: Mother said to me, “I was waiting for you for a long time.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: Maria says, “My father is an Engineer.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: He said, “I have passed the math test.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: She said to me, “You are my only friend.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p139-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 139, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect speeches: He said, “I have got a bad headache.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p140-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 140, NULL, 'Change the following sentence into indirect speech: Robi said to Maria, “Why are you crying? What makes you so upset? Is there anything wrong with your classmates? Have you got punishment in school?” Maria said, “Why are you so anxious?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: Maria said to her mother, “Do you always get up early?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: He said to me, “Do you like music?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: The teacher said to Maria, “Who were you waiting for?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: I said to you, “What do you want?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: The policeman said to him, “Are you in a hurry to cross the road?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p141-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 141, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into indirect: Jaya said to the watchman, “Did you find the key anywhere?”'),
