  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p147-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 147, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into Indirect Speech : Boys said,” Hurrah! We have won the match.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p147-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 147, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into Indirect Speech : She said, “What a beautiful bird it is!”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p147-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 147, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into Indirect Speech : Father said, “What a lazy fellow she is!”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch16-p147-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch16', 147, NULL, 'Change the following sentences into Indirect Speech : The cobbler said, “How stupid I am!”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p152-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 152, NULL, 'Read the following passage and underline the active and passive verbs: The Sonargaon folk museum was built in the area named Narayangonj. It has been artistically decorated for the visitors. It stores many archaeological things including Bronze statues and caskets, terracotta plaques, utensils, coins, jewelries, pottery etc. They have a great historical value. The government has taken many steps to enhance the facilities for the visitors.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p152-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 152, NULL, 'Use the following verbs in active and passive forms: touch, invite, decorate, touch, break, request'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p152-e3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 152, NULL, 'Change the sentences into the passive voice. Mention the tense of the verb. Our new teacher teaches us English. Now, he is teaching us a new lesson. We have completed the lesson on paragraphs. We are practicing the new lesson. Our teacher taught us the skills of learning language. Last week we were practicing pronunciation. We had learnt the uses of articles before we learnt the rules. We will write a paragraph tomorrow.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 1, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: The criminal ______ (send) to prison. (Future simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 10, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: They ______ (teach) English. (Present simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 2, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: My brother ______ (just win) the game. (Present perfect)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 3, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: I ______ (tell) you to wait outside. (Past simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 4, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: Ruma ______ (not pay) for the work. (Past simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 5, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: Policemen ______ (often ask) the way. (Present simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 6, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: The room ______ (clean) once a day. (Present simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 7, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: The letter ______ (write) tomorrow. (Future simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 8, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: The towels ______ (not use). (Past simple tense)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch17-p157-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch17', 157, 9, 'Fill in the blanks according to the mentioned tenses. Use the appropriate forms of verbs given in brackets: He ______ (not sell) the books. (Present perfect)'),
