  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p17-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 17, 8, 'Now use the correct form of verbs in the following gaps : Things in this shop ______ expensive.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p17-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 17, 9, 'Now use the correct form of verbs in the following gaps : Mom often asks me, “Do you brush your teeth regularly?” “Yes, I ______.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 1, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the following gaps : When I ______ a child I ______ how to ride a bicycle. My elder brother ______ me carefully and at one stage I ______ able to learn it.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 6, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: We/ celebrate/ in our village/holiday'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q11', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 7, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: Why / you come/ late to class?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q12', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 8, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: | / come late/ because it / rain/ in the morning'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q13', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 9, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: When /your father/ promote/ as General Manager?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q14', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 10, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: My father/ promote/ early this year.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 2, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the following gaps : Our school ______ an inter school debate competition On 23 March and we ______ the runner up position. We ______ a certificate and a crest from the chief guest.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 3, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the following gaps : Last night we ______ no electricity in our locality. My father ______ some candles nd we all ______ a candle light dinner. It ______ a great fun.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 4, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the following gaps : He ______ play football in his youth.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 1, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: Who/you see/ in the room? Who did you see in the room?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 2, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: I see/ Jamal /there'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 3, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: When / you go/ to school?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 4, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: We/ go / to school/ at 8.15 am.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p19-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 19, 5, 'Make past tense questions and answers using the words given. One is done for you: Where / you celebrate/ your holiday?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, 1, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : Next Saturday my uncle ______ for Saudi Arabia. So my father and I ______ to the airport to see him off.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, 2, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : The weather forecast says it ______ rain tomorrow.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, 3, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : I ______ an umbrella if it rains.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, 4, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : The waiter says, “ ______ I give you cold drinks, sir?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, 5, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : I am going home now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p20-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 20, NULL, 'Supply the correct form of verbs in the gap of the following sentences : I am going home now. Ok, I ______ you Sunday morning.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, NULL, 'Suppose you and your partner are playing the role of a palmist and a client. The dialogue will go like this. Use the verbs employ, earn, export, offer and import and complete the dialogue: Palmist : You will have a big business in future. Client : What kind of business? P : It will be a garment business'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, NULL, 'Now match these sentences with the predictions below: Sentences: 1. It''s Friday morning 2. I am back from my school 3. If you are not careful 4. On Fridays 5. The class teacher is coming to the class. Predictions: a. she will call our names b. shops will remain open. c. I will take some rest now. d. we will say our Jumma prayer. e. you will slip from the steep staircase.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, 1, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: Don’t worry; the student volunteers will manage discipline about the program.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, 2, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I am sure you ______ your visit to Rangamaati.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, 3, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I ______ you tonight and ______ you about the situation.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, 4, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: I am very tired. I ______ to bed early tonight.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p21-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 21, 5, 'Use the correct verbs in the following sentences. The first one is done for you: People are very angry about the problem. They ______ a compromising solution of the problem.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 1, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Nafisa’s school is closed today. She is reading a story book.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 2, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Asif : What are you doing now? Come and join us in a game if you are free. Maruf : Sorry, I can’t. I am taking my sister to a doctor. She is suffering from fever.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 3, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Please don’t interrupt me while I am talking over the phone.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 4, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Desk officer: Are you being served? Client: Yes, that young lady is helping me.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 5, 'Read the following text and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Teacher:Are you listening to me? Students: Yes ma’m, we are.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 1, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Take this umbrella. It ______ outside now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 2, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : “ ______ you still ______ in a bank?” “No, recently I have left it.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 3, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Please don’t disturb me. I ______ my homework.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p22-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 22, 4, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : Please wait for a minute. I ______ soon.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 5, 'Supply appropriate verbs in the gaps of the following sentences : There are a few doctors in this clinic. Many patients (not) ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 1, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: I am going to visit my grandma this weekend. What about you?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 2, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Do you think our teacher is going to give us a good grade for this assignment?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 3, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: Who of you are going to work as volunteers? Please raise your hands.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 4, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: When is your uncle coming back from his overseas study?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p23-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 23, 5, 'Read the following sentences and look at the underlined verbs. Tell your partner which tense it is: It is going to be a big problem if you do not pay attention to it now.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p24-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 24, 1, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you decided to spend extra money? B: Well, I think I ______ to a restaurant for a good dinner but haven’t decided yet.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p24-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 24, 2, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you decided how you will spend the holiday? B: Not yet but I think I ______ to my village for a few days.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p24-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 24, 3, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: My cousins are coming from Italy this Friday. B: ______ you ______ to receive them at the airport?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p24-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 24, 5, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Our school has set up a new routine for our classes effective from this Saturday. B: Yes, we ______ to attend the first class much earlier.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p24-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 24, 6, 'Now complete the dialogues below using the verbs in brackets with will or going to: A: Have you collected your tickets for the concert? B: Not yet. But I think we ______ there on Friday if we can.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, NULL, 'Compare these two remarks: Why, do you think, is the form of the verb ''rain'' different in (a) and (b)? (a) It will rain tomorrow as soon as we get to the park. (b) According to the weather forecast it''s going to rain tomorrow. May be we shouldn''t go to the park.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, 1, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: The opposition has called a strike on Sunday. I ______ (not go) to attend my classes.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, 2, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: I ______ (carry) an umbrella if it rains.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, 3, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: The way all Kiwi wickets are falling, I think Tigers ______ (win) the match easily.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, 4, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: Son: Father, any plan for the weekend? Father: Our whole family has been invited to my colleague’s daughter’s wedding. So, we ______ (attend) the party.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p25-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 25, 5, 'Now use will or be going to in the following sentences: It is not cold here. I ______ (wear) a jumper.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 1, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Please open your book. Have you (open) it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 2, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Wow! It’s a wonderful piece of drawing. Who ______ (draw) it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 3, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Excuse me, teacher. Could you please repeat what you ______ (say) just now?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 4, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: I am very worried about my homework. I ______ (not finish) it yet.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 5, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: There is a big museum in the city. ______ you ______ there?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p26-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 26, 6, 'Now, look at the following sentences and fill in the blanks with appropriate forms of verbs of the present perfect: Please tell me what exactly you ______ done and what is yet to be done.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 1, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Teacher: We have only one day left for the science fair. Now let me know who ______ what. Zarif: I ______ the wall, sir.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 2, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Mother: There are only a few chocolates on the table. Who ______ the others? Mayisha: Mom, I ______ just one.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 3, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Teacher: Let’s brainstorm on the topic for a minute. Now Anika, tell me what ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 4, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : Hanif: Wait, this math problem is not that easy. But I ______ something about it. Monoj: Ok, tell us what ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 5, 'Now use appropriate verbs in the blanks of the following dialogues : ‘Three Idiots’ is an excellent movie. ______ you ______ it?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p27-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 27, 1, 'Write some sentences about your activities you have done since morning. Show your sentences to your partner to check. You may start like this. First, I have said my morning prayer.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 1, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The sun (shine) when we went out.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 10, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: Who (talk) there when I knocked at the door? “I (call) my sister.”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 2, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: When you came, I (write).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 3, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: My brother asked me, “Why didn’t you receive my call?” “I (sleep) then”.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 4, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: When the teacher came to the class, all students (stand) up.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 5, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The bus started while some passengers (get) on.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 6, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The boy took another piece of cake when the mother (not look).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 7, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The teacher asked his students,‘Why you (make) a noise in the class?”'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 8, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: We (have) dinner when electricity went off.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p28-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 28, 9, 'Use the past continuous form of the verbs in the following sentences: The boy jumped off the train while it (move).'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p29-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 29, 1, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: It ______ heavily outside when I ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p29-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 29, 2, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Where ______ when I ______ you?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p29-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 29, 3, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: When my elder ______ my father ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p29-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 29, 4, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Our grandma ______ with us when we ______ in our village.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch3-p29-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch3', 29, 5, 'Use the correct forms of verbs in the blanks of the following sentences: Everybody ______ until the fire accident occurred.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 1, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : My name is Nazia Rahman. | am a student of a famous school. My two brothers are also students of the same school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 5, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: You work in a bank. How long you here?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 2, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Deena was a student of this school too. But her two sisters were not students of this school. They studied in another school.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 3, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : The bus is very late. Passengers are being impatient.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 4, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Tahmid has got a lot of toys on his birthday. He is getting restless with them.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 5, 'Look at the underlined words and guess what these are : Samrin is ill. She has been absent from the school for a few days. Her parents have been very worried about her medical treatment.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 1, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: My teachers all very qualified and trained. | do not know who he .'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 2, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: Once his father an ordinary farmer.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 3, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: your mother a housewife?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p30-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 30, 4, 'Write the correct forms of ‘be verbs’in the gaps of the following sentences: You are asking the same questions repeatedly. You silly.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 1, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : During the final exam I worked until late night.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 10, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Nobody knew how he made it possible.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 2, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Many students attended their class late because of transport strike.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 3, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Our school’s annual cultural program went very well.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 4, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : A computer operator solved the problem at last.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 5, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : Who typed the whole document?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 6, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : They have all sung the national anthem in the assembly session.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 7, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : During hartal days our classes were not held.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 8, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : My father cooked all meals when he had lived overseas.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p31-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 31, 9, 'Look at the underlined verbs and guess if these are regular or irregular : It was decided that teachers would come to school this Friday for make up classes.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch4-p33-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch4', 33, NULL, 'Look at the table below and fill in the gaps with the correct form of verb: Base Form / Past Simple / Past Participle: admire / admired / ______; ban / ______ / banned; burn / burnt / ______; claim / ______ / claimed; carry / ______ / carried; chew / ______ / ______; dare / ______ / ______; employ / employed / ______; excuse / excused / ______; frighten / ______ / frightened; guess / guessed / ______; hate / ______ / ______; invent / ______ / Invented; rely / relied / ______; scold / ______ / ______; shop / shopped / ______; share / ______ / shared; shave / ______ / shaved; skip / skipped / ______.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch5-p51-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch5', 51, NULL, 'Identify adjectives in the following passage: Muntaha is Bani’s best friend. Bani is a brilliant student. She borrowed three books from Muntaha. All the books are new. The books are interesting as well. Do all the above adjectives take the same position in the sentences? In some sentences, the adjective is used before a noun. But in other sentences, the adjective comes after the verb. The adjectives that come before a noun are called attributive adjectives and those coming after a verb are called predicative adjectives.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch5-p52-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch5', 52, NULL, 'Use the following adjectives in different positions. One is done for you: safe, interesting, new, old, unsafe, excellent, huge, quite, cold, yellow, nice, hot, enormous, furious, gorgeous, crazy, tiny Safe: We had a safe journey. (before a noun) Our journey was safe. (after a verb) I found him safe. (after an object)'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch5-p52-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch5', 52, NULL, 'Match the following adjectives with the nouns they go with: Adjectives: gorgeous, terrifying, tiny, exhausted, soaked, huge, starving, freezing, furious, terrible, hilarious, deafening. Nouns: crowd, insect, experience, music, temperatures, dress, customer, clothes, meal, comedy show, refugee, runner.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch5-p57-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch5', 57, NULL, 'Fill in the blanks with appropriate adjectives: Sirajum Munira is a ------ girl. Bondhon is her cousin. Both of them read in the same school. Bondhon is -------- than Munira.Bondhon has a very -----brother, named Tanbin. He is so cute. To Munira’s aunt, he is ------- ------- -------- baby in the world. Munira loves Tanbin so much. She is Tanbin’s --------- sister. She plays with him. She is ------- than Tanbin.Bondhon is -------- about Tanbin, so is Munira about him. When Tanbin cries, Bondhon calls his mother and Munira gives him ------ toys. Tanbin loves ----- toys. Tanbin’s father presents him with ----- toys too.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: A wagon train that was very long started out from Laksam.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The doctor sometimes stays up all night.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The trail through the mountains was fairly hazardous.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Bangladesh is a densely populated country.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: The students are inside.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: She will go to Rajshahi tomorrow.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: He will join the party tonight.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Uncle came home yesterday.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Ahsanullah Master fought against the drug smugglers bravely.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p59-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 59, NULL, 'Identify the adverbs in the following sentences and say which words they modify: Salma is studying hard for her examination.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p61-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 61, NULL, 'Use the following adverbs of time in the box to fill in the blanks: later, occasionally, yesterday, often, in 1932 I met Abdul Matin Siddiqui ______ . He was born ______ . He had his primary education in the mid- thirties of the last century. ______ he came to Dhaka. He wrote poems ______ . His elder brother ______ inspired him.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p62-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 62, NULL, 'Use the following adverbs of place in the box to fill in the blanks: outside, back, around, nearby, everywhere, inside, there, in John looked ______ but he couldn''t see the monkey. I searched ______ I could think of. I was going ______ to camp. John built a house ______ . He took the child ______ . I found the monkey ______ the camp. John reached ______ . The monkey was sitting beside a snake there. Suddenly an elephant stepped ______ .'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Look at the following picture and then complete the passage below it using the adverbs given in the box: [Image: Three men riding on a motorcycle; the man in the middle holds an LMG (light machine gun) between them and one of them holds a fish market bag.] It was 1971. We can -------- forget those days of war. Maya was -------- serious about his purpose. He had two other companions. They rode from Gendaria. Three sat on the bike keeping the LMG in between them. They were moving towards the pre decided spot -------- , though they were pretending to be feeble and helpless with their shabby wearing. One of them was holding a fish market bag. The bike was an old one. It was not moving -------- fast. Somehow they kept their ultimate goal of urgency in their pretension. One, two Pakistani military truck passed by --------. They were facing death --------; three Pakistani soldiers were taking tea --------. But they did not notice Maya''s bike --------. Even then they did not ride -------- . At Joykali Mandir crossing a street vendor handed over to them a small packet in the fish bag --------. One of them sitting on the bike opened the packet and got three ''grenades''. His pulse increased -------- . But Maya was -------- calm. He was in the middle. He was holding the arms -------- . He was trying to remember the directions -------- . He was observing his surroundings -------- . They were moving -------- then. They moved past Baitul Mukarram Mosque --------. In front of G.P.O. there were some Pakistani soldiers, they were five in number as Maya could count -------- . No sooner had their bike reached a spot opposite to the Pak soldiers than Maya got down from the bike and opened fire upon the Pakistani soldiers. One of the soldiers was saying, "Mukut aya......." (Meaning Muktis have come.) All the Pak soldiers were killed --------. Maya and others left the spot --------. Box: accurately, unusually, strongly, rapidly, secretly, hardly, suddenly, very, fearlessly, safely, then, there, well, faster, carefully, slowly, easily, quickly, quite.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: now'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q10', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fluently'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: soon'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: then'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: hardly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: politely'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: immediately'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q7', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: quietly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q8', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fairly'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch6-p63-q9', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch6', 63, NULL, 'Use each of the following adverbs in a sentence and say which word it modifies. One is done for you: fast'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'Let us find some prepositions in pictures. Describe the positions of the girl in each of the following pictures by using appropriate prepositions. Some of them are done for you: [Image: Twelve small pictures of a girl in different positions: a girl standing at the door of a house; a girl standing between two pillars; a girl standing inside a box; a girl standing behind a sofa; a girl standing under a big table; a girl standing on a small table; a girl standing near a desk with a computer; a girl standing in front of a desk with a computer; a girl standing next to a desk with a computer; a girl standing before a curtained doorway; a girl standing before a blackboard with sums written on it; a girl sitting at a desk.] At home. ______ the two pillars. ______ the box. ______ the sofa. ______ the big table. ______ the small table. Near the desk. In front of the desk. Next to the desk. ______ home. ______ school. ______ work.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-q1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where is the bird?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-q2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where is the rainbow?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-q3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where are the flowers?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-q4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] Where are the boy and the girl?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p69-q5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'See the picture below carefully and answer the questions accordingly: [Image: A boy and a girl stand in a garden beside a winding path; the boy points toward a bird sitting on a tree branch; a rainbow arcs in the sky behind them; flowers grow in the foreground and bushes line the path.] What is the boy showing the girl?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch7-p71-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch7', 71, NULL, 'See the positions of the boy in the following pictures and match the sentences with the relevant pictures: [Image: Sixteen pictures labelled a to p: a. a boy standing between two trees; b. a boy upside down (doing a handstand) beside a tree; c. a boy standing in front of a tree; d. a boy riding on a horse; e. a bird sitting in a tree; f. a boy standing to the right of a tree; g. a bird flying above a tree; h. a boy standing beside a horse; i. a boy standing to the left of a tree; j. a boy in a swimming pool; k. a boy climbing at the bottom of a ladder; l. a boy standing behind a tree (partly hidden by the tree); m. a boy standing to the right of a tree; n. a boy standing out of (beside) a swimming pool; o. a boy standing at the top of a ladder; p. a boy standing under a tree.] Sentences: i. The boy is off the horse. ii. The bird is in the tree. iii. The boy is behind the tree. iv. The boy is in front of the tree. v. The boy is to the left of the tree. vi. The boy is between the two trees. vii. The boy is under the tree. viii. The bird is above the tree. ix. The boy is upside down. x. The boy is on the horse. xi. The boy is in the swimming pool. xii. The boy is out of the swimming pool. xiii. The boy is on the right side of the tree. xiv. The boy is at the bottom of the ladder. xv. The boy is at the top of the ladder. xvi. The boy is to the left of the tree.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p79-e1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 79, NULL, 'Ask and answer the questions in pair: What is the function of a ‘chain’? What does the word ‘link’ mean? A chain links things together. You have certainly learnt that ‘to link’ means to connect two or more things or ideas together.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p79-e2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 79, NULL, 'Read the following paragraph and answer the questions that follow: Somen Chanda was born in a village named Baliya in Narsingdi on 24 May, 1920. He was an avid reader from his boyhood and he passed the Entrance Examination in 1936 from Pogose School, Dhaka. Then, he was admitted to Dhaka Mitford Medical School, but he had to discontinue his studies because of ill health. Yet, his pen did not stop. His writings S reflect struggles of the general people. Thus his writings survive him q even today. The words in italics are linking words. What are the functions of these linking words?'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p81-t1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 81, 1, 'Activity: Identify the linking words in the following passage: Bangladesh was in a good team spirit in the world cup cricket tournament 1999. Besides, all the players were in good form. In fact, they proved it in the field. Anyway, they defeated a big team like Pakistan.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p81-t2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 81, 2, 'Activity: Read the following paragraph and make it meaningful by using the linking words given in the box. The first one is done for you: A student needs to have lots of qualities. He should be very studious. He should participate in outdoor games and debating activities. He should be punctual. He should have moral qualities. He should be social. He can be successful if he has these qualities. Linking words: and, firstly, thus, secondly, next, then. A student needs to have lots of qualities. Firstly, he should be very studious.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p81-t3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 81, 3, 'Activity: Fill up the blanks picking up linkers from the box below. The first one is done for you: firstly, secondly, thirdly, fourthly, to begin with, moreover, to conclude, next Several reasons were given for the language movement of the students of this country in 1952. Firstly, they were motivated to establish Bangla as their mother tongue. ______ they were committed to the ideology of Bengali Nationalism. ______ they wanted to raise awareness among the common folks of Bangladesh. ______ they gave ultimatum to the Pakistani rulers. ______ they felt frustrated and guilty in living a carefree life in the eastern part of Pakistan.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t1', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, 4, 'Activity: Rewrite the following paragraph using linking words: Dipak is twelve years old. He does not go to school. His father does not send him to school. He does not believe in education. He considers education to be a wastage of time and energy. Dipak helps his father in the poultry farm. His mother also does not find any interest in sending her son to school for some hours. Dipak is being deprived of primary education.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t2', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Purnava is a student of Jahangirnagar University. Purnava takes part in debate competitions.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t3', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Ukhin Mong is a good teacher. He does not take classes every day.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t4', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: It is raining. Rajib is going to market.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t5', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Bangladesh is a third world country. The Government of Bangladesh distributes books among all the students of primary and secondary schools.'),
  ('class7-english-grammar-en-ch8-p82-t6', 'class7-english-grammar-en', 'class7-english-grammar-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Activity: Join the following sentences with linking words: Kamal was sick. He did not go to school.'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p2-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 2, NULL, 'একক কাজ: স্রষ্টা ও ঈশ্বরের সম্পর্ক ব্যাখ্যা কর।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p4-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 4, NULL, 'একক কাজ: ঈশ্বরের সাকার রূপের দুইটি গুণ চিহ্নিত করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p5-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 5, NULL, 'একক কাজ: ঈশ্বরের একত্ব সম্পর্কে পাঁচটি যুক্তি দাও।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p7-q1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 7, 1, 'ঈশ্বর শব্দের অর্থ কী? ক. জ্ঞান খ. প্রভু গ. স্তুতি ঘ. তপস্যা'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p7-q2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 7, 2, 'ঈশ্বর কী কারণে জীবরূপে পৃথিবীতে অবতরণ করেন? ক. ন্যায় ও সত্য প্রতিষ্ঠা করা খ. নিজেকে প্রকাশ করা গ. সৃষ্টির সমতা বিধান করা ঘ. অসীম ক্ষমতা প্রকাশ করা'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p7-q3', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 7, 3, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড়ো এবং ৩ ও ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: দৃশ্যপট-১ তীর্থদের গ্রামের আশে পাশে প্রতিদিন চুরি বা ডাকাতি হয়। সে মন দিয়ে ঈশ্বরকে তাদের গ্রামে এসে তাদেরকে রক্ষা করার জন্য প্রার্থনা করে। দৃশ্যপট-২ ধর্মপরায়ণ স্পন্দন পড়ালেখার পাশাপাশি প্রতিদিন সকালে একটি বই পাঠ করেন। যেখানে ঈশ্বরের উপাসনার নানান পথ নিয়ে আলোচনা করা হয়েছে। ৩। তীর্থর প্রার্থনায় ঈশ্বর কীভাবে তাদের গ্রামে আসতে পারেন? ক. ব্রহ্মা খ. শ্রীকৃষ্ণ গ. গণেশ ঘ. বিষ্ণু'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, 1, 'সব সাকার রূপ একই ঈশ্বরের ভিন্ন প্রকাশ- ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q1a', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, '১) অনিতা রানী ভক্তিভরে প্রতি বৃহস্পতিবার ঘরে প্রতিষ্ঠিত লক্ষ্মীদেবীর বিগ্রহে পূজা করেন। তার সন্তানেরাও মায়ের সাথে পূজায় অংশ নেয়। অন্যদিকে অনিতাদের প্রতিবেশী শিলারানী প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় বাড়িতে সকলের মঙ্গল কামনা করে সমবেত প্রার্থনার আয়োজন করেন। ক) জীবাত্মা কাকে বলে?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q1b', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, '১) অনিতা রানী ভক্তিভরে প্রতি বৃহস্পতিবার ঘরে প্রতিষ্ঠিত লক্ষ্মীদেবীর বিগ্রহে পূজা করেন। তার সন্তানেরাও মায়ের সাথে পূজায় অংশ নেয়। অন্যদিকে অনিতাদের প্রতিবেশী শিলারানী প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় বাড়িতে সকলের মঙ্গল কামনা করে সমবেত প্রার্থনার আয়োজন করেন। খ) ঈশ্বর কীভাবে জীব-জগৎকে নিয়ন্ত্রণ করছেন- বুঝিয়ে লেখ।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q1c', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, '১) অনিতা রানী ভক্তিভরে প্রতি বৃহস্পতিবার ঘরে প্রতিষ্ঠিত লক্ষ্মীদেবীর বিগ্রহে পূজা করেন। তার সন্তানেরাও মায়ের সাথে পূজায় অংশ নেয়। অন্যদিকে অনিতাদের প্রতিবেশী শিলারানী প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় বাড়িতে সকলের মঙ্গল কামনা করে সমবেত প্রার্থনার আয়োজন করেন। গ) উদ্দীপকের অনিতা রানীর পূজায় ঈশ্বরের কোন রূপটি প্রতিফলিত হয়েছে তা ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q1d', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, '১) অনিতা রানী ভক্তিভরে প্রতি বৃহস্পতিবার ঘরে প্রতিষ্ঠিত লক্ষ্মীদেবীর বিগ্রহে পূজা করেন। তার সন্তানেরাও মায়ের সাথে পূজায় অংশ নেয়। অন্যদিকে অনিতাদের প্রতিবেশী শিলারানী প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় বাড়িতে সকলের মঙ্গল কামনা করে সমবেত প্রার্থনার আয়োজন করেন। ঘ) শিলারানীর প্রার্থনার মাধ্যমে কী ঈশ্বর লাভ সম্ভব- পাঠ্যবইয়ের আলোকে মূল্যায়ন করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, 2, 'পৃথিবীতে ঈশ্বর কেন অবতার রূপে আবির্ভূত হন? ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q3', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, 3, 'ঈশ্বরের স্বরূপ সম্পর্কিত শ্লোকটি অর্থসহ লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch1-p8-q4', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch1', 8, 4, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড়ো এবং ৩ ও ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: দৃশ্যপট-১ তীর্থদের গ্রামের আশে পাশে প্রতিদিন চুরি বা ডাকাতি হয়। সে মন দিয়ে ঈশ্বরকে তাদের গ্রামে এসে তাদেরকে রক্ষা করার জন্য প্রার্থনা করে। দৃশ্যপট-২ ধর্মপরায়ণ স্পন্দন পড়ালেখার পাশাপাশি প্রতিদিন সকালে একটি বই পাঠ করেন। যেখানে ঈশ্বরের উপাসনার নানান পথ নিয়ে আলোচনা করা হয়েছে। ৪। স্পন্দনের পঠিত গ্রন্থটি যে ধর্মগ্রন্থকে নির্দেশ করে তার অন্তর্নিহিত বিষয় হচ্ছে - i. ঈশ্বরের সৃষ্টি করার অসীম ক্ষমতা রয়েছে ii. বিভিন্ন রূপের মাধ্যমে ঈশ্বরের শক্তির প্রকাশ ঘটে iii. ঈশ্বর কেবল পূজা করলেই তুষ্ট হন নিচের কোনটি সঠিক? ক. i ও ii খ. ii ও iii গ. i ও iii ঘ. i, ii, ও iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p10-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 10, NULL, 'একক কাজ: তোমার জানা একজন ব্যক্তির জীবসেবামূলক কর্মকাণ্ড বর্ণনা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p12-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 12, NULL, 'একক কাজ: কর্মবাদ ধারণাটি কয়েকটি উদাহরণ দিয়ে বুঝিয়ে লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p12-t2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 12, NULL, 'একক কাজ: মোক্ষলাভের কয়েকটি উপায়ের ক্ষেত্র উল্লেখ কর'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p14-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 14, NULL, 'একক কাজ: জন্মান্তরে কর্মফল ভোগের ধর্মীয় উপাখ্যানের শিক্ষা তোমার জীবনে কীভাবে প্রতিফলিত হবে।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p15-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 15, NULL, 'দলীয় কাজ: নারীকে কীভাবে যথাযোগ্য মর্যাদায় ভূষিত করা যেতে পারে তার কয়েকটি উপায় লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p16-q1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 16, 1, 'কোন দেবতাকে দেবরাজ বলা হয়? ক) ইন্দ্র খ) শিব গ) বিষ্ণু ঘ) ব্রহ্মা'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p16-q2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 16, 2, 'পুরাণ পাঠ করার মাধ্যমে- i) জীব জগতের উৎপত্তি সম্পর্কে জানা যায় ii) দেবী মহামায়ার উদ্ভব সম্পর্কে জানা যায় iii) হিন্দু ধর্মের ঐতিহাসিক জীবন সম্পর্কে জানা যায় নিচের কোনটি সঠিক? ক) i ও ii খ) i ও iii গ) ii ও iii ঘ) i, ii ও iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p16-q3', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 16, 3, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড় ৩ ও ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: সৌমি প্রতিদিন একটা ধর্মবই পাঠ করে যার মাধ্যমে সে বিভিন্ন দেবদেবী কীভাবে উদ্ভব হয়েছে এবং তাঁদের গুণাবলী সম্পর্কে জানতে পারে। কিন্তু তার বাবা রতন বাবু প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় জোরে জোরে একটা গ্রন্থ পড়েন যার মাধ্যমে সে অনেক মুনি ঋষি ও তাদের বসবাসের স্থান সম্পর্কে জেনে গেছে। ৩) সৌমি কোন ধর্মগ্রন্থটি পাঠ করতো? ক) শ্রীমদ্ভগবদ্গীতা খ) শ্রীশ্রী চণ্ডী গ) পুরাণ ঘ) উপনিষদ'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-q1a', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'তথ্য-১ সূর্যনগর গ্রামের পাশ দিয়ে বয়ে যাওয়া নদীর মাঝখানে চর জেগেছে। পলাশ বাবার সাথে ঘুরতে গিয়ে এটা নিয়ে বাবাকে প্রশ্ন করে, বাবা জানান একসময় ওখানে গ্রাম ছিল, নদীর মাঝে তলিয়ে গিয়েছিল, এখন আবার জেগে উঠেছে। তথ্য-২ সঞ্জয় দুর্ধর্ষ ও নিষ্ঠুর প্রকৃতির। সে অশ্লীল রেগে যায় এবং সবার সঙ্গে দুর্ব্যবহার করেন জোর-জবরদস্তি করে অন্যের সম্পদ দখল করা তার নিত্যদিনকার কাজ। সে এলাকার অনেককেই ঘর ছাড়া করেছে। ক. পুরাণ কাকে বলে?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-q1b', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'তথ্য-১ সূর্যনগর গ্রামের পাশ দিয়ে বয়ে যাওয়া নদীর মাঝখানে চর জেগেছে। পলাশ বাবার সাথে ঘুরতে গিয়ে এটা নিয়ে বাবাকে প্রশ্ন করে, বাবা জানান একসময় ওখানে গ্রাম ছিল, নদীর মাঝে তলিয়ে গিয়েছিল, এখন আবার জেগে উঠেছে। তথ্য-২ সঞ্জয় দুর্ধর্ষ ও নিষ্ঠুর প্রকৃতির। সে অশ্লীল রেগে যায় এবং সবার সঙ্গে দুর্ব্যবহার করেন জোর-জবরদস্তি করে অন্যের সম্পদ দখল করা তার নিত্যদিনকার কাজ। সে এলাকার অনেককেই ঘর ছাড়া করেছে। খ. দেবী মহামায়া অস্থিকার রূপ কেন ধারণ করেছিলেন?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-q1c', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'তথ্য-১ সূর্যনগর গ্রামের পাশ দিয়ে বয়ে যাওয়া নদীর মাঝখানে চর জেগেছে। পলাশ বাবার সাথে ঘুরতে গিয়ে এটা নিয়ে বাবাকে প্রশ্ন করে, বাবা জানান একসময় ওখানে গ্রাম ছিল, নদীর মাঝে তলিয়ে গিয়েছিল, এখন আবার জেগে উঠেছে। তথ্য-২ সঞ্জয় দুর্ধর্ষ ও নিষ্ঠুর প্রকৃতির। সে অশ্লীল রেগে যায় এবং সবার সঙ্গে দুর্ব্যবহার করেন জোর-জবরদস্তি করে অন্যের সম্পদ দখল করা তার নিত্যদিনকার কাজ। সে এলাকার অনেককেই ঘর ছাড়া করেছে। গ. তথ্য-১ এর ঘটনার সাথে পুরাণের কোন বৈশিষ্ট্যের মিল রয়েছে? -ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-q1d', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'তথ্য-১ সূর্যনগর গ্রামের পাশ দিয়ে বয়ে যাওয়া নদীর মাঝখানে চর জেগেছে। পলাশ বাবার সাথে ঘুরতে গিয়ে এটা নিয়ে বাবাকে প্রশ্ন করে, বাবা জানান একসময় ওখানে গ্রাম ছিল, নদীর মাঝে তলিয়ে গিয়েছিল, এখন আবার জেগে উঠেছে। তথ্য-২ সঞ্জয় দুর্ধর্ষ ও নিষ্ঠুর প্রকৃতির। সে অশ্লীল রেগে যায় এবং সবার সঙ্গে দুর্ব্যবহার করেন জোর-জবরদস্তি করে অন্যের সম্পদ দখল করা তার নিত্যদিনকার কাজ। সে এলাকার অনেককেই ঘর ছাড়া করেছে। ঘ. তথ্য-২ এর সঞ্জয়ের আচরণ তোমার পাঠ্যবইয়ের যে চরিত্রের প্রতিনিধিত্ব করে ধর্মগ্রন্থের আলোকে তার গুরুত্ব মূল্যায়ন করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-q4', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, 4, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড় ৩ ও ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: সৌমি প্রতিদিন একটা ধর্মবই পাঠ করে যার মাধ্যমে সে বিভিন্ন দেবদেবী কীভাবে উদ্ভব হয়েছে এবং তাঁদের গুণাবলী সম্পর্কে জানতে পারে। কিন্তু তার বাবা রতন বাবু প্রতিদিন সন্ধ্যায় জোরে জোরে একটা গ্রন্থ পড়েন যার মাধ্যমে সে অনেক মুনি ঋষি ও তাদের বসবাসের স্থান সম্পর্কে জেনে গেছে। ৪। রতন বাবুর পঠিত গ্রন্থের মাহাত্ম্য হলো- i) এতে গল্পের মাধ্যমে নীতি শিক্ষা প্রদান করা হয়েছে ii) এর মাধ্যমে সৃষ্টির আদি পুরুষ সম্পর্কে জানা যায় iii) এতে প্রায় সাতশত মন্ত্র আছে নিচের কোনটি সঠিক? ক) i ও ii খ) ii ও iii গ) i ও iii ঘ) i, ii ও iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-qক', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'দেবী মাহাত্ম্য কোন পুরাণের অন্তর্ভুক্ত সে সম্পর্কে লিখো'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-qখ', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'দেবী দুর্গার প্রণাম মন্ত্রটি অর্থসহ লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch2-p17-qগ', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch2', 17, NULL, 'দেবী দুর্গাকে দুর্গতিনাশিনী বলা হয় কেন?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p19-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 19, NULL, 'একক কাজ: পুরাণসমূহের নাম লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p19-t2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 19, NULL, 'একক কাজ: পুরাণের বিষয়বস্তুসমূহ চিহ্নিত করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p20-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 20, NULL, 'একক কাজ: পুরাণের শিক্ষার মাধ্যমে জীবনকে সুন্দরভাবে গড়ে তুলতে কী কী পদক্ষেপ নেবে?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p20-t2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 20, NULL, 'দলীয় কাজ: শ্রীশ্রীচণ্ডীর কয়েকটি বৈশিষ্ট্য লেখো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p22-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 22, NULL, 'একক কাজ: রাজা সুরথ এবং সমাধি বৈশ্য যে কারণে ঘর ছেড়েছেন সে কারণগুলো চিহ্নিত করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p22-t2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 22, NULL, 'একক কাজ: মহিষাসুর বধ কাহিনির শিক্ষা চিহ্নিত করে তোমার প্রাত্যহিক জীবনে তার প্রভাব বর্ণনা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p23-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 23, NULL, 'দলীয় কাজ: কালিকা বা অম্বিকার হাতে নিহত অসুরদের একটি তালিকা তৈরি করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p24-q1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 24, 1, 'কর্মফল ভোগের জন্য পুনরায় জন্মগ্রহণ করাকে কী বলে? ক) মোক্ষলাভ খ) কর্মবাদ গ) জন্মান্তর ঘ) ধর্মকৃত্য'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p24-t1', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 24, NULL, 'দলীয় কাজ: ''শ্রীশ্রীচণ্ডীর শিক্ষাই ব্যক্তির অসুরশক্তিকে বিনাশ করতে পারে।'' উদাহরণসহ যুক্তি দাও।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p25-q2', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 25, 2, 'মোক্ষলাভের অন্যতম উপায় হতে পারে- ক) দেব-দেবীকে সবসময় ভক্তি করা খ) নিজের কল্যাণ চিন্তা করে কাজ করা গ) কোন আশা না করে কর্ম করা ঘ) ভক্তিপূর্ণ মনে সাধনা করা'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p25-q3', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 25, 3, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড়ো ৩ এবং ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: সৌমিরানি চাকরির পাশাপাশি সংসারের যাবতীয় দায়িত্ব পালন করেন। তিনি ভীষণভাবে পাপ কাজের ভয় পান। তার ধর্মপরায়ণ স্বামী নারায়ণ বাবুও বাড়ির প্রতিটা অনুষ্ঠানের পর যজ্ঞের সাথে অতিথিদের সেবা করান। মাঝে মাঝে তিনি পরিবারের অন্য সদস্যদের সাথে নিয়ে তীর্থ ভ্রমণেও যান। ৩) সৌমিরানির মাঝে কোন বিষয়টির প্রতিফলন ঘটেছে? ক) মোক্ষলাভ খ) কর্মবাদ গ) জন্মান্তর ঘ) ধর্মকৃত্য'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p25-q4', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 25, 4, 'নিচের উদ্দীপকটি পড়ো ৩ এবং ৪ নম্বর প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও: সৌমিরানি চাকরির পাশাপাশি সংসারের যাবতীয় দায়িত্ব পালন করেন। তিনি ভীষণভাবে পাপ কাজের ভয় পান। তার ধর্মপরায়ণ স্বামী নারায়ণ বাবুও বাড়ির প্রতিটা অনুষ্ঠানের পর যজ্ঞের সাথে অতিথিদের সেবা করান। মাঝে মাঝে তিনি পরিবারের অন্য সদস্যদের সাথে নিয়ে তীর্থ ভ্রমণেও যান। ৪) নারায়ণবাবুর মধ্যে হিন্দুধর্মের যে বৈশিষ্ট্য পরিলক্ষিত হয় তার মাধ্যমে- i) জীব ও জগতের কল্যাণ ঘটে ii) আত্মসম্মান বৃদ্ধি পায় iii) হিন্দু ধর্মের স্বরূপ প্রকাশ পায় নিচের কোনটি সঠিক? ক) i ও ii খ) ii ও iii গ) i ও iii ঘ) i, ii, ও iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-q1a', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, 'অধীর বাবুর দুই মেয়েকেই তিনি লেখাপড়া শিখিয়েছেন। মেয়েদের যে কোনো ইচ্ছাকে তিনি গুরুত্বের সাথে বিবেচনা করেন। বড় মেয়েকে বিয়ে দেওয়ার সময় টাকা পয়সা নয় বরং যে পরিবার মেয়েদের শ্রদ্ধা করে এমন পরিবার বেছে নেন। তিনি আত্মীয়-স্বজন সকলের বিপদে এগিয়ে যান। তিনি আর্থিকভাবে বিভিন্ন দরিদ্র পরিবারকে বিভিন্ন সময় সহায়তা করেন। সব কাজকে তিনি ঈশ্বরের মনে করে সকলের পাশে দাঁড়ান। এ কাজের জন্য তিনি কোনো কিছু প্রত্যাশা করেন না। ক. ভগবান কাকে বলে?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-q1b', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, 'অধীর বাবুর দুই মেয়েকেই তিনি লেখাপড়া শিখিয়েছেন। মেয়েদের যে কোনো ইচ্ছাকে তিনি গুরুত্বের সাথে বিবেচনা করেন। বড় মেয়েকে বিয়ে দেওয়ার সময় টাকা পয়সা নয় বরং যে পরিবার মেয়েদের শ্রদ্ধা করে এমন পরিবার বেছে নেন। তিনি আত্মীয়-স্বজন সকলের বিপদে এগিয়ে যান। তিনি আর্থিকভাবে বিভিন্ন দরিদ্র পরিবারকে বিভিন্ন সময় সহায়তা করেন। সব কাজকে তিনি ঈশ্বরের মনে করে সকলের পাশে দাঁড়ান। এ কাজের জন্য তিনি কোনো কিছু প্রত্যাশা করেন না। খ. ধর্মকৃত্যের মধ্য দিয়ে কী প্রকাশ পায় তা ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-q1c', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, 'অধীর বাবুর দুই মেয়েকেই তিনি লেখাপড়া শিখিয়েছেন। মেয়েদের যে কোনো ইচ্ছাকে তিনি গুরুত্বের সাথে বিবেচনা করেন। বড় মেয়েকে বিয়ে দেওয়ার সময় টাকা পয়সা নয় বরং যে পরিবার মেয়েদের শ্রদ্ধা করে এমন পরিবার বেছে নেন। তিনি আত্মীয়-স্বজন সকলের বিপদে এগিয়ে যান। তিনি আর্থিকভাবে বিভিন্ন দরিদ্র পরিবারকে বিভিন্ন সময় সহায়তা করেন। সব কাজকে তিনি ঈশ্বরের মনে করে সকলের পাশে দাঁড়ান। এ কাজের জন্য তিনি কোনো কিছু প্রত্যাশা করেন না। গ. মেয়েদের প্রতি অধীরবাবুর আচরণে হিন্দুধর্ম বিশ্বাসের যে দিকটি প্রতিফলিত হয়েছে, তা ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-q1d', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, 'অধীর বাবুর দুই মেয়েকেই তিনি লেখাপড়া শিখিয়েছেন। মেয়েদের যে কোনো ইচ্ছাকে তিনি গুরুত্বের সাথে বিবেচনা করেন। বড় মেয়েকে বিয়ে দেওয়ার সময় টাকা পয়সা নয় বরং যে পরিবার মেয়েদের শ্রদ্ধা করে এমন পরিবার বেছে নেন। তিনি আত্মীয়-স্বজন সকলের বিপদে এগিয়ে যান। তিনি আর্থিকভাবে বিভিন্ন দরিদ্র পরিবারকে বিভিন্ন সময় সহায়তা করেন। সব কাজকে তিনি ঈশ্বরের মনে করে সকলের পাশে দাঁড়ান। এ কাজের জন্য তিনি কোনো কিছু প্রত্যাশা করেন না। ঘ. আত্মীয় স্বজনের প্রতি অধীর বাবুর আচরণের মাধ্যমে কী চিরমুক্তি সম্ভব - পাঠ্যবইয়ের আলোকে মূল্যায়ন করো।'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-qক', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, 'ভরত মুনিকে হরিণরূপে জন্মগ্রহণ করতে হয়েছিল কেন?'),
  ('class7-hindu-bn-ch3-p26-qখ', 'class7-hindu-bn', 'class7-hindu-bn-ch3', 26, NULL, '''আত্মমোক্ষায় জগদ্ধিতায় চ'' - কথাটি বলতে কী বুঝায়?'),
