  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p26-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 26, NULL, 'Individual work: Describe the inference of the teaching of the killing of Mahishasur in your daily life.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p27-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 27, NULL, 'Individual work: Make a list of dead demons who were killed by Kalika and Ambika.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p28-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 28, NULL, 'Group work: "The teachings of Sri Sri Chandi can destroy an individual''s demonism"- explain reasons with examples.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p29-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 29, 1, 'What is rebirth for the purpose of enjoying the results of one''s actions called? a) Moksha b) Karma c) Reincarnation d) Religious practices'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p29-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 29, 2, 'One of the ways to attain salvation can be- a) Always worship God and Goddess b) Work thinking about one''s own welfare c) Work without any expectations c) Practice with a devotional mind'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p29-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 29, 3, 'Read the stimulus below and answer questions 3 and 4: Along with her job, Soumi Rani performs all the responsibilities of the family. She is terribly afraid of committing sins. Her pious husband Narayan Babu also serves the guests with care after every ceremony at home. Sometimes, he also goes on pilgrimages with other family members. 3) Which thing is reflected in Soumi Rani? a) Mokshalabh b) Karma c) Jamantar d) Dharma kritya'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p29-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 29, 4, 'Read the stimulus below and answer questions 3 and 4: Along with her job, Soumi Rani performs all the responsibilities of the family. She is terribly afraid of committing sins. Her pious husband Narayan Babu also serves the guests with care after every ceremony at home. Sometimes, he also goes on pilgrimages with other family members. 4) Through the characteristics of Hinduism observed in Narayan Babu- i) Welfare of living beings and the world occurs ii) Self-respect increases iii) The nature of Hinduism is revealed Which of the following is correct? A. i and ii B. ii and iii C. i and iii D. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Mr. Adhir has educated both of his daughters. He considers any wish of the daughters seriously. While giving the eldest daughter in marriage, he does not choose money but a family that respects girls. He goes ahead in the trouble of all his relatives. He helps various poor families financially at different times. He considers all the work as God and stands by everyone. He does not expect anything for this work. A. What is God?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Mr. Adhir has educated both of his daughters. He considers any wish of the daughters seriously. While giving the eldest daughter in marriage, he does not choose money but a family that respects girls. He goes ahead in the trouble of all his relatives. He helps various poor families financially at different times. He considers all the work as God and stands by everyone. He does not expect anything for this work. B. Explain what is revealed through religious rituals.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Mr. Adhir has educated both of his daughters. He considers any wish of the daughters seriously. While giving the eldest daughter in marriage, he does not choose money but a family that respects girls. He goes ahead in the trouble of all his relatives. He helps various poor families financially at different times. He considers all the work as God and stands by everyone. He does not expect anything for this work. C. Explain the aspect of Hinduism reflected in Adhir Babu''s behavior towards women.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Mr. Adhir has educated both of his daughters. He considers any wish of the daughters seriously. While giving the eldest daughter in marriage, he does not choose money but a family that respects girls. He goes ahead in the trouble of all his relatives. He helps various poor families financially at different times. He considers all the work as God and stands by everyone. He does not expect anything for this work. D. Is eternal liberation possible through Adhir Babu''s behavior towards his relatives - evaluate in the light of the textbook.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-qa', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Why did Bharat Muni have to be born as a deer?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-qb', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'What does it mean to say that atmoksha is jagaddhita?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch3-p30-qc', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch3', 30, NULL, 'Why do people have to be reborn?'),
