  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p35-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 35, NULL, 'Individual work: Demonstrate Shalvasana.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p35-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 35, NULL, 'Individual work: Make a poster on the usefulness of Shalvasana.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p36-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 36, NULL, 'Individual work: Practice and show the Pashchimottanasan doing exercise.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p36-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 36, NULL, 'Individual work: Make a list of benefits for the exercise of Pashchimottanasana.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p37-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 37, 1, 'Afternoon activities rituals are which category of daily activities? a) Third b) Fourth c) Fifth d) Sixth'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p37-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 37, 2, 'In the third category of daily activities- i. The body has to be rested ii. The body has to be exercised with attention iii. When someone comes home, he has to be fed Which of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. ii and iii c. i and iii d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p37-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 37, 3, 'Read the following stimulus and answer questions 3 and 4: Rama worships the idol installed in the house in the morning before going to school and starts the day with other activities. Rama has to walk to school. It was seen that he was hunched while walking. When the teacher noticed it, he asked Rama to practice an asana. As a result, Rama''s problem was solved. 3) Uddipkar''s Rama''s daily routine includes which stage of daily routine? a) Breakfast b) Morning c) Afternoon d) Evening'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p37-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 37, 4, 'Read the following stimulus and answer questions 3 and 4: Rama worships the idol installed in the house in the morning before going to school and starts the day with other activities. Rama has to walk to school. It was seen that he was hunched while walking. When the teacher noticed it, he asked Rama to practice an asana. As a result, Rama''s problem was solved. 4) Rama''s other benefits that can be obtained as a result of the asanas prescribed by the teacher are- i) Constipation will be relieved ii) The structure of the waist muscles will be beautiful iii) Restlessness of mind will be relieved Which of the following is correct? A. i and ii b. ii and iii c. i and iii d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p38-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 38, NULL, 'Sujan is skinny and obese. As a result, she cannot do all the tasks easily. Seeing such a condition, Sujan''s mother became worried and when she remembered the doctor, the doctor asked her to practice an asana. On the other hand, Sujan''s friend Shyamal wakes up early in the morning and starts the day by reciting mantras. He does his work, eats and drinks properly. Takes care of his body and recites mantras before going to bed. a) What is daily routine?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p38-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 38, NULL, 'Sujan is skinny and obese. As a result, she cannot do all the tasks easily. Seeing such a condition, Sujan''s mother became worried and when she remembered the doctor, the doctor asked her to practice an asana. On the other hand, Sujan''s friend Shyamal wakes up early in the morning and starts the day by reciting mantras. He does his work, eats and drinks properly. Takes care of his body and recites mantras before going to bed. b) Who is served when serving a guest? Explain.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p38-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 38, NULL, 'Sujan is skinny and obese. As a result, she cannot do all the tasks easily. Seeing such a condition, Sujan''s mother became worried and when she remembered the doctor, the doctor asked her to practice an asana. On the other hand, Sujan''s friend Shyamal wakes up early in the morning and starts the day by reciting mantras. He does his work, eats and drinks properly. Takes care of his body and recites mantras before going to bed. c) Which asana did the doctor tell Uddipkar Sujan to practice? Explain.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p38-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 38, NULL, 'Sujan is skinny and obese. As a result, she cannot do all the tasks easily. Seeing such a condition, Sujan''s mother became worried and when she remembered the doctor, the doctor asked her to practice an asana. On the other hand, Sujan''s friend Shyamal wakes up early in the morning and starts the day by reciting mantras. He does his work, eats and drinks properly. Takes care of his body and recites mantras before going to bed. d) Analyze whether Shyamal is able to follow the rules of Hinduism through his daily activities in the light of the textbook.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch4-p38-qa', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch4', 38, NULL, 'How do you practice Paschimottanasana? Explain.'),
