  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p46-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 46, 1, 'Which is a part of Panchopachar? a) Vandana b) Asana c) Madhuparka d) Puspa'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p46-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 46, 2, 'Why is an oath taken in worship? a) To remember Vishnu b) To purify all the upchars c) To worship according to the rules d) To pray to the desired deity'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p46-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 46, 4, 'Read the following prompt and answer questions 3 and 4: A special puja is organized in the house of the devotees on the full moon day of Ashwini. Before the puja starts, the priest Thakur removes all the defects. The devotees also fast with their mother, offer alms at home and collect various upchars for the puja. For example - five types of grains. A joyful atmosphere is created in their house on the occasion of this puja. 4) What can be called the work of the priest Thakur? a) Sankalpa b) Atma-Sarpan c) Achaman d) Pran Pratthi'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p46-q5', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 46, 5, 'Read the following prompt and answer questions 3 and 4: A special puja is organized in the house of the devotees on the full moon day of Ashwini. Before the puja starts, the priest Thakur removes all the defects. The devotees also fast with their mother, offer alms at home and collect various upchars for the puja. For example - five types of grains. A joyful atmosphere is created in their house on the occasion of this puja. 5) Through the puja held at home, the devotees - i) Wealth will increase ii) Knowledge of folk art will develop iii) Flexibility in nature will increase Which of the following is correct? a) i and ii b) ii and iii c) i and iii d) i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Scenario-1 Avni Babu is a blacksmith by profession. Every year, he worships the deity with utmost devotion in various ways to gain skill in this profession and to gain grace. In this puja, he keeps the materials used in his profession near the deity''s idol. He thinks that it is not possible to succeed in his profession unless he can gain the grace of the deity. Scenario-2 [Picture: colour image of Goddess Lakshmi - crowned four-armed goddess, holding lotus buds in two hands and a golden pot, wearing a pink-blue sari, against an orange-red background] a) What is the basis of worship?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Scenario-1 Avni Babu is a blacksmith by profession. Every year, he worships the deity with utmost devotion in various ways to gain skill in this profession and to gain grace. In this puja, he keeps the materials used in his profession near the deity''s idol. He thinks that it is not possible to succeed in his profession unless he can gain the grace of the deity. Scenario-2 [Picture: colour image of Goddess Lakshmi - crowned four-armed goddess, holding lotus buds in two hands and a golden pot, wearing a pink-blue sari, against an orange-red background] b) What is the act of cleaning everything with water during worship? Explain and write.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Scenario-1 Avni Babu is a blacksmith by profession. Every year, he worships the deity with utmost devotion in various ways to gain skill in this profession and to gain grace. In this puja, he keeps the materials used in his profession near the deity''s idol. He thinks that it is not possible to succeed in his profession unless he can gain the grace of the deity. Scenario-2 [Picture: colour image of Goddess Lakshmi - crowned four-armed goddess, holding lotus buds in two hands and a golden pot, wearing a pink-blue sari, against an orange-red background] c) Scenario-1 Describe the method of worship of the deity that Avani Babu worships.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Scenario-1 Avni Babu is a blacksmith by profession. Every year, he worships the deity with utmost devotion in various ways to gain skill in this profession and to gain grace. In this puja, he keeps the materials used in his profession near the deity''s idol. He thinks that it is not possible to succeed in his profession unless he can gain the grace of the deity. Scenario-2 [Picture: colour image of Goddess Lakshmi - crowned four-armed goddess, holding lotus buds in two hands and a golden pot, wearing a pink-blue sari, against an orange-red background] d) Analyze the teachings and effects of the worship of the goddess mentioned in the picture indicated in Scenario-2 in the light of the textbook.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-qa', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'Why are the rules of worship followed?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch5-p47-qb', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch5', 47, NULL, 'How should one approach the worship? Explain.'),
