  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p54-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 54, NULL, 'Individual work: Name a self denying person you know and narrate an incident of his sacrifice.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p56-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 56, 1, 'In which era did Vishnu himself appear as Shri Ram? a) In Satya Yuga b) In Treta Yuga c) In Dwapara Yuga d) In Kali Yuga'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p56-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 56, 2, 'The lesson of Aruni''s story is- a. Not telling lies b. Fulfilling responsibilities towards everyone c. Giving up one''s own interests d. Not being greedy'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p56-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 56, 3, 'Read the stimulus below and answer questions 3 and 4: Robin Sarkar is a successful businessman. He has a beautiful shop in Kali Bazar. All the businessmen know him by one name. Because he does not compromise on business rules. His son Nirmal is very greedy and calm in nature. He does not pledge to his father after seeing the good clothes of his friends. He can easily give away any thing of his choice to others. 3. Which moral quality is noticeable in the character of Robin Sarkar in Uddip? a) Honesty b) Duty c) Altruism d) Sacrifice-Titiksha'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Despite working for a low salary, Nilratanbabu was living a happy family life. Although his family was poor, he lived with his father, mother and younger brothers. He took care of everyone''s needs and met their needs as much as he could. Although he had been married for several years, he did not have any children. The doctor says that there is no possibility of their having a child. There is a feeling of despair between the two of them. The house servant Dinanath notices the matter. He is poor. He has three children. Dinanath convinces his wife and hands over one of his children to Manorama. Peace returns to Manorama''s family. A. What is honesty?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Despite working for a low salary, Nilratanbabu was living a happy family life. Although his family was poor, he lived with his father, mother and younger brothers. He took care of everyone''s needs and met their needs as much as he could. Although he had been married for several years, he did not have any children. The doctor says that there is no possibility of their having a child. There is a feeling of despair between the two of them. The house servant Dinanath notices the matter. He is poor. He has three children. Dinanath convinces his wife and hands over one of his children to Manorama. Peace returns to Manorama''s family. B. Which moral quality is included in fulfilling one''s duties towards parents? Explain.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Despite working for a low salary, Nilratanbabu was living a happy family life. Although his family was poor, he lived with his father, mother and younger brothers. He took care of everyone''s needs and met their needs as much as he could. Although he had been married for several years, he did not have any children. The doctor says that there is no possibility of their having a child. There is a feeling of despair between the two of them. The house servant Dinanath notices the matter. He is poor. He has three children. Dinanath convinces his wife and hands over one of his children to Manorama. Peace returns to Manorama''s family. C. Explain which moral quality is reflected in the character traits of Nilratan Babu.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Despite working for a low salary, Nilratanbabu was living a happy family life. Although his family was poor, he lived with his father, mother and younger brothers. He took care of everyone''s needs and met their needs as much as he could. Although he had been married for several years, he did not have any children. The doctor says that there is no possibility of their having a child. There is a feeling of despair between the two of them. The house servant Dinanath notices the matter. He is poor. He has three children. Dinanath convinces his wife and hands over one of his children to Manorama. Peace returns to Manorama''s family. D. Evaluate the ideal of the quality observed in Dinanath in the light of the anecdote read in your textbook.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, 4, 'Read the stimulus below and answer questions 3 and 4: Robin Sarkar is a successful businessman. He has a beautiful shop in Kali Bazar. All the businessmen know him by one name. Because he does not compromise on business rules. His son Nirmal is very greedy and calm in nature. He does not pledge to his father after seeing the good clothes of his friends. He can easily give away any thing of his choice to others. 4. The moral quality that is observed in Nirmal''s behavior is included in the anecdotes in the textbook: i. Aruni went to the field to tie Al. ii. Sitadevi went to the forest with her husband. iii. Bharat came to take his uncle back home. Which of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. ii and iii c. i and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-qB', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'What are the benefits of living an honest life?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-qC', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Explain the part of duty in religion.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch6-p57-qa', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch6', 57, NULL, 'Why is sacrificing one''s own interests important in religion?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p59-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 59, NULL, 'Individual work: Why did Sri Krishna kill Batsasur and Bokasur?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p60-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 60, NULL, 'Individual work: How did the poisonous water of Kalindi become drinkable?'),
