  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p64-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 64, NULL, 'Individual work: a. Identify the areas of moral lessons from the ideal life of Sri Chaitanya Dev.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p64-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 64, NULL, 'Individual work: b. Narrate the influence of Sri Chaitanya Dev on social life.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p64-t3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 64, NULL, 'Group work: How will you apply the lessons you learn from Chaitanya Dev?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p66-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 66, NULL, 'Individual work: Why did Zamindar Durgacharan honour Rama prasad?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p67-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 67, NULL, 'Individual work: Identify the incidents and teachings from the life of Rama Prasad.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p67-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 67, NULL, 'Individual work: Write about the childhood of Sarada Devi.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p68-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 68, NULL, 'Group work: Mention how did Sarada Devi become Shreema.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p69-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 69, NULL, 'Group work: Identify the main happenings of Sarada Devi and their lessons.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p70-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 70, NULL, 'Individual work: How did Biley show honesty and fearlessness.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p71-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 71, NULL, 'Group work: Which steps did Vivekananda advocate for the development of the country?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p72-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 72, NULL, 'Individual work: How did Vivekananda become best speaker at the conference of World''s Religions?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p74-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 74, NULL, 'Group work: Identify the lessons of Vivakananda''s life.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p76-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 76, NULL, 'Individual Work: Describe the role of Jagadbandhu in changing the society?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p76-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 76, NULL, 'Individual work: How will you apply the lessons you gain from the life of Prabhu Jagadbandhu?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p76-t3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 76, NULL, 'Group work: Write ten sentences about a great man or woman of your acquaintances.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p77-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 77, 1, 'Who used to practice Kali''s sadhana in Brahmajnana? A. Sri Chaitanya B. Prabhu Jagadbandhu C. Swami Vivekananda D. Sadhak Ramprasad'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p77-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 77, 2, 'What is the ideal of Prabhu Jagadbandhu''s life? A. Killing bad people and protecting good people B. Without renunciation, nothing great can be achieved C. One cannot be arrogant for knowledge D. Unnecessary enthusiasm for others is not good'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, NULL, 'Scenario-1 In addition to teaching, Animesh Babu also writes books for the worldly and spiritual development of people. He is generous, so he married his children in other castes. Moreover, he always thinks about the welfare of people and society. Scene-2 Being at the feet of his mother He does not rise up- A. What is a great man?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, NULL, 'Scenario-1 In addition to teaching, Animesh Babu also writes books for the worldly and spiritual development of people. He is generous, so he married his children in other castes. Moreover, he always thinks about the welfare of people and society. Scene-2 Being at the feet of his mother He does not rise up- B. Everyone is very happy with this speech of Vivekananda - which speech is being talked about here? Describe.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, NULL, 'Scenario-1 In addition to teaching, Animesh Babu also writes books for the worldly and spiritual development of people. He is generous, so he married his children in other castes. Moreover, he always thinks about the welfare of people and society. Scene-2 Being at the feet of his mother He does not rise up- C. Explain which great man''s ideals are reflected in Animesh Babu in incident-1.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, NULL, 'Scenario-1 In addition to teaching, Animesh Babu also writes books for the worldly and spiritual development of people. He is generous, so he married his children in other castes. Moreover, he always thinks about the welfare of people and society. Scene-2 Being at the feet of his mother He does not rise up- D. Evaluate the song of incident-2 in the light of the ideal life and character of the great man whose song is similar to the song written by him.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, 3, 'Read the following stimulus and answer questions 3 and 4: Story-1 In the village of Lakshpipur, a large snake was spotted in a pond. Out of fear of the snake, no one dared to go near the pond for any work. Upon hearing the news, a snake charmer arrived and killed the snake, saving the villagers. Story-2 After Ratna Rani''s marriage, her husband mostly stays at his workplace, while she spends her time at her parental home engaged in religious activities. Her devout husband visits her parental home only after a long time, and that''s when they meet. Whenever they do, he advises Ratna Rani to stay on the path of God. 3. Which incident of the ideal life story can be seen in the activity of the snake in incident-1? a. Killing of Bakasura b. Holding Govardhan c. Defeating Kaliya d. Sarveswari Devi'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p78-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 78, 4, 'Read the following stimulus and answer questions 3 and 4: Story-1 In the village of Lakshpipur, a large snake was spotted in a pond. Out of fear of the snake, no one dared to go near the pond for any work. Upon hearing the news, a snake charmer arrived and killed the snake, saving the villagers. Story-2 After Ratna Rani''s marriage, her husband mostly stays at his workplace, while she spends her time at her parental home engaged in religious activities. Her devout husband visits her parental home only after a long time, and that''s when they meet. Whenever they do, he advises Ratna Rani to stay on the path of God. 4. The lesson of the ideal life story that is similar to incident-2 in real life is- i. Sadhana and bhajan should be done at an early age ii. One should work without greed towards the world iii. Finding someone''s fault does not bring peace Which of the following is correct? a) i and ii b) ii and iii c) i and iii d) i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p79-qA', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 79, NULL, 'How did Beel show honesty?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p79-qB', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 79, NULL, 'How did Keshav Mishra''s arrogance fall? Explain.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p79-qC', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 79, NULL, 'How can we put the teachings of Sarada Devi into practice?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p79-qD', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 79, NULL, 'How did Vatsasur try to kill Sri Krishna?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch7-p79-qD-2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch7', 79, NULL, 'Why did the cowherds leave Gokul and go to Vrindavan?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p81-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 81, NULL, 'Individual work: Explain the relation between religion and moral education with four examples.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p82-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 82, NULL, 'Individual work: Identify two liberal persons of your society and narrate their qualities.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p83-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 83, NULL, 'Group work: Identify five examples of charity and write about their impacts.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p84-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 84, NULL, 'Individual work: Identify four areas to show courage and then write your roles in those places.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p85-t1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 85, NULL, 'Individual work: Identify five areas to practice tolerance.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p85-t2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 85, NULL, 'Individual work: Give arguments in favour of the statement—open-mindedness, charity, courage flourishes human character.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p87-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 87, 1, 'What is the act of working for others without any expectations? A. Altruism B. Generosity C. Truthfulness D. Duty'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p87-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 87, 2, 'What is meant by courage? A. Working with the recognition of others'' opinions B. Serving someone with love C. Working without expecting benefits D. Standing up for injustice'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p87-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 87, 3, 'Read the following prompt and answer questions 3 and 4: On any festival day, Sadhan Chandra invites people from all walks of life to lunch and he also eats with them. His wife Sulekhadevi is also very determined, always giving importance to the opinions of others when doing any work. The neighbors are impressed by their behavior and are inspired to practice it. 3. What moral values are revealed in Sadhan Chandra''s behavior? A. Forgiveness B. Courage C. Generosity D. Philanthropy'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p87-q4', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 87, 4, 'Read the following prompt and answer questions 3 and 4: On any festival day, Sadhan Chandra invites people from all walks of life to lunch and he also eats with them. His wife Sulekhadevi is also very determined, always giving importance to the opinions of others when doing any work. The neighbors are impressed by their behavior and are inspired to practice it. 4. The values that Uddipkar Sulekhadevi shares with her can be used to- i. Conflicts can be avoided ii. Bigotry and bigotry can be removed iii. People in the society benefit from it Which of the following is correct? A) i and ii B) ii and iii C) i and iii D) i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q1', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, 1, 'What does it mean to say "Udar Charitanam Tu Vasudhaiva Kutumbakam"?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q1a', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, NULL, 'Even though Puravi Dutta''s husband is abroad, she is happy with everyone in the joint family. She is very patient and heals anyone in the family when they are sick. No one returns from her house hungry. This makes everyone in the family like and respect her. The only problem in the family is Puravi''s brother-in-law. Her brother-in-law Sukhlal''s words and deeds do not match, he hangs out with bad people for many nights and sleeps until late. Lately, he has been irritable. As a result, there is constant unrest in the world. A. What are the signs of religion?'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q1b', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, NULL, 'Even though Puravi Dutta''s husband is abroad, she is happy with everyone in the joint family. She is very patient and heals anyone in the family when they are sick. No one returns from her house hungry. This makes everyone in the family like and respect her. The only problem in the family is Puravi''s brother-in-law. Her brother-in-law Sukhlal''s words and deeds do not match, he hangs out with bad people for many nights and sleeps until late. Lately, he has been irritable. As a result, there is constant unrest in the world. B. Explain what is one way of teaching morality.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q1c', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, NULL, 'Even though Puravi Dutta''s husband is abroad, she is happy with everyone in the joint family. She is very patient and heals anyone in the family when they are sick. No one returns from her house hungry. This makes everyone in the family like and respect her. The only problem in the family is Puravi''s brother-in-law. Her brother-in-law Sukhlal''s words and deeds do not match, he hangs out with bad people for many nights and sleeps until late. Lately, he has been irritable. As a result, there is constant unrest in the world. C. Explain the moral quality that emerges in the character of Uddipak''s Puravi Dutta in the light of moral values education.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q1d', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, NULL, 'Even though Puravi Dutta''s husband is abroad, she is happy with everyone in the joint family. She is very patient and heals anyone in the family when they are sick. No one returns from her house hungry. This makes everyone in the family like and respect her. The only problem in the family is Puravi''s brother-in-law. Her brother-in-law Sukhlal''s words and deeds do not match, he hangs out with bad people for many nights and sleeps until late. Lately, he has been irritable. As a result, there is constant unrest in the world. D. Evaluate the results that the activities of a person like Sukhlal can bring in life in the light of the textbook.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q2', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, 2, 'Write an example of how you want to do philanthropy.'),
  ('class7-hindu-en-ch8-p88-q3', 'class7-hindu-en', 'class7-hindu-en-ch8', 88, 3, 'What harm can drug use cause to the body?'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p3-t1', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 3, NULL, 'গৃহ ব্যবস্থাপনার স্তর অনুযায়ী একটি ক্লাসপার্টির আয়োজন করতে হলে তোমার কী করতে হবে তা লেখো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p4-t2', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 4, NULL, 'তোমার একটি লক্ষ্য উল্লেখ করো এবং লক্ষ্য অর্জন করতে তুমি কী সম্পদ ব্যবহার করবে তার একটি তালিকা তৈরি করো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p4-t3', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 4, NULL, 'সম্পদের বৈশিষ্ট্য অনুযায়ী তোমার পরিবারের সম্পদগুলো চিহ্নিত করো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p6-t4', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 6, NULL, 'তোমার মানবীয় সম্পদগুলো চিহ্নিত করো। লক্ষ্য অর্জনের জন্য সেগুলো কীভাবে সহায়তা করছে?'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p6-t5', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 6, NULL, 'তোমার পরিবারের সকল বস্তুগত সম্পদের তালিকা করো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p8-t6', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, 'ছুটির দিনে তোমার সময় ও কাজের তালিকা তৈরি করো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p8-t7', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, 'তোমার হাত খরচের টাকা থেকে কীভাবে সঞ্চয় করবে লেখো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-q1', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, 1, 'কোন বিষয়টিকে কেন্দ্র করে গৃহ ব্যবস্থাপনার স্তরগুলো চক্রাকারে আবর্তিত হয়? ক. সংগঠন খ. লক্ষ্য গ. নিয়ন্ত্রণ ঘ. পরিকল্পনা'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-q2', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, 2, 'গৃহ ব্যবস্থাপনার স্তরগুলোকে চক্রাকারে সাজালে নিয়ন্ত্রণের পর কোন স্তরটির স্থান— ক. সংগঠন খ. পরিকল্পনা গ. মূল্যায়ন ঘ. সিদ্ধান্ত'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-q3', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, 3, 'নিচের অনুচ্ছেদটি পড়ো এবং ৩ নং প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও। সচেতন গৃহিণী মনিরা বেগম সব সময় কেনাকাটা করতে যাওয়ার আগে পরিবারের সদস্যদের কার কী প্রয়োজন তা জেনে নেন এবং সর্বোচ্চ কত টাকার মধ্যে প্রত্যেকের প্রয়োজন মেটানো যায় তা চিন্তা ভাবনা করেন। মনিরা বেগমের অনুসৃত পদ্ধতিটিকে কী বলে? ক. কর্মতালিকা খ. বাজেট গ. মেনু পরিকল্পনা ঘ. দ্রব্যতালিকা'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-q4', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, 4, 'নিচের অনুচ্ছেদটি পড়ো এবং ৪ নং প্রশ্নের উত্তর দাও। সচেতন গৃহিণী মনিরা বেগম সব সময় কেনাকাটা করতে যাওয়ার আগে পরিবারের সদস্যদের কার কী প্রয়োজন তা জেনে নেন এবং সর্বোচ্চ কত টাকার মধ্যে প্রত্যেকের প্রয়োজন মেটানো যায় তা চিন্তা ভাবনা করেন। মনিরা বেগমের অভ্যাসের কারণে তার পরিবারে সদস্যদের— i. অর্থের অপব্যবহার কমবে ii. প্রয়োজনীয় চাহিদা মিটবে iii. সঞ্চয়ের অভ্যাস গড়ে উঠবে। নিচের কোনটি ঠিক? ক. i ও ii খ. i ও iii গ. ii ও iii ঘ. i, ii ও iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-t8', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, NULL, 'তোমার পরিবারের প্রতিদিনের বিভিন্নরকম কাজ সহজীকরণের কৌশলগুলো চার্টের মাধ্যমে দেখাও।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p10-t9', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 10, NULL, 'তুমি তোমার ঘরটি পরিপাটি ও পরিচ্ছন্ন রাখার ক্ষেত্রে যেসব সহজ পদ্ধতি অবলম্বন করো তা উল্লেখ করো।'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p11-q1', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 11, 1, 'গৃহসম্পদ কী?'),
  ('class7-homescience-bn-ch1-p11-q1a', 'class7-homescience-bn', 'class7-homescience-bn-ch1', 11, NULL, 'গ্রামে বসবাসকারী রহিমা বানু তার স্বল্প আয়ে সংসারের যাবতীয় চাহিদা অগ্রাধিকারের ভিত্তিতে পূরণ করতে চেষ্টা করেন। রান্নাঘর থেকে পানির চাপকল দূরে হওয়ায় তিনি পানি বালতিতে ভরে রাখেন। রান্নার প্রয়োজনীয় সরঞ্জাম হাতের নাগালে মাটির তৈরি তাকে রাখেন। যার ফলে নির্দিষ্ট সময়ের মধ্যে রান্না শেষ করে তিনি বাচ্চাদের নিয়ে স্কুলে যান। সম্পদ কী?'),
