  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p26-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 26, NULL, 'Draw five designs with the use of different types of line.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p26-t3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 26, NULL, 'Draw designs with geometrical and free forms.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p27-t4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 27, NULL, 'Write the names of five objects of different textures.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p29-t5', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 29, NULL, 'Draw five pictures following the five principles of art. Write a caption for each picture accordingly.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p31-t6', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 31, NULL, 'Make a list of the factors that you will consider for arrangement of furniture and prioritize them.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p32-t7', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 32, NULL, 'Which factors will you consider to buy the curtains for the drawing room of your house?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p34-t8', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 34, NULL, 'Make a wall hanging by using local items.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p35-t9', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 35, NULL, 'Which factors will you consider for the entrance of natural light in a room?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p37-t10', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 37, NULL, 'Arrange flowers with branches and leaves following different styles. Take help from your teacher.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 1, 'Which one of the following is a primary colour? a. orange b. red c. purple d. green'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1-2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 1, 'What are mixed colors?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, NULL, 'Mrs. Saleha and Halima live in the apartments of same space. Mrs. Saleha has used sky coloured curtains. On the other hand, Halima has used curtains which are printed with red flowers. She has kept a large tub made of clay beside the door. One day Maria Akter, from a neighbouring apartment went to Mrs. Saleha''s house. From there she went to Mrs. Halima''s house and said that it could be better if you have a little bigger drawing room. a. What is the source of light?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, NULL, 'Mrs. Saleha and Halima live in the apartments of same space. Mrs. Saleha has used sky coloured curtains. On the other hand, Halima has used curtains which are printed with red flowers. She has kept a large tub made of clay beside the door. One day Maria Akter, from a neighbouring apartment went to Mrs. Saleha''s house. From there she went to Mrs. Halima''s house and said that it could be better if you have a little bigger drawing room. b. What is an interior decoration?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, NULL, 'Mrs. Saleha and Halima live in the apartments of same space. Mrs. Saleha has used sky coloured curtains. On the other hand, Halima has used curtains which are printed with red flowers. She has kept a large tub made of clay beside the door. One day Maria Akter, from a neighbouring apartment went to Mrs. Saleha''s house. From there she went to Mrs. Halima''s house and said that it could be better if you have a little bigger drawing room. c. On which factor has Mrs. Saleha given emphasis in decorating her room? Explain.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q1d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, NULL, 'Mrs. Saleha and Halima live in the apartments of same space. Mrs. Saleha has used sky coloured curtains. On the other hand, Halima has used curtains which are printed with red flowers. She has kept a large tub made of clay beside the door. One day Maria Akter, from a neighbouring apartment went to Mrs. Saleha''s house. From there she went to Mrs. Halima''s house and said that it could be better if you have a little bigger drawing room. d. Analyze the efficiency of Mrs. Halima in decorating her home.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 2, 'Which line can create more variety? a. zigzag line b. diagonal line c. vertical line d. curved line'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q2-2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 2, 'Describe the different geometric shapes in a art.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 3, 'Read the passage and answer questions 3 and 4. Mrs. Nishat has chosen curtains that match the color of her walls. She also decorates her home with flowers. Which art principle is shown through the matching colors of walls and curtains? a. proportion b. balance c. similarity d. rhythm'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q3-2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 3, 'What is the principle of art?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch3-p38-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch3', 38, 4, 'Read the passage and answer questions 3 and 4. Mrs. Nishat has chosen curtains that match the color of her walls. She also decorates her home with flowers. The actions by Mrs. Nishat help create prominence using flowers- i. placing the vase in a visible spot. ii. using an elegant and eye-catching vase. iii. placing the most attractive flowers among others. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii, and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p42-t1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 42, NULL, 'As a member of a family what will be your responsibilities?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p42-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 42, NULL, 'What are the qualities that you should have as you grow up for the welfare of the society?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p45-t3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 45, NULL, 'How do you and your brother or sister help each other in your family? Give some examples.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p47-t4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'What kind of manner do the children learn through peer group?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p47-t5', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 47, NULL, 'What kind of development does a child have with the co-curricular activities?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p48-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 48, 1, 'Which quality is needed to become self-reliant? a. move forward to help others when they are in danger b. to stay in a safe distance c. education for a long time d. to depend on others'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p48-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 48, 2, 'What quality do children have when they mix with their peers? i. self-confidence ii. attitudes of co-operation iii. respect to each other. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p48-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 48, 3, 'Read the following stem and answer to the questions number 3 & 4. Ruma and Kona are two sisters. Their mother encourages them to do their own works. Ruma is a student of class VII and her sister is a student of class VI. Ruma very often arranges the books, clothes and bed of her sister. What kind of attitude does Ruma have? a. co-operation b. discipline c. leadership d. sympathy'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p48-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 48, 4, 'Read the following stem and answer to the questions number 3 & 4. Ruma and Kona are two sisters. Their mother encourages them to do their own works. Ruma is a student of class VII and her sister is a student of class VI. Ruma very often arranges the books, clothes and bed of her sister. What will be the result of Ruma''s behaviour towards Kona? i. Kona will be less willing to work. ii. Kona will be dependent on others. iii. Kona will be sympathetic to others. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, 1, 'What is the role of school in a child''s moral development?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q1a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Rebeka Begum has her busy husband and two children, Suman and Sumana, in her family. Her husband is always busy at his work. Rebeka Begum exchanges her feelings with her children like a friend. Their father also spends time with them in spite of his busy schedule and takes them to the parks and historical places for their entertainment. a. What is a family?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q1b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Rebeka Begum has her busy husband and two children, Suman and Sumana, in her family. Her husband is always busy at his work. Rebeka Begum exchanges her feelings with her children like a friend. Their father also spends time with them in spite of his busy schedule and takes them to the parks and historical places for their entertainment. b. Why is it necessary to follow the rules and regulations of a society in making a good citizen of the country?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q1c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Rebeka Begum has her busy husband and two children, Suman and Sumana, in her family. Her husband is always busy at his work. Rebeka Begum exchanges her feelings with her children like a friend. Their father also spends time with them in spite of his busy schedule and takes them to the parks and historical places for their entertainment. c. What kind of manner of a child will be developed from the influence of Rebeka Begum''s behaviour towards her children?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q1d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Rebeka Begum has her busy husband and two children, Suman and Sumana, in her family. Her husband is always busy at his work. Rebeka Begum exchanges her feelings with her children like a friend. Their father also spends time with them in spite of his busy schedule and takes them to the parks and historical places for their entertainment. d. The environment mentioned in the stem is helpful to obtain a sound development for the children – justify this statement.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, 2, 'Why do people prefer to be in groups?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q2a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Roni reads in class VII. He discusses the lessons and other general topics with his classmates. Roni made a club named ''Sabuj Shangho'' to make his community pollution free with his friends. Roni and his friends with the help of community people arranged some large drums to keep all wastes into them properly. "Sabuj Shangha" organized by Roni and his friends is involved with many development works which have been appreciated by all. Roni''s mother always encourages him in his activities. a. Which technique is the most important to guide children properly?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q2b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Roni reads in class VII. He discusses the lessons and other general topics with his classmates. Roni made a club named ''Sabuj Shangho'' to make his community pollution free with his friends. Roni and his friends with the help of community people arranged some large drums to keep all wastes into them properly. "Sabuj Shangha" organized by Roni and his friends is involved with many development works which have been appreciated by all. Roni''s mother always encourages him in his activities. b. Why is it necessary to have a friendly relationship among siblings?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q2c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Roni reads in class VII. He discusses the lessons and other general topics with his classmates. Roni made a club named ''Sabuj Shangho'' to make his community pollution free with his friends. Roni and his friends with the help of community people arranged some large drums to keep all wastes into them properly. "Sabuj Shangha" organized by Roni and his friends is involved with many development works which have been appreciated by all. Roni''s mother always encourages him in his activities. c. Which quality of Roni has been developed through the activities mentioned in the stem? Explain.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q2d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, NULL, 'Roni reads in class VII. He discusses the lessons and other general topics with his classmates. Roni made a club named ''Sabuj Shangho'' to make his community pollution free with his friends. Roni and his friends with the help of community people arranged some large drums to keep all wastes into them properly. "Sabuj Shangha" organized by Roni and his friends is involved with many development works which have been appreciated by all. Roni''s mother always encourages him in his activities. d. ''Mother''s encouragement and good association have made Roni familiar with all.''– justify this statement.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch4-p49-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch4', 49, 3, 'What roles do teachers play in the social development of children?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p54-t1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 54, NULL, 'Make a list of outdoor games and indoor games that you know.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p54-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 54, NULL, 'Describe the importance of the game with the movement of body for physical development.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p56-t3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 56, NULL, 'Describe what kinds of games help for socialization?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p58-t4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 58, NULL, 'Make a list of the kinds of games that will develop your creative mind.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p60-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 60, 1, 'Which one is a constructive game? a. swimming b. riding cycle c. making doll d. hide and seek'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p60-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 60, 2, 'Through which game the quality of leadership is built? a. video game b. chess c. football d. drawing picture'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p60-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 60, 3, 'Read the following stem and answer to the question number 3 and 4. Fahim is a very good student. He gets pleasure by reading story books and drawing picture in leisure time. Fahim plays chess with her mother and often wins. What kind of development does Fahim have by playing games? a. skill b. socialization c. attitude to imitate d. strength of muscle'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p60-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 60, 4, 'Read the following stem and answer to the question number 3 and 4. Fahim is a very good student. He gets pleasure by reading story books and drawing picture in leisure time. Fahim plays chess with her mother and often wins. In which area does Fahim have improvement? i. mental development ii. intelligence iii. capability of creation or invention. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p60-t5', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 60, NULL, 'How do you maintain your hobby beside your study? Describe.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, 1, 'What is a constructive game?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q1a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Faraz is a dependable goalkeeper of the football team of his school. He tries to co-operate his neighbours. He sometimes makes different kinds of flowers, birds and other designs by cutting pieces of paper in his leisure time. Besides, collecting stamps and reading book are also his hobbies. a. What kind of game is chess?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q1b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Faraz is a dependable goalkeeper of the football team of his school. He tries to co-operate his neighbours. He sometimes makes different kinds of flowers, birds and other designs by cutting pieces of paper in his leisure time. Besides, collecting stamps and reading book are also his hobbies. b. Why is the hobby of coin collection helpful to increase the knowledge beside entertainment?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q1c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Faraz is a dependable goalkeeper of the football team of his school. He tries to co-operate his neighbours. He sometimes makes different kinds of flowers, birds and other designs by cutting pieces of paper in his leisure time. Besides, collecting stamps and reading book are also his hobbies. c. What kind of development does Faraz have with the way that he spends his leisure time? Explain.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q1d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Faraz is a dependable goalkeeper of the football team of his school. He tries to co-operate his neighbours. He sometimes makes different kinds of flowers, birds and other designs by cutting pieces of paper in his leisure time. Besides, collecting stamps and reading book are also his hobbies. d. ''It is possible to achieve the social qualities through following Faraz.'' -Analyze this statement.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, 2, 'What is the indoor game?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q2a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Sumita is a working lady. She always gives nutritious foods to her only daughter Mita who is 5 years old. Mita spends her leisure time by watching television and playing computer games. Recently Sumita has noticed that Mita is becoming fat and instead of mixing with other children of her age she plays alone. a. How does every healthy child spend most of the time of a day?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q2b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Sumita is a working lady. She always gives nutritious foods to her only daughter Mita who is 5 years old. Mita spends her leisure time by watching television and playing computer games. Recently Sumita has noticed that Mita is becoming fat and instead of mixing with other children of her age she plays alone. b. The nature for play is changed with the growing of age– explain it.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q2c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Sumita is a working lady. She always gives nutritious foods to her only daughter Mita who is 5 years old. Mita spends her leisure time by watching television and playing computer games. Recently Sumita has noticed that Mita is becoming fat and instead of mixing with other children of her age she plays alone. c. Explain the reasons for physical change of Mita.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q2d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, NULL, 'Sumita is a working lady. She always gives nutritious foods to her only daughter Mita who is 5 years old. Mita spends her leisure time by watching television and playing computer games. Recently Sumita has noticed that Mita is becoming fat and instead of mixing with other children of her age she plays alone. d. How will the ways that Mita''s spends her leisure time affect on her social development? Analyze.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, 3, 'How do sports help a child''s physical growth?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch5-p61-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch5', 61, 4, 'How does entertainment benefit a child''s development?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p65-t1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 65, NULL, 'What are the rights for the children who are employed to do household works at home.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p69-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 69, 1, 'Which one is a right to live your life? a. to know the information b. to speak with freedom c. to live a standard life d. to get a healthy environment'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p69-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 69, NULL, 'Make a list of rights which our children cannot get according to the declaration of the United Nations (UN). What are the ways to achieve those rights?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, 1, 'What is child labor?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q1a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, NULL, 'Rana is 12 years old. He reads in class V and is a good student. His ricksha puller father cannot work properly as he has been sick for a long time. In this circumstance, his parents have stopped Rana''s education and has sent him to a nearby garments factory to work there. a. Which is the most widely expected human right?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q1b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, NULL, 'Rana is 12 years old. He reads in class V and is a good student. His ricksha puller father cannot work properly as he has been sick for a long time. In this circumstance, his parents have stopped Rana''s education and has sent him to a nearby garments factory to work there. b. Why most of the children of Bangladesh are deprived of a good protection according to the declaration?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q1c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, NULL, 'Rana is 12 years old. He reads in class V and is a good student. His ricksha puller father cannot work properly as he has been sick for a long time. In this circumstance, his parents have stopped Rana''s education and has sent him to a nearby garments factory to work there. c. Which right has Rana been deprived of? Explain.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q1d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, NULL, 'Rana is 12 years old. He reads in class V and is a good student. His ricksha puller father cannot work properly as he has been sick for a long time. In this circumstance, his parents have stopped Rana''s education and has sent him to a nearby garments factory to work there. d. To what extent is Abdul Malek''s decision justified according to the declaration of United Nations? Analyze it.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, 2, 'Read the stem below and answer to the question number 2 and 3. On the way of going to the school from home Turzo often sees one man. Sometimes the man gives him chocolate. One day he took Turzo far away saying that they were going to a park and he handed over Turzo to a stranger. Of which situation has Turzo become a victim? a. showing fear b. discrimination c. fraudulence d. negligence'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q2-2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, 2, 'Why is child trafficking more common in Bangladesh?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, 3, 'Read the stem below and answer to the question number 2 and 3. On the way of going to the school from home Turzo often sees one man. Sometimes the man gives him chocolate. One day he took Turzo far away saying that they were going to a park and he handed over Turzo to a stranger. According to the description in the stem what may happen to Turzo? i. he may become a victim of child trafficking. ii. he may become involved with juvenile delinquencies. iii. kidnappers may demand a ransom for his release. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch6-p70-q3-2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch6', 70, 3, 'What does separation against the will of a child mean?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p75-t1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 75, NULL, 'Write about the type of disability of a person you know.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p75-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 75, NULL, 'Write about the early stimulation that the disabled child is given and read your answer aloud to the class.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p77-t3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 77, NULL, 'Make a chronological list of the responsibilities of a family towards the disabled child.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p80-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 80, 1, 'Which day is observed as the "World Autism Day"? a. 2nd December b. 3rd December c. 4th December d. 5th December'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p80-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 80, 2, 'A loving family can help a child to- i. proper development ii. reduce disability iii. become self-dependent. Which of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p80-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 80, 3, 'Read the following stem and answer the question number 3 and 4. Chayan studies in class two. Listening to his teacher he can write correctly in the notebook. But he cannot write following the board. As a result he cannot complete the class work in time. This would make his teacher annoyed at Chayan. Hence Chayan became withdrawn. The class teacher noticed this and informed Chanyan''s parents. They immediately took him to the doctors. Chayan is- a. hearing impaired b. speech impaired c. intellectually impaired d. visually impaired'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p80-t4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 80, NULL, 'How relatives, neighbors and teachers can assist a family having trouble with the disabled child? Discuss.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, 1, 'Who is considered visually impaired?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q1a', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, NULL, 'Pranti and Pratoy are brothers and sisters. Protoy is two years old and Pranti is a teenager. Pranti usually behaves like Pratoy and often laughs without any reason. Her family members keep her busy with songs, painting and drawing pictures and telling her stories. Everyone in the family listens to her attentively and her mother takes care of her with a lot of love and patience. a. Who constitutes the society?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q1b', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, NULL, 'Pranti and Pratoy are brothers and sisters. Protoy is two years old and Pranti is a teenager. Pranti usually behaves like Pratoy and often laughs without any reason. Her family members keep her busy with songs, painting and drawing pictures and telling her stories. Everyone in the family listens to her attentively and her mother takes care of her with a lot of love and patience. b. Why is the early stimulation necessary?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q1c', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, NULL, 'Pranti and Pratoy are brothers and sisters. Protoy is two years old and Pranti is a teenager. Pranti usually behaves like Pratoy and often laughs without any reason. Her family members keep her busy with songs, painting and drawing pictures and telling her stories. Everyone in the family listens to her attentively and her mother takes care of her with a lot of love and patience. c. What disability can you notice in Pranti? Explain.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q1d', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, NULL, 'Pranti and Pratoy are brothers and sisters. Protoy is two years old and Pranti is a teenager. Pranti usually behaves like Pratoy and often laughs without any reason. Her family members keep her busy with songs, painting and drawing pictures and telling her stories. Everyone in the family listens to her attentively and her mother takes care of her with a lot of love and patience. d. ''The behavior of all the family members of Pranti is a great support for her mental development.'' - analyze the statement.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, 2, 'What is a hearing impairment?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, 3, 'Why should children with disabilities not be neglected?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch7-p81-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch7', 81, 4, 'Read the following stem and answer the question number 3 and 4. Chayan studies in class two. Listening to his teacher he can write correctly in the notebook. But he cannot write following the board. As a result he cannot complete the class work in time. This would make his teacher annoyed at Chayan. Hence Chayan became withdrawn. The class teacher noticed this and informed Chanyan''s parents. They immediately took him to the doctors. Which of the following steps could have saved Chayan from this situation- i. help from the family. ii. help from the teachers. iii. timely treatment. Which of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. ii and iii c. i and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p85-t1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 85, NULL, 'Write the names of protein-rich foods we eat everyday.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p85-t2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 85, NULL, 'Write down the functions of protein in our body.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p87-t3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 87, NULL, 'Why will you eat food containing carbohydrate? Explain'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p89-t4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 89, NULL, 'Make a list of foods that you take everyday containing fat.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p89-t5', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 89, NULL, 'What are the functions of the food containing fat in your body?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p91-t6', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 91, NULL, 'Write down the names of sources of different kinds of vitamins.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p93-t7', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 93, NULL, 'Why is it necessary to eat food containing minerals? Describe.'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p96-t8', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 96, NULL, 'In which conditions does the demand of water in the body increase?'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p98-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 98, 1, 'How many nutrients are present in food? a. 5 b. 6 b. 7 d. 8'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p98-q2', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 98, 2, 'Which one is essential or the normal growth of a growing child? a. carbohydrate b. protein c. fat d. minerals'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p98-q3', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 98, 3, 'Read the following stem and answer to the question number 3 and 4. Rita is 8 years old. She likes to eat rice with vegetables only. Rita becomes tired when she plays with her friends of the same age. She has no interest in study. If she is asked to do any work by her mother, she does not want to do that. Her lack of interest in all matters makes her family anxious. Which nutrient is absent in Rita''s food? a. protein b. minerals c. carbohydrate d. water'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p98-q4', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 98, 4, 'Read the following stem and answer to the question number 3 and 4. Rita is 8 years old. She likes to eat rice with vegetables only. Rita becomes tired when she plays with her friends of the same age. She has no interest in study. If she is asked to do any work by her mother, she does not want to do that. Her lack of interest in all matters makes her family anxious. Which list below should be emphasised in Rita''s daily meals? a. date palm, raisin, pineapple, banana b. ientils, nuts, soya bean oil, seeds of bean c. oil, ghee, butter and coconut d. sea fish, liver, egg yolk'),
  ('class7-homescience-en-ch8-p99-q1', 'class7-homescience-en', 'class7-homescience-en-ch8', 99, 1, 'What is the role of lipids in the body?'),
