ঘ) দৃশ্যপট-২ সেলিম উল্লাহর কর্মকাণ্ডে তোমার পাঠ্য বইয়ের যে ঘটনার সাথে সাদৃশ্যপূর্ণ তা চিহ্নিত করে এর গুরুত্ব বিশ্লেষণ করো'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p5-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 5, NULL, 'The students will read the significance of Tawhid, memorize this and write it down in copy and they will show it to their friend sitting next to them.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p5-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 5, NULL, 'They will make a list of probable changes that might take place in one''s personal life and activities for believing in Tawhid.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p7-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 7, NULL, 'Only firm belief in Tawhid can present a strong moral character in a man. The students will discuss the matter in groups in the class and present it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p8-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 8, NULL, 'Student will be divided into two groups. A group will deseribe the indentity of kufr. The other group will describe the evils and consequences of disbelief.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p9-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 9, NULL, 'Students will make a list of the activities of Shirk and Show it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p9-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 9, NULL, 'Describe the ways of avoiding Shirk.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p12-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 12, NULL, 'The students will discuss the seven aspects of Iman-E-Mufassal in groups.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p12-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 12, NULL, 'Every student will read out Iman-E-Mufassal with meaning and will listen to each other.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p16-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Describe the impact of the attributive names of Allah in human life.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p16-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 16, NULL, 'Write five attributive names of Allah with their meanings.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p18-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 18, NULL, 'Describe the importance and significance of belief in Risalat.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p19-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 19, NULL, 'All students of the class will be divided into two groups. One group will be telling the meaning and types of Wahi from their memory. The other group will discuss the importance of Wahi. Again, the first group will discuss the importance of Wahi, while the second group will tell the meaning and types of Wahi from their memory.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p23-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 23, 1, 'What is ''the belief in Allah, the exalted as a unique soul'' called?
a. Aqaid
b. Takwa
c. Tawhid
d. Obedience'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p23-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 23, 2, 'Belief in Risalat –
i. Helps in achieving the pleasure of Allah
ii. Makes one interested in following the teachings of the Holy Prophet (PBUH)
iii. Helps in increasing personal social status
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p23-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 23, NULL, 'Write the importance of belief in the Hereafter.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p23-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 23, NULL, 'Make a list of the stages of the Hereafter.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p24-q1a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 24, NULL, 'Rasel and Sohel are in the same class. Two months before the annual examination, ''Rasel'' becomes very ill. One month before the examination, his father dies. ''Rasel'' patiently seeks help from Allah and participates in the annual examination. On the other hand, before the examination, ''Sohel'' asks for dua from the Imam of the mosque before the examination. After the results are published, he comes to know that he has done badly in the examination. Once he comments, if there was a Creator, I would not have failed.
a) What is revelation/ohi?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p24-q1b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 24, NULL, 'Rasel and Sohel are in the same class. Two months before the annual examination, ''Rasel'' becomes very ill. One month before the examination, his father dies. ''Rasel'' patiently seeks help from Allah and participates in the annual examination. On the other hand, before the examination, ''Sohel'' asks for dua from the Imam of the mosque before the examination. After the results are published, he comes to know that he has done badly in the examination. Once he comments, if there was a Creator, I would not have failed.
b) Why is belief in angels important? Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p24-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 24, 3, 'Nasir crossed a bridge on his way home from the market with his father. As soon as he was leaving the market, Nasir noticed some people were playing something for money sitting in the position like party celebration. Out of curiosity, when he asked his father about it, he said, "This is gambling." It is forbidden and sinful in Islam.
Which stage of the afterlife is highlighted in the statement of Nasir''s father''s?
a. the grave
b. the resurrection
c. the scale
d. the Bridge over Hell'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p24-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 24, 4, 'Nasir crossed a bridge on his way home from the market with his father. As soon as he was leaving the market, Nasir noticed some people were playing something for money sitting in the position like party celebration. Out of curiosity, when he asked his father about it, he said, "This is gambling." It is forbidden and sinful in Islam.
The consequences of the violation of the creed by the actions of the mentioned people are:
i. He will enjoy get punished in Hell.
ii. Peace will be hampered in the society.
iii. Human dignity will be diminished.
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 1, '''Tawheed gives people a sense of oneness.'' Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 2, 'Why is belief in the books of Allah the Almighty important?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q2a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, NULL, 'Anis Mia is a businessman. He gives underweight while selling goods. He thinks that he will not have to be accountable to anyone for this. Anis Mia''s neighbour, Mr. Tamal, works in a multinational company. He thinks that honesty or dishonesty in his life depends on the orders of his boss. A few days ago, Mr. Tamal''s elder son was arrested for robbery. He was sentenced to prison in the trial.
a) What is Mizan?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q2b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, NULL, 'Anis Mia is a businessman. He gives underweight while selling goods. He thinks that he will not have to be accountable to anyone for this. Anis Mia''s neighbour, Mr. Tamal, works in a multinational company. He thinks that honesty or dishonesty in his life depends on the orders of his boss. A few days ago, Mr. Tamal''s elder son was arrested for robbery. He was sentenced to prison in the trial.
b) ''Tawheed and morality complement each other''. Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q2c', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, NULL, 'Anis Mia is a businessman. He gives underweight while selling goods. He thinks that he will not have to be accountable to anyone for this. Anis Mia''s neighbour, Mr. Tamal, works in a multinational company. He thinks that honesty or dishonesty in his life depends on the orders of his boss. A few days ago, Mr. Tamal''s elder son was arrested for robbery. He was sentenced to prison in the trial.
c) Which fundamental aspect of faith is violated in the actions of Mr. ''Anis''? Explicate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q2d', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, NULL, 'Anis Mia is a businessman. He gives underweight while selling goods. He thinks that he will not have to be accountable to anyone for this. Anis Mia''s neighbour, Mr. Tamal, works in a multinational company. He thinks that honesty or dishonesty in his life depends on the orders of his boss. A few days ago, Mr. Tamal''s elder son was arrested for robbery. He was sentenced to prison in the trial.
d) Identify the issue of Aqaid that has emerged in the mindset of Mr. ''Tomal'' and analyze its social consequences.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 3, '''The destiny of everything is in the hands of Allah.'' Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 4, '''Revelation/ohi is the source of all knowledge and science.'' Illustrate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q5', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 5, 'Why should there be no distinction between the Prophets?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q6', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 6, 'Why should one believe in resurrection after death?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch1-p25-q7', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch1', 25, 7, 'Why is the world called the grain-field of the Hereafter?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p28-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'The students will be divided into groups and make a list of the duties of the Imam and muktadis and write them on poster paper with marker.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p28-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 28, NULL, 'Describe the importance of performing Salat-e-Jamaat.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p29-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 29, NULL, 'A learner went to the mosque to say his Magrib prayer but joined only one rakat with the imam. How will he complete his remaining rakat? The learners will be divided in groups and discuss it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p30-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 30, NULL, 'The learners will make a list of the Salat which will have to be performed in full and also the Salat which will have to be performed as Qasr. Then they will make a poster and present it in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p31-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 31, NULL, 'The learners will discuss the ways of performing Salat for the sick persons in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p33-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 33, NULL, 'The learners will discuss the methods of perfoming Salat of Jumu''ah in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p34-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 34, NULL, 'The learners will make a chart on the wazib and sunnah works to be done on the day of Eid-ul-Fitr. Then they will write the chart on a poster.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p34-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 34, NULL, 'Describe the importance of Eid-ul-Fitr.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p36-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 36, NULL, 'A learner will show the rules of Salat of Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Adha by performing them in the class. The others will note down the mistakes in their copies and then discuss.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p38-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 38, NULL, 'The learners will be divided into groups and then discuss the importance of Salatul janazah in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p38-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 38, NULL, 'Describe the way of performing Salatul Janazah.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p39-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 39, NULL, '“Performing salat-e-Tarawih in Jamat lessens the probability of mistakes” The learners will get into groups and discuss it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p40-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 40, NULL, '''Servants of Allah, can get the closeness of Allah through the performance of Salat of Tahajjud. The learners will discuss it in groups.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p41-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 41, NULL, 'The learners will make a table about the timings and rakats of Salatul Ishraq and Salatul Awabin. They will make a poster and present it in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p42-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 42, NULL, 'The moral teaching of Salat makes a man dutiful. The learners will discuss this matter in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p42-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 42, NULL, 'The learners will discuss in group and make a list of the moral teachings of Salat.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p44-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 44, NULL, 'The learners will make a chart of the religious and moral teachings of Sawm and show it in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p45-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 45, NULL, 'The learners will write the timetable of the Sahri, Iftar and its dua in a chart and present it in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p46-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 46, NULL, 'The learners will write down the reasons of qaza and kaffara of fasting on different posters and then present it in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p47-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 47, NULL, '“It is possible to gain the Lailatul Qadr through Itikaf” The learners will discuss this.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p48-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 48, NULL, 'The learners will be divided into groups and discuss the significance of ‘sadakatul fitr’.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p49-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 49, NULL, '‘The self-restraint teaching of sawm plays a special role in controlling the bad instinct of human beings.’ The learners will be divided into groups and discuss it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p49-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 49, NULL, '‘The compassion gained from Sawm helps a man to be sympathetic to the poor’. Explain it.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p50-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 50, 1, 'Which Ibadat teaches mankind about self-restraint?
a. Salat
b. Zakat
c. Sawm
d. Hajj'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p50-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 50, 2, 'Through paying Sadakatul Fitr
i. all errors of observing Sawm are removed.
ii. wealth increases.
iii. foods are arranged for poor.
Which one is correct?
a. i
b. i & ii
c. i & iii
d. i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p50-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 50, NULL, 'The learners will write down how they will make use of the teachings of the chapter ''Ibadat'' in their future life. They will make a list and write them on a poster.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q1a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, NULL, '''Rafid'' is ten years old. He took his food at dawn to seek the pleasure of Allah and did not eat anything else before sunset. His uncle Mr. ''Tariq'' stays in the mosque during the last ten days of a particular month and engages in worship. Since he cannot maintain any contact with his family during this time, ''Rafid'' always buys things from the market at his uncle''s house.
A. What is a Muqtadi?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q1b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, NULL, '''Rafid'' is ten years old. He took his food at dawn to seek the pleasure of Allah and did not eat anything else before sunset. His uncle Mr. ''Tariq'' stays in the mosque during the last ten days of a particular month and engages in worship. Since he cannot maintain any contact with his family during this time, ''Rafid'' always buys things from the market at his uncle''s house.
B. Why is Friday prayer important? Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q1c', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, NULL, '''Rafid'' is ten years old. He took his food at dawn to seek the pleasure of Allah and did not eat anything else before sunset. His uncle Mr. ''Tariq'' stays in the mosque during the last ten days of a particular month and engages in worship. Since he cannot maintain any contact with his family during this time, ''Rafid'' always buys things from the market at his uncle''s house.
C. Which basic act of worship has been observed in the activities of ''Rafid''? Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q1d', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, NULL, '''Rafid'' is ten years old. He took his food at dawn to seek the pleasure of Allah and did not eat anything else before sunset. His uncle Mr. ''Tariq'' stays in the mosque during the last ten days of a particular month and engages in worship. Since he cannot maintain any contact with his family during this time, ''Rafid'' always buys things from the market at his uncle''s house.
D. Identify the topics of your textbook that has emerged in the act of worship of Mr. ''Tariq'' and analyze its results.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, 3, 'In the month of Ramadan, Mr. ''Murad'' fasts and leaves for his village home in the morning. Due to the traffic jam, he buys cold water from the fridge of a shop and drinks it in the heat of the afternoon. On the other hand, his son Mr. ''Tanim'' goes to the mosque to offer Zuhr prayer. Since he is a little late in reaching the mosque, he can offer one rak''ah of prayer with the Imam.
What has been violated by Mr. ''Murad''s action?
A. Fard
B. Wajib
C. Sunnah
D. Nafl'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p51-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 51, 4, 'In the month of Ramadan, Mr. ''Murad'' fasts and leaves for his village home in the morning. Due to the traffic jam, he buys cold water from the fridge of a shop and drinks it in the heat of the afternoon. On the other hand, his son Mr. ''Tanim'' goes to the mosque to offer Zuhr prayer. Since he is a little late in reaching the mosque, he can offer one rak''ah of prayer with the Imam.
What should be done in the case of ''Tanim'' –
i. Standing after the Imam''s prayer
ii. Performing the remaining three rak''ahs
iii. Offering the prayer in a short form
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 1, 'Explain the role of the Imam in prayer.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 2, '''Allah''s permission to offer shortened prayers for travelers is a great blessing.'' Illustrate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 3, '''Harmony and brotherhood are developed in congregational prayer.'' Explicate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 4, '''The closeness of Allah is attained through the Tahajjud prayer.'' Clarify'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q5', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 5, 'Indeed, prayer prevents people from indecent and bad deeds.'' Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q6', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 6, '''Fasting is a shield.'' Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q7', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 7, 'Why is Sadaqatul Fitr obligatory? Interpret.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch2-p52-q8', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch2', 52, 8, '''Fasting teaches people self-control.'' Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p57-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 57, NULL, 'At the end of this lesson the learners, will learn about the compilation of the Quran and discuss it in some groups and write a summary of this.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p61-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 61, NULL, 'The learners will make a list of the signs of Waqf.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p65-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 65, NULL, 'On their exercise book, the learners will write down three learning points of Sura Adiyat and will show it to the teacher.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p70-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 70, NULL, 'The learners will tell the background of Sura At-Takasur to the friends sitting next to them.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p70-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 70, NULL, 'The learners will make a poster with the earning points of the Surah At-Takasur.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p71-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 71, NULL, 'The learners will make a list of the learning points of Sura Lahab'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p73-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 73, NULL, 'The learners will write down the learning points of Sura Ikhlas and make a poster.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p75-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 75, NULL, 'The learners will tell one another these three verses with the meanings.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p75-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 75, NULL, 'The learners will make a poster with the three verses on it and hang in front of their reading table.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p79-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 79, NULL, 'The learners will memorize the three hadith and tell their meanings too.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p80-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 80, 1, 'How many verses are there in Surah Al-Ikhlas?
A. 4
B. 5
C. 8
D. 11'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p80-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 80, 2, 'If you recite the Quran, you will-
i. Increase your social status
ii. Receive endless rewards
iii. Receive intercession on the Day of Judgment
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p80-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 80, 3, '''Raseed'' and ''Nayeem'' are two brothers. ''Raseed'' finds a verse in the Quran instructing him to pray, but he is worried about how to perform it. The Imam of their mosque advises him to follow the principles of prayer of the Prophet (PBUH). ''Nayeem'' can recite the Quran. While reciting the Quran, he does not stop at the place where the sign of waqf (م) is in the Quranic verse and reads it together
Which source of Islamic way of life did Imam Sahib point to?
A. Quran
B. Hadith
C. Ijma
D. Qiyas'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p80-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 80, 4, '''Raseed'' and ''Nayeem'' are two brothers. ''Raseed'' finds a verse in the Quran instructing him to pray, but he is worried about how to perform it. The Imam of their mosque advises him to follow the principles of prayer of the Prophet (PBUH). ''Nayeem'' can recite the Quran. While reciting the Quran, he does not stop at the place where the sign of waqf (م) is in the Quranic verse and reads it together
The violation of the rules of reciting the Quran Majeed in the recitation of ''Nayeem'' will result in –
i. The prayer will not be right
ii. The command of Allah will be disobeyed
iii. Social rules will be violated
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, 1, 'Why is Hazrat Usman (RA) called Jami''ul Quran?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q1a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'While reciting the Quran, Shabiha did not read the letters that have the vertical jabar (ٰ) above, the vertical jer (ٖ) below and the inverted pesh (ٗ) above by one alif. His father, Mr. ''Asad'', is the owner of immense wealth. He deposits thousands of crores of taka in the bank every year. He competes with the rich for wealth.
a) What is Madde Farai?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q1b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'While reciting the Quran, Shabiha did not read the letters that have the vertical jabar (ٰ) above, the vertical jer (ٖ) below and the inverted pesh (ٗ) above by one alif. His father, Mr. ''Asad'', is the owner of immense wealth. He deposits thousands of crores of taka in the bank every year. He competes with the rich for wealth.
b) Why is it necessary to make waqf while reciting the Quran? Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q1c', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'While reciting the Quran, Shabiha did not read the letters that have the vertical jabar (ٰ) above, the vertical jer (ٖ) below and the inverted pesh (ٗ) above by one alif. His father, Mr. ''Asad'', is the owner of immense wealth. He deposits thousands of crores of taka in the bank every year. He competes with the rich for wealth.
c) Which aspect of reciting the Quran has been violated by Shabiha? Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q1d', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'While reciting the Quran, Shabiha did not read the letters that have the vertical jabar (ٰ) above, the vertical jer (ٖ) below and the inverted pesh (ٗ) above by one alif. His father, Mr. ''Asad'', is the owner of immense wealth. He deposits thousands of crores of taka in the bank every year. He competes with the rich for wealth.
d) Identify the Surah in which the teachings of Mr. ''Asad'' are violated and analyze its consequences.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, 2, 'Why is it important to know the lesson of Surah Al-Qari''ah?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q2a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'Fact-1: Mr. ''Jarif'' is a rich and influential person in the area. He invites the rich people of the area to various functions at his house and feeds them. The poor people of the area cannot enter Jarif''s house during the functions.
Fact-2: Mr. ''Mahfuz'' keeps his shop open during the call to prayer and conducts business. On the other hand, other businessmen close their shops and go to offer prayers. A business friend of his advised ''Mahfuz'' to offer prayers. In response, Samad said that there is no need for prayers for the progress of business.
a) What is Sihah Sittah?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q2b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'Fact-1: Mr. ''Jarif'' is a rich and influential person in the area. He invites the rich people of the area to various functions at his house and feeds them. The poor people of the area cannot enter Jarif''s house during the functions.
Fact-2: Mr. ''Mahfuz'' keeps his shop open during the call to prayer and conducts business. On the other hand, other businessmen close their shops and go to offer prayers. A business friend of his advised ''Mahfuz'' to offer prayers. In response, Samad said that there is no need for prayers for the progress of business.
b) Explain the hadith ''He who cuts off the ties of kinship will not enter Paradise.'''),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q2c', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'Fact-1: Mr. ''Jarif'' is a rich and influential person in the area. He invites the rich people of the area to various functions at his house and feeds them. The poor people of the area cannot enter Jarif''s house during the functions.
Fact-2: Mr. ''Mahfuz'' keeps his shop open during the call to prayer and conducts business. On the other hand, other businessmen close their shops and go to offer prayers. A business friend of his advised ''Mahfuz'' to offer prayers. In response, Samad said that there is no need for prayers for the progress of business.
c) Which hadith teaching regarding moral qualities did Mr. ''Jarif''s not follow in Fact-1? Explicate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q2d', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, NULL, 'Fact-1: Mr. ''Jarif'' is a rich and influential person in the area. He invites the rich people of the area to various functions at his house and feeds them. The poor people of the area cannot enter Jarif''s house during the functions.
Fact-2: Mr. ''Mahfuz'' keeps his shop open during the call to prayer and conducts business. On the other hand, other businessmen close their shops and go to offer prayers. A business friend of his advised ''Mahfuz'' to offer prayers. In response, Samad said that there is no need for prayers for the progress of business.
d) Identify the Surah in which the lesson isnot reflected in the activity of Mr.''Mahfuz'' in Fact-2 and analyze its results.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q3', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, 3, 'Why is the lesson of Surah Al-Lahab important?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, 4, '''Hadith is the second source of Islamic way of life.'' Explain.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch3-p81-q5', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch3', 81, 5, 'The righteous and perfect never abandon the worship of Allah Almighty? Elucidate.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p83-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 83, NULL, 'State the good effects of Akhlaq-e-Hamidah (good character).'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p83-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 83, NULL, 'Describe the importance of good behaviour.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p84-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 84, NULL, 'Students will work in groups and make a list of the ways of helping people.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p85-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 85, NULL, 'Students will work in groups. Each group will write a poster listing the good impacts of decency and present before the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p86-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 86, NULL, '“The indecent dress and behavior bring about disruption”- Explain'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p87-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 87, NULL, 'Students will work in groups and make a list of deeds related to looking after the creatures.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p89-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 89, NULL, 'Students will work in groups to discuss for making a list of activities of trustworthiness.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p90-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 90, NULL, 'Students will make a list of work they can do themselves and present in the class.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p92-t1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 92, NULL, 'Students will write down small events of forgiveness occurred in their lives and show it to their teachers.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch4-p92-t2', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch4', 92, NULL, 'Describe the importance of forgiveness.'),
