c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p119-q4', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 119, 4, 'Mr. ''Jalal'' is the youngest son in his family. He was forced to leave home due to the oppression of his brothers. ''Janal'' became quite rich by doing business. Due to drought, there was a shortage of food in the country. At this time, when ''Jalal''s brothers came to him for help, he forgave them. His daughter ''Jabiha'' does not send a beggar home empty-handed when he comes. ''Jabiha'' buys books, notebooks and pens for her poor classmates. She does not leave the house without a veil. Despite being the daughter of a rich father, she wears ordinary clothes.
Which scholar''s work is similar to that of Mr. ''Jalal''?
a. Hazrat Ismail (AS)
b. Hazrat Yusuf (AS)
c. Hazrat Usman (RA)
d. Hazrat Ali (RA)'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p119-q5', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 119, 5, 'Mr. ''Jalal'' is the youngest son in his family. He was forced to leave home due to the oppression of his brothers. ''Janal'' became quite rich by doing business. Due to drought, there was a shortage of food in the country. At this time, when ''Jalal''s brothers came to him for help, he forgave them. His daughter ''Jabiha'' does not send a beggar home empty-handed when he comes. ''Jabiha'' buys books, notebooks and pens for her poor classmates. She does not leave the house without a veil. Despite being the daughter of a rich father, she wears ordinary clothes.
If you follow the work of the Muslim scholar whose work is similar to that of ''Jabiha'', you will –
i. Be patient
ii. Be adorned with a leadership position in the society
iii. Be granted the mercy of Allah
Which one is correct?
a. i & ii
b. i & iii
c. ii & iii
d. i & ii & iii'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p120-q1', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 120, 1, 'Why was Hazrat Ismail (AS) given the title of ''Sadaqul Waad''?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p120-q1a', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 120, NULL, 'Scenario-1: During the dry season, the canals in Bhasanchar Union dry up. This causes difficulties for the farmers in their cultivation. Mr. ''A'', a wealthy man of the area, installs ten deep tube wells. When there is a shortage in the village due to drought, Mr. ''A'' distributes twenty kilograms of rice to each family.
Scenario-2 : A dispute arises between the residents of two neighboring villages over a trivial incident. At the height of the dispute, a meeting is held with ten members from each village under the mediation of Mr. ''B'', a prominent son of the neighboring village. A 12-point agreement is signed at the meeting. This ends the hostilities between the two villages.
a. What is the Treaty of Hudaybiyah?'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p120-q1b', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 120, NULL, 'Scenario-1: During the dry season, the canals in Bhasanchar Union dry up. This causes difficulties for the farmers in their cultivation. Mr. ''A'', a wealthy man of the area, installs ten deep tube wells. When there is a shortage in the village due to drought, Mr. ''A'' distributes twenty kilograms of rice to each family.
Scenario-2 : A dispute arises between the residents of two neighboring villages over a trivial incident. At the height of the dispute, a meeting is held with ten members from each village under the mediation of Mr. ''B'', a prominent son of the neighboring village. A 12-point agreement is signed at the meeting. This ends the hostilities between the two villages.
b. Explain the statement ''I am the city of knowledge, and Ali (RA) is its gate''.'),
  ('class7-islam-en-ch5-p120-q1c', 'class7-islam-en', 'class7-islam-en-ch5', 120, NULL, 'Scenario-1: During the dry season, the canals in Bhasanchar Union dry up. This causes difficulties for the farmers in their cultivation. Mr. ''A'', a wealthy man of the area, installs ten deep tube wells. When there is a shortage in the village due to drought, Mr. ''A'' distributes twenty kilograms of rice to each family.
