  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e15', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 15, 'Solve: (3y + 1)/5 = (3y − 7)/3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e16', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 16, 'Solve: (x + 1)/2 − (x − 2)/3 − (x − 3)/5 = 2'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e17', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 17, 'Solve: 2(x + 3) = 10'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e18', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 18, 'Solve: 5(x − 2) = 3(x − 4)'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e19', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 19, 'Solve: 7(3 − 2y) + 5(y − 1) = 34'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 2, 'Solve: 5x − 3 = 2x + 3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e20', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 20, 'Solve: (z − 1)(z + 2) = (z + 4)(z − 2)'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 3, 'Solve: 3y + 1 = 7y − 1'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 4, 'Solve: 7y − 5 = y − 1'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 5, 'Solve: 17 − 2z = 3z + 2'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 6, 'Solve: 13z − 5 = 3 − 2z'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e7', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 7, 'Solve: x/4 = 1/3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e8', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 8, 'Solve: x/2 + 1 = 3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-e9', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 9, 'Solve: x/3 + 5 = x/2 + 7'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 1, 'Solve: 2x − 1 = 0'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 2, 'Solve: x/2 + 1 = 3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p120-t3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 120, 3, 'Solve: 4(y − 3) = 8'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p121-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 121, 1, 'Form the equations by the given information: If 25 is subtracted from five times of a number x, the difference will be 190. — Equation: □'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p121-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 121, 3, 'Form the equations by the given information: Length of a rectangular pond is x metre, breadth is 3 metres less than the length and perimeter of the pond is 26 metres. — Equation: □'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 1, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: What is the number, if 5 is added to its twice, the sum will be 25?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e10', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 10, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: A fruit seller has some fruits of which 1/2 portion is apple, 1/3 portion is orange and 40 mangoes. How many fruits are there in total?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e11', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 11, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: The present age of a father is 6 times of the present age of his son. After 5 years, sum of their ages will be 45 years. What are the present ages of father and son?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e12', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 12, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Ratio of the ages of Sara and Saba is 2 : 3. If the sum of their ages is 30 years, what are their individual age?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e13', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 13, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: In a cricket match the total number of runs scored by Imon and Sumon was 58. Number of Imon''s run was 5 runs less than twice the number of Sumon''s run. What was the number of runs scored by Imon in that game?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e14', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 14, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: A train moving with the speed of 30 km per hour travelled from Kamalapur station to Narayangonj station. If the speed of the train was 25 km per hour, it would take 10 minutes more for the journey. What is the distance between the two stations?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 2, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: What is the number, if 27 is subtracted from it, the difference will be −21?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 3, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Of what number one-third will be equal to 4?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 4, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: What is the number, if 5 is subtracted from it, 5 times the difference will be equal to 20?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 5, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: What is the number if one-third of it is subtracted from its half, the difference will be 6?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 6, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Sum of three consecutive natural numbers is 63; find the numbers.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e7', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 7, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Sum of two numbers is 55 and 5 times the larger number is equal to 6 times of the smaller number. Determine the two numbers.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e8', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 8, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Deena, Meena and Rina together have 180 taka. Deena has 6 taka less and Rina has 12 taka more than that of Meena. How much money does each of them have?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p125-e9', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 125, 9, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: Total price of an exercise book and a pen is 75 taka. If the price of the exercise book would be less by 5 taka and the price of the pen be more by 2 taka, price of the exercise book would be twice the price of the pen. What are the prices of the exercise book and the pen?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p126-e15', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 126, 15, 'Form equations from the following problems and solve: The length of a rectangular land is thrice its breadth and the perimeter of the land is 40 metres. Determine the length and breadth of the land.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p128-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 128, NULL, 'From the graph, find the co-ordinates of the points Q, R, S, T. [Figure: graph paper with XOX′ horizontal axis and YOY′ vertical axis, origin O; point S in the first quadrant, point T in the second quadrant, point Q in the third quadrant, point R in the fourth quadrant.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 1, 'Which one of the following is the root of the equation x/3 − 3 = 0? −9 −3 3 9'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 2, 'What is the number of which one-fourth is equal to 4? (a) 16 (b) 4 (c) 1/4 (d) 1/16'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 3, 'If which quadrant is the position of the point (2, −2)? (a) First (b) Second (c) Third (d) Fourth'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 4, 'What is the abscissa of the point along the y-axis? (a) 0 (b) 1 (c) x (d) y'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 5, 'The difference between two numbers is y. If the larger number is z, what is the smaller number? (a) z − y (b) z + y (c) −y − z (d) −z + y'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 1, 'Draw the graphs of the solution of the following equations: 2x − 1 = 0'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p130-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 130, 2, 'Draw the graphs of the solution of the following equations: 3x + 5 = 2'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e10', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 10, 'By plotting the following points on graph paper join them successively as directed by arrow-heads and give the geometric name of the figures: (a) (2, 2) → (6, 2) → (6, 6) → (2, 2) (b) (0, 0) → (−6, −6) → (8, 6) → (0, 0)'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e11', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 11, 'Solve and show the solutions in graphs: (a) x − 4 = 0 (b) 2x + 4 = 0 (c) x + 3 = 8 (d) 2x + 1 = x − 3 (e) 3x + 4 = 5x'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e12a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, NULL, 'Himu and Sumon went to the market with 475 Taka and bought a notebook and a pen for 75 Taka. The price of a pen is 1/4th of the price of a notebook. They divide the remaining money in the ratio 2 : 3. (a) Determine the number from whose double if 3 is subtracted, the result will be 5.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e12b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, NULL, 'Himu and Sumon went to the market with 475 Taka and bought a notebook and a pen for 75 Taka. The price of a pen is 1/4th of the price of a notebook. They divide the remaining money in the ratio 2 : 3. (b) Determine the price of the pen.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e12c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, NULL, 'Himu and Sumon went to the market with 475 Taka and bought a notebook and a pen for 75 Taka. The price of a pen is 1/4th of the price of a notebook. They divide the remaining money in the ratio 2 : 3. (c) Determine how much money Himu and Sumon each will get.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 6, 'Which of the following is the equivalant fraction of (ab)/(xy)? (a) (abc)/(xyz) (b) (a²b)/(x²y) (c) (2ab)/(2xy) (d) (ab²)/(xy²)'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e7', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 7, 'What is the power of the equation 3x + 1 = 0? (a) −1/3 (b) 1/3 (c) 1 (d) 3'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e8', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 8, 'With which number does addition of −5 equal to 15? (a) −20 (b) 10 (c) −10 (d) 20'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p131-e9', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 131, 9, 'What value of x satisfies the equation of 4x + 1 = 2x + 7? (a) 0 (b) 2 (c) 3 (d) 4'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, 1, 'Length of three sides of a triangle are (x + 1) cm., (x + 2) cm. and (x + 3) cm. (x > 0). If the perimeter of the triangle is 15 cm., what is the value of x? (a) 3 cm. (b) 6 cm. (c) 8 cm. (d) 9 cm.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, 2, 'Based on the information below, answer Questions 2 & 3: 2x − 5 = −x + 4 is an equation and (2, −1) is a point. What is the solution to the equation? (a) 1 (b) 2 (c) 3 (d) 4'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, 3, 'Based on the information below, answer Questions 2 & 3: 2x − 5 = −x + 4 is an equation and (2, −1) is a point. (2, −1) is a point so that – i. the x-coordinate of the point is 2 ii. the point lies in the fourth quadrant iii. the point lies on the graph of 2x − 5. Which of the following is correct? (a) i & ii (b) i & iii (c) ii & iii (d) i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q4a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(3y − 2)/5 + (y + 7)/4 = (y + 1)/10 and 3x − 1 = x + 1 are two equations. (a) If the sum of 2 added to any positive number is 9, find the number.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q4b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(3y − 2)/5 + (y + 7)/4 = (y + 1)/10 and 3x − 1 = x + 1 are two equations. (b) Solve the first equation to find the value of y.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q4c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(3y − 2)/5 + (y + 7)/4 = (y + 1)/10 and 3x − 1 = x + 1 are two equations. (c) Solve the second equation using a graph.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q5a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(a) If the sum of two consecutive positive integers is 21, find the larger number.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q5b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(b) If (x + 2)/5 − (3 − x)/5 = 1 then, find the value of x.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q5c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(c) A daughter''s age is one-third of her mother''s age and their total age is 48 years. Find the mother''s age.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch7-p132-q5d', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch7', 132, NULL, '(d) The perimeter of a pond is 34 metres. If its width is 7 metres less than its length, find the width.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p135-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 135, NULL, '1. (a) Name the pairs of angles in each figure. [Figure: three separate figures; each with two straight lines and a transversal; first figure has angles 1 and 2 marked, second figure has angles 3 and 4 marked, third figure has angles 5 and 6 marked.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p135-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 135, NULL, '1. (b) Identify the corresponding angles of ∠3 and ∠6. [Figure: three separate figures; each with two straight lines and a transversal; first figure has angles 1 and 2 marked, second figure has angles 3 and 4 marked, third figure has angles 5 and 6 marked.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p135-t3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 135, NULL, '1. (c) Identify the vertical opposite angle of ∠4 and the angle supplementary to ∠1. [Figure: three separate figures; each with two straight lines and a transversal; first figure has angles 1 and 2 marked, second figure has angles 3 and 4 marked, third figure has angles 5 and 6 marked.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p136-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 136, 1, 'On a ruled sheet of paper draw two parallel lines and a transversal as like as the figure below. Identify two pairs of corresponding angles. Verify whether each pair of corresponding angles are equal. Are they really equal? [Figure: ruled sheet with two parallel lines l and m and a transversal t; angles 1 and 2 marked on the left figure, angles 3 and 4 marked on the right figure.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p136-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 136, 2, 'Identify two pairs of alternate angles. Verify whether each pair of corresponding angles are equal. Are they really equal? [Figure: ruled sheet with two parallel lines l and m and a transversal t; angles 1 and 2 marked on the left figure, angles 3 and 4 marked on the right figure.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p136-t3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 136, 3, 'Measure the pair of interior angles on the same side of the transversal. Find the sum of the two angles. Compare the sum with the sum done by your peers. Is your sum around 180°? [Figure: ruled sheet with two parallel lines l and m and a transversal t; angles 1 and 2 marked on the left figure, angles 3 and 4 marked on the right figure.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p137-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 137, 1, 'Prove that when a transversal cuts two parallel straight lines, the sum of interior angles on the same side of the transversal is two right angles.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p138-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 138, 1, 'Take two points on a straight line. Draw two 60° angles at these points in the same direction. Verify whether the drawn sides of the angles are parallel.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p138-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 138, 2, 'Find the value of angles made by the transversals. [Figure: two figures, each with two parallel lines and a transversal; first figure has a 40° angle marked, second figure has 70° and 100° angles marked.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, 1, 'In the figure ∠PQR = 55°, ∠LRN = 90° and PQ ∥ MR. Which one of the following is the value of ∠MRN? (a) 35° (b) 45° (c) 55° (d) 90° [Figure: Q—R—L straight line, triangle PQR with vertex P, RN vertical, RM slant; ∠PQR = 55°, ∠LRN = 90°, PQ ∥ MR.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, 2, 'In the figure, if PQ ∥ SR, PQ = PR and ∠PRQ = 50°, what is the value of ∠LRS? (a) 80° (b) 75° (c) 55° (d) 50° [Figure: Q—R—L straight line, triangle PQR with vertex P, RS slant from R; PQ ∥ SR, PQ = PR, ∠PRQ = 50°.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e3i', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD ∥ EF. Based on the given information answer questions (i), (ii) and (iii). [Figure: three horizontal parallel lines AB, CD, EF with a slanting transversal; 45° marked at AB, y marked at CD, x and 32° and z marked at EF.] (i) Which one of the following is the value of ∠x? (a) 28° (b) 32° (c) 45° (d) 58°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e3ii', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD ∥ EF. Based on the given information answer questions (i), (ii) and (iii). [Figure: three horizontal parallel lines AB, CD, EF with a slanting transversal; 45° marked at AB, y marked at CD, x and 32° and z marked at EF.] (ii) Which one of the following is the value of ∠z? (a) 58° (b) 103° (c) 122° (d) 148°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e3iii', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD ∥ EF. Based on the given information answer questions (i), (ii) and (iii). [Figure: three horizontal parallel lines AB, CD, EF with a slanting transversal; 45° marked at AB, y marked at CD, x and 32° and z marked at EF.] (iii) Which one of the following is the value of y − z? (a) 58° (b) 77° (c) 103° (d) 122°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p139-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 139, 4, 'What is meant by ≅ (a) Equal (b) congruent (c) Parallel (d) Perpendicular'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, 5, 'Answer to the questions no. 5 & 6 based on the following figure. [Figure: two intersecting lines crossing a horizontal line; 105°, x, y and 55° angles marked.] x = ? (a) 75° (b) 55° (c) 50° (d) 45°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, 6, 'Answer to the questions no. 5 & 6 based on the following figure. [Figure: two intersecting lines crossing a horizontal line; 105°, x, y and 55° angles marked.] x + y = ? (a) 160° (b) 125° (c) 100° (d) 85°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-e7a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD, ∠BPE = 60° and PQ = PR. [Figure: AB ∥ CD, transversal E–F crossing at P and Q, triangle PQR with vertex P on AB and base QR on CD; ∠BPE = 60°, PQ = PR.] (a) Show that 1/2 ∠APE = 60°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-e7b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD, ∠BPE = 60° and PQ = PR. [Figure: AB ∥ CD, transversal E–F crossing at P and Q, triangle PQR with vertex P on AB and base QR on CD; ∠BPE = 60°, PQ = PR.] (b) Determine the value of ∠CQF'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-e7c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, NULL, 'In the figure, AB ∥ CD, ∠BPE = 60° and PQ = PR. [Figure: AB ∥ CD, transversal E–F crossing at P and Q, triangle PQR with vertex P on AB and base QR on CD; ∠BPE = 60°, PQ = PR.] (c) Prove that, PQR is an equilateral triangle.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-q1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, 1, 'If ∠B + ∠C = 90°, then in ΔABC, ∠A = ? (a) 90° (b) 110° (c) 120° (d) 160°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p140-q2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 140, 2, 'In the adjacent figure, AB ∥ CD, and line segment PQ intersects AB and CD at points R and S respectively. According to the figure – i. ∠PRB corresponds to ∠RSD ii. ∠ARS is alternate to ∠RSD iii. ∠CSQ + ∠CSR = 180°. Which of the following is correct? (a) i & ii (b) i & iii (c) ii & iii (d) i, ii & iii [Figure: AB ∥ CD, line segment PQ intersecting AB and CD at points R and S respectively.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, 3, 'Answer to the questions no. 3 & 4 based on the following figure. AB ∥ CD. [Figure: AB ∥ CD, transversal PQ intersecting at E and F, a 50° angle marked.] What is the measurement of ∠PEA? (a) 40° (b) 50° (c) 90° (d) 130°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, 4, 'Answer to the questions no. 3 & 4 based on the following figure. AB ∥ CD. [Figure: AB ∥ CD, transversal PQ intersecting at E and F, a 50° angle marked.] What is the measurement of ∠EFD? (a) 30° (b) 40° (c) 50° (d) 90°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q5a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, 'In the figure, PQ ∥ RS and AB is their transversal. [Figure: PQ ∥ RS with transversal AB intersecting at E and F.] (a) If the complement of ∠x is 25°, find the value of ∠x.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q5b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, 'In the figure, PQ ∥ RS and AB is their transversal. [Figure: PQ ∥ RS with transversal AB intersecting at E and F.] (b) Prove that ∠PEF = ∠EFS.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q5c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, 'In the figure, PQ ∥ RS and AB is their transversal. [Figure: PQ ∥ RS with transversal AB intersecting at E and F.] (c) Show that ∠PEF + ∠EFR = 180°.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q6a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, '(a) BC and DE are two parallel straight lines intersected by line segment PQ at points L and M respectively. Draw a figure and identify a pair of alternate interior angles formed at points L and M.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q6b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, '(b) If line PQ intersects line segment AB at point B, draw a figure and identify the pair of adjacent angles formed at the point of intersection.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch8-p141-q6c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch8', 141, NULL, '(c) If AC and BD are two parallel straight lines intersected by line segment LM at points P and Q respectively, draw a figure and calculate the sum of the interior angles on the right side of the transversal BM.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p143-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 143, 1, 'How many medians does a triangle have? How many altitudes?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p143-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 143, 2, 'Do a median and an altitude lie entirely in the interior of the triangle?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p143-t3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 143, 3, 'Draw a triangle whose altitude and median are on the same line segment.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p143-t4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 143, 1, 'Draw a triangle. Cut out the three angles. Rearrange them as shown in Fig (ii). The three angles now constitute one angle. This angle is a straight angle and measures 180°. Thus, the sum of the measures of the three angles of a triangle is 180°. [Figure: (i) a triangle with angles 1, 2, 3 marked; (ii) the three cut angles rearranged to form one straight angle.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p144-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 144, 2, 'Draw a triangle and make two copies of it. Arrange the three copies as shown in the figure. What do you observe about three angles seen together? Do they make a straight angle? [Figure: three copies of triangle ABC with angles 1, 2, 3, arranged together so the three angles form a straight angle.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p144-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 144, 3, 'Draw any three triangles in your notebook according to your choice. Use your protractor and measure each of the angles of these triangles. Tabulate your results; one is done for you. In ΔABC: ∠A = 60°, ∠B = 65°, ∠C = 55°, ∠A + ∠B + ∠C = 180°. Do you find that the sum of the three angles always gives around 180°?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p145-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 145, 1, 'Determine the value of ∠ABD, ∠CBD and ∠BCD. [Figure: right-angled triangle ABC, right angle at B, angle 48° at A, point D on AC, BD perpendicular to AC.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p145-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 145, 2, 'The vertical angle of an isosceles triangle is 50°. Find value of the other two angles.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p146-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 146, 3, 'Prove that the sum of the angles of a quadrilateral is equal to 4 right angles.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p146-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 146, 4, 'The two line segments PQ and RS intersect at O and L, M, E, F are four points on them such that LM ⊥ RS, EF ⊥ PQ. Prove that ∠MLO = ∠FEO.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p146-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 146, 5, 'In the triangle ΔABC, AC ⊥ BC; E is a point on AC produced. ED ⊥ AB is drawn to meet BC at O. Prove that ∠CEO = ∠DBO.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p146-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 146, 1, 'Draw an angle. Take two points on both the sides at equal distance from the vertex. Join the two points and obtain an isosceles triangle. Now measure the base angles with a protractor. Are the two angles equal?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p147-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 147, 1, 'Draw any three triangles. Measure the lengths of the sides of each triangle with a ruler and also the angles with a protractor and complete the table. In ΔABC: AB = 3cm, BC = 4cm, CA = 6cm, A = 60°, B = 75°, C = 45°, AC > BC > AB or AB < BC < AC, ∠B > ∠A > ∠C or ∠C < ∠A < ∠B. In each case, compare any two sides and their opposite angles. What conclusion can you draw?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p148-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 148, 1, 'Collect 15 sticks of different lengths. Try to construct a triangle with any three of them. Are you successful in all of your attempts? If not, explain.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p148-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 148, 2, 'Draw any three triangles ΔABC, ΔPQR and ΔXYZ. Measure the lengths of the sides of the triangles by a ruler and complete the table (AB − BC < CA, BC − CA < AB, CA − AB < BC, and similarly for ΔPQR and ΔXYZ). [Figure: (i) triangle ABC, (ii) triangle PQR, (iii) right-angled triangle XYZ.] '),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p149-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 149, NULL, 'In which of the following cases it is possible to draw a triangle—explain. 1. 1cm, 2cm and 3cm 2. 1cm, 2cm and 4cm 3. 4cm, 3cm and 4cm'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 1, 'Answer the questions 1-3 on the basis of the following information: In the figure, CE is the bisector of ∠ACD. AB ∥ CE and ∠ECD = 60°. [Figure: triangle ABC with BC produced to D, CE the bisector of ∠ACD, AB ∥ CE, ∠ECD = 60°.] Which one of the following is the value of ∠BAC? (a) 30° (b) 45° (c) 60° (d) 120°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e10a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, NULL, 'In the ΔABC, ∠ABC > ∠ACB. D is the mid point on BC. (a) Draw the figure on the basis of the information.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e10b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, NULL, 'In the ΔABC, ∠ABC > ∠ACB. D is the mid point on BC. (b) Show that, AC > AB.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e10c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, NULL, 'In the ΔABC, ∠ABC > ∠ACB. D is the mid point on BC. (c) Prove that, AB + AC > 2AD.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e11', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 11, 'In the ΔABC, AB = AC and D is a point on AC. Prove that AB > AD.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e12', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 12, 'In the ABC, AB ⊥ AC and D is a point on AC. Prove that, BC > BD.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e13', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 13, 'Prove that the hypotenuse of a right angled triangle is the greatest side.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 2, 'Answer the questions 1-3 on the basis of the following information: In the figure, CE is the bisector of ∠ACD. AB ∥ CE and ∠ECD = 60°. [Figure: triangle ABC with BC produced to D, CE the bisector of ∠ACD, AB ∥ CE, ∠ECD = 60°.] Which one of the following is the value of ∠ACD? (a) 60° (b) 90° (c) 120° (d) 180°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 3, 'Answer the questions 1-3 on the basis of the following information: In the figure, CE is the bisector of ∠ACD. AB ∥ CE and ∠ECD = 60°. [Figure: triangle ABC with BC produced to D, CE the bisector of ∠ACD, AB ∥ CE, ∠ECD = 60°.] What type of triangle is ABC? (a) obtuse-angled (b) Isosceles (c) Equilateral (d) Right-angled'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 4, 'The lengths of two sides of a triangle are 5 cm. and 4 cm respectively. Which one of the following is the possible measurement of the other side of the triangle? (a) 1 cm. (b) 4 cm. (c) 9 cm. (d) 10 cm.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 5, 'If one of the two acute angles of a right angled triangle is 40°, which of the following is the value of the other acute angle? (a) 40° (b) 45° (c) 60° (d) 140°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 6, 'If the sum of two angles is equal to the third angle of a triangle, what type of triangle is it? (a) Equilateral (b) Acute-angled (c) Right-angled (d) Obtuse-angled'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e7', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 7, 'In the ΔABC, AB > AC and the bisectors of the ∠B and ∠C intersect at the point P. Prove that PB > PC.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e8', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 8, 'ABC is an isosceles triangle and AB = AC. The side BC is extended up to D. Prove that AD > AB.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p151-e9', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 151, 9, 'In the quadrilateral ABCD, AB = AD, BC = CD and CD > AD. Prove that ∠DAB > ∠BCD.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p152-e14', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 152, 14, 'Prove that to the angle opposite to the greatest side of a triangle is also the greatest angle of that triangle.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p152-e15a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 152, NULL, 'In the figure, if, ∠QPM = ∠RPM and ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm. [Figure: right-angled triangle QPR, right angle at P, point M on QR, PM perpendicular to QR; ∠QPM = ∠RPM, ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm.] a) Find the value of ∠QPM.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p152-e15b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 152, NULL, 'In the figure, if, ∠QPM = ∠RPM and ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm. [Figure: right-angled triangle QPR, right angle at P, point M on QR, PM perpendicular to QR; ∠QPM = ∠RPM, ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm.] b) What are the values of ∠PQM and ∠PRM?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p152-e15c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 152, NULL, 'In the figure, if, ∠QPM = ∠RPM and ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm. [Figure: right-angled triangle QPR, right angle at P, point M on QR, PM perpendicular to QR; ∠QPM = ∠RPM, ∠QPR = 90°, PQ = 6 cm.] c) Find the value of PR.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p153-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 153, 1, 'Construct a triangle with side length of 8 cm, 5 cm. and 6 cm.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p153-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 153, 2, 'Try to construct a triangle with side lenght of 12 cm, 5 cm, and 3 cm. Are you successful in drawing the triangle?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p155-t1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 155, 1, 'Construct a triangle with a side of length 7 cm and adjoining angles 50° and 60°.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p155-t2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 155, 2, 'Try to construct a triangle with a side of length 6 cm and adjoining angles 140° and 70°. Can you draw the triangle? Explain why.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 1, 'If two sides of a triangle and one angle opposite to one of the sides are given, then how many triangles can be drawn? (a) 1 (b) 2 (c) 3 (d) 4'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e10', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 10, 'Two sides and an angle opposite to the first side are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 5 cm, 6 cm and 60° (b) 4 cm, 5 cm and 30°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 2, 'When is it possible to draw a triangle when the lengths of the sides are respectively – (a) 1 cm, 2 cm, 3 cm (b) 3 cm, 4 cm, 5 cm. (c) 2 cm, 4 cm, 6 cm. (d) 3 cm, 4 cm, 7 cm.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 3, 'What is the sum of length of the three sides of triangle called? (a) Area (b) Volume (c) Length (d) Perimeter'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 4, 'How many internal angles are there of triangle? (a) 1 (b) 2 (c) 3 (d) 4'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e5', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 5, 'If one angle of a right angled triangle is 60°, how much degree in the other angle? (a) 30° (b) 60° (c) 90° (d) 180°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e6', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 6, 'The lengths of three sides of a triangle are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 3 cm, 4 cm and 6 cm (b) 3.5 cm, 4.7 cm and 5.6 cm'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e7', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 7, 'The lengths of two sides and the angle included between these sides are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 3 cm, 4 cm and 60° (b) 3.8 cm, 4.7 cm and 45°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e8', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 8, 'The length of a side and two of its adjoining angles are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 5 cm, 30° and 45° (b) 4.5 cm, 45° and 60°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p158-e9', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 158, 9, 'Two angles and a side opposite to the first angle are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 120°, 30° and 5 cm (b) 60°, 30° and 4 cm'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e11', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, 11, 'The lengths of the hypotenuse and other one side of a right-angled triangle are given. Construct the triangle. (a) 7 cm and 4 cm (b) 4 cm and 3 cm'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e12', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, 12, 'A side of a right-angled triangle is 5 cm and one of the acute angles is 45°. Construct the triangle.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e13a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'There are three points A, B and C which are not collinear. (a) Draw a triangle through the three points.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e13b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'There are three points A, B and C which are not collinear. (b) Draw perpendicular from the vertex to the base of the drawn triangle.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e13c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'There are three points A, B and C which are not collinear. (c) If the base of the drawn triangle is the hypotenuse of right angled isosceles triangle, then draw the triangle.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e14a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two sides a = 3 cm, b = 4 cm and an angle ∠B = 30° of a triangle are given. (a) Draw an angle equal to ∠B.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e14b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two sides a = 3 cm, b = 4 cm and an angle ∠B = 30° of a triangle are given. (b) Draw a triangle whose two sides are equal to a and b and the included angle is equal to ∠B.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e14c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two sides a = 3 cm, b = 4 cm and an angle ∠B = 30° of a triangle are given. (c) Draw a triangle whose one side is b and the opposite side of ∠B is 2a.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e15a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, '15. [Figure: right-angled triangle ABC, right angle at B.] (a) What is the hypotenuse in the figure?'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e15b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, '15. [Figure: right-angled triangle ABC, right angle at B.] (b) Find the measure the hypotenuse in centimetres and draw an angle equal to the angle ∠ACB.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e15c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, '15. [Figure: right-angled triangle ABC, right angle at B.] (c) Draw a right-angled triangle whose hypotenuse is 2 cm larger than that of the drawn triangle and an angle equal to ∠ACB.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e16a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two parallel straight lines AB and CD and the line PQ intersects AB and CD at E and F respectively. (a) Draw the figure based on information.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e16b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two parallel straight lines AB and CD and the line PQ intersects AB and CD at E and F respectively. (b) Show that, ∠AEP = ∠CFE'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p159-e16c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 159, NULL, 'Two parallel straight lines AB and CD and the line PQ intersects AB and CD at E and F respectively. (c) Prove that, ∠AEF + ∠CFE = 2 right angles'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q1', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, 1, 'How much degree is each of the angles of equilateral triangles? (a) 30° (b) 45° (c) 60° (d) 90°'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q2', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, 2, 'A triangle can be constructed if – i. The lengths of its three sides are given ii. Its three angles are given iii. Two sides and the included angle are given. Which of the following is correct? (a) i & ii (b) i & iii (c) ii & iii (d) i, ii & iii'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q3', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, 3, 'Based on the adjacent figure, answer questions 3 and 4. [Figure: triangle ABC with side BA produced to D.] To draw a line parallel to BA at the point C, equal to which angle is to be constructed? (a) ∠ABC (b) ∠ACB (c) ∠BAC (d) ∠CAD'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q4', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, 4, 'Based on the adjacent figure, answer questions 3 and 4. [Figure: triangle ABC with side BA produced to D.] Which one of the following is equal to ∠CAD? (a) ∠BAC + ∠ACB (b) ∠ABC + ∠ACB (c) ∠ABC + ∠ACB + ∠BAC (d) ∠ABC + ∠BAC'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q5a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, 'The lengths of the three sides of a triangle are: a = 4 cm, b = 5 cm, and c = 6 cm. (a) Draw an equilateral triangle taking b as one of its sides.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q5b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, 'The lengths of the three sides of a triangle are: a = 4 cm, b = 5 cm, and c = 6 cm. (b) With appropriate markings and descriptions, draw a triangle taking a, b and c as the three sides.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q5c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, 'The lengths of the three sides of a triangle are: a = 4 cm, b = 5 cm, and c = 6 cm. (c) Taking a and b as the two sides adjacent to the right angle, draw a right-angled triangle with proper markings and description.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q6a', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, '(a) In an equilateral triangle ΔABC, if side BC is extended to a point D, find the measure of ∠ABD.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q6b', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, '(b) In triangle ΔABC, if AB > BC > AC, arrange the angles in ascending order of their measures.'),
  ('class7-math-en-ch9-p160-q6c', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch9', 160, NULL, '(c) Using a ruler and compass, draw a triangle with side lengths 3 cm, 4 cm, and 5 cm.'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q1', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 1, 'শাস্ত্রীয়সংগীত কাকে বলে?'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q10', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 10, 'আকার মাত্রিক স্বরলিপি পদ্ধতির তালচিহ্নগুলি লেখ।'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q11', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 11, 'ভাতখণ্ডে স্বরলিপি পদ্ধতির তালচিহ্নগুলি লেখ।'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q12', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 12, 'ত্রিতালের তাললিপি লেখ।'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q13', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 13, 'ঝাঁপতালের তাললিপি লেখ।'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q14', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 14, 'তেওড়া তালের তাললিপি লেখ।'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q2', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 2, 'নাদ কাকে বলে? নাদ কত প্রকার?'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q3', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 3, 'শ্রুতি কাকে বলে? শ্রুতি কয়টি?'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q4', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 4, 'পকড় কী?'),
  ('class7-music-bn-ch1-p5-q5', 'class7-music-bn', 'class7-music-bn-ch1', 5, 5, 'তান কাকে বলে?'),
