  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p32-b3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 32, 3, 'Presentation of importance of leaf modifications with reasons.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p32-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 32, 1, 'In which plant Moniliform roots are found? a. Dahlia b. Mango ginger c. Sweet Potato d. Bitter Gourd'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p32-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 32, 2, 'Characteristics of Rhizome are – i. Definite nodes and internodes. ii. Nodes and internodes are compressed. iii. Stay in horizontal position under the soil. Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p33-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 33, 3, 'Follow the stem and answer question number 3 and 4. [Figure: cross-section of an onion bulb, parts labelled M, N, O and P] 3. The functions of the plant marked M are- i. Store foods ii. Protect axillary buds iii. Help in reproduction Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p33-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 33, 4, 'Follow the stem and answer question number 3 and 4. [Figure: cross-section of an onion bulb, parts labelled M, N, O and P] 4. From which parts of the stems do seedlings grow? a. M and N b. N and O c. O and P d. M and P'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p34-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 34, 1, 'Why are potatoes not roots? Explain'),
