  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p34-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 34, 5, 'What are the reasons of root modifications? Explain'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch3-p34-t1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch3', 34, 1, 'Collect Chili plant, grass, a piece of ginger, a piece of turmeric, Oxalis plant, weak stems of arum, cactus and thorn of wood apple. Write down the names of stems of these plants and give reason of your opinion.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p39-b1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 39, 1, 'Observe the breathing of your classmates. Try to do this pressing hard the diaphragm. What happens? Why? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p39-b2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 39, 2, 'Stand up and sit down or run for some time. Count your breathing. You''ll find that the breathing rate will be higher than in resting state. Count breathing per minute of your younger sister and brother.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p42-b3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 42, 3, 'Write down the point of differences between photosynthesis and respiration and present on a poster paper.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p43-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 43, 1, 'Which one is not a organ of respiratory system? a. Skin b. Lenticel c. Guard cell d. Stomata'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p43-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 43, 2, 'Which of the following is usually used for respiration in lower animals? i. gills and skin ii. skin and trachea iii. lungs and gills Which one of the following is correct: a. i b. ii c. i and ii d. i and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p43-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 43, 3, 'See the stem below and answer the question no. 3, 4 and 5: [Figure: trachea and bronchi diagram, parts labelled V (trachea), W (bronchus), X (alveolar wall), Y (alveolus)] 3. What is the name of ''W'' labeled part? a. Alveolus b. Bronchus c. Bronchiole d. Trachea'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p43-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 43, 4, 'See the stem below and answer the question no. 3, 4 and 5: [Figure: trachea and bronchi diagram, parts labelled V (trachea), W (bronchus), X (alveolar wall), Y (alveolus)] 4. In which part of the stem does the exchange of O2 and CO2 occur? a. V b. W c. X d. Y'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p43-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 43, 5, 'See the stem below and answer the question no. 3, 4 and 5: [Figure: trachea and bronchi diagram, parts labelled V (trachea), W (bronchus), X (alveolar wall), Y (alveolus)] 5. Which disease is caussed by the infection of part ''V'' a. Asthma b. Bronchitis c. Pneumonia d. Tuberculosis'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 1, 'What is internal respiration?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human head and lungs, CO2 leaving, O2 entering, dust labelled F, lungs labelled E] a. What is pleura?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human head and lungs, CO2 leaving, O2 entering, dust labelled F, lungs labelled E] b. Pneumonia is a respiratory disease – Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human head and lungs, CO2 leaving, O2 entering, dust labelled F, lungs labelled E] c. Explain the process shown in the diagram.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human head and lungs, CO2 leaving, O2 entering, dust labelled F, lungs labelled E] d. Analyze the remedies of the problem created when ''F'' substance enters into ''E''.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 2, 'What are the causes of pneumonia?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: X — sun, Y — tree, Z — bird] a. What is respiration?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: X — sun, Y — tree, Z — bird] b. How does stomata help in respiration? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: X — sun, Y — tree, Z — bird] c. Which one of ''Y'' and ''Z'' utilizes product of ''X''? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, NULL, '[Figure: X — sun, Y — tree, Z — bird] d. Give a comparative account of the respiration processes of organisms Y and Z.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 3, 'Mention the necessity of respiration.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 4, 'Mention the function of alveoli.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 5, 'Explain respiration in plants and animals.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch4-p44-t1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch4', 44, 1, 'Draw a diagram of respiratory system and label it. Discuss the importance of lungs in respiration.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. Which parts of buccal cavity moved while chewing foods?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. Did the biscuits and dry piece of bread show changes while they are inside the mouth?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. After chewing did any change occur in taste?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. What types of food constituents are there in bread and biscuits?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1e', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. Which parts of your body moved while swallowing foods?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p46-b1f', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 46, NULL, 'This experiment needs two students. Put toast biscuits or a dry piece of bread (boiled potatoes or rice) into the mouth of one student and tell him/her to chew for some time and to keep it inside the mouth without swallowing. Ask the other students to observe these activities. Then the second student will repeat the same activities and the first student will observe the activities of the first student. Now both of them will jointly answer the following questions. After swallowing where does the food go? Observe how it moves.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p47-b2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 47, 2, 'How foods get into stomach: Take one marble and a piece of rubber pipe. Take care that the size of the marble is not bigger than the girth of the pipe. Push the marble into the pipe. Now press at the back side of the marble. It will move forward through the pipe. Similarly food moves forward through the oesophagus. The oesophagus has ring like muscles. These muscles expand and contract. Muscles posterior to food material contract and muscle anterior to food expands. This expansion and contraction is called peristalsis. As a result, food materials gradually reach to the stomach.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p51-b3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 51, 3, 'Students will write names of diseases of digestive system. They will write in groups the causes of these diseases. One from every group will present their findings and other will compare them.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p55-b4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 55, 4, 'Count your friend''s heart beat with the help of your watch.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p55-b5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 55, 5, 'Once Sagar''s father was ill. His elder brother is a physician. He placed his hand on his father''s wrist and was looking at the watch. Sagar noticed it. At night he asked his elder brother what he was examining placing his hand on father''s wrist. What is the name of the vessels on the upper side of the hand? His elder brother told him that he was examining father''s pulse. What is a pulse? Beats created in the artery by alternate expansion and contraction of heart are known as pulse. Artery remains in interior side while veins are on the upper surface of the body. Now examine your friend''s pulse. Observe veins of his hands. Your friend will examine your pulse. Now, you run in your school field for five minutes. Tell your friend to examine your pulse. Do you find any change? Physical labour increases expansion and contraction of the heart that enhances the pulse rate.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p57-b6', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 57, 6, 'Draw a labeled diagram of heart. Show the pathway of blood flow in the heart. Make a chart showing how awareness about heart diseases can be created.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p57-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 57, 1, 'Which one is the largest gland of the body? a. Pancreas b. Intestinal glands c. Gastric gland d. Liver'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a digestive organ, parts labelled Z and Y with a duct] a. What is villus?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a digestive organ, parts labelled Z and Y with a duct] b. Which part of the digestive system does not digest food? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a digestive organ, parts labelled Z and Y with a duct] c. Explain the functions of Y-marked part.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a digestive organ, parts labelled Z and Y with a duct] d. If Z-marked part is damaged, Analyse what are the problems arise in human body?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, 2, 'Which one is available in saliva? a. Ptyalin and water b. Tripsin and water c. Lipase and water d. Amylase and water'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, 3, 'Follow the stem and answer question nos. 3,4,5 [Figure: microscopic view of a blood smear, parts labelled M, N, O and P] 3. Nucleus is absent in- i. M, N ii. N,O iii. O, M Which one of the following is correct? a. i b. ii c. i and ii d. i and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, 4, 'Follow the stem and answer question nos. 3,4,5 [Figure: microscopic view of a blood smear, parts labelled M, N, O and P] 4. Function of P is to— i. carry food extracts ii. act as security guard iii. help expulsion of wastes Which one of the following is correct? a. i and ii b. i and iii c. ii and iii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p58-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 58, 5, 'Follow the stem and answer question nos. 3,4,5 [Figure: microscopic view of a blood smear, parts labelled M, N, O and P] 5. Which one of the following helps blood to clot? a. M b. N c. O d. P'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 1, 'Where and how digested foods are absorbed?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 2, 'Explain the necessity of cleaning teeth.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human heart with blood-flow arrows] a. What is Pericardium?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human heart with blood-flow arrows] b. What is Lipase? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human heart with blood-flow arrows] c. Explain how is blood circulated through the path marked by arrow in the diagram.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, NULL, '[Figure: diagram of a human heart with blood-flow arrows] d. Analyse with reasoning why we should take precautions to keep the organ shown in the stem health.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 3, 'Describe how foods move from the mouth to stomach.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 4, 'Explain the importance of blood cells in your body.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 5, 'What functions do the blood vessels perform in our body?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-t1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 1, 'How would you examine your friend''s pulse? Examine your friend''s pulse after physical exercise. Can you find any change? Explain the causes of these changes.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch5-p59-t2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch5', 59, 2, 'In a group, prepare a chart of the human digestive system and write down the functions against each organ.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p65-b1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 65, 1, 'Find some objects of spherical shape. Make models of water and oxygen molecules from these objects with the help of sticks. Hydrogen atoms form a 104.5° angle with oxygen atom.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p69-b2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 69, 2, 'Demonstration of the use of water as a universal solvent. Necessary Equipment: water, test-tube, different types of matter (for example: common salt, eating soda, testing salt, bit salt, copper sulphate, sugar, vinegar, spirit, vitamin C tablet, glucose etc.) Method: Take about 5 millimeter water in a test-tube. Shake it well by adding some eating salt. Has the salt dissolved in water? Yes, exactly. Now take each and every substance mentioned above and observe whether they are dissolved in the water or not. Every substance or matter is found dissolving. From the mentioned substance normal salt, eating soda, testing salt, bit salt, copper sulphate are the in-organic substances but sugar, vinegar, spirit, vitamin C tablet, glucose are organic substances. So it is proved that water can dissolve organic and innorganic substances. It means water is a universal solvent.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p70-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 70, 1, 'Which one is the molecule of elements? a. H b. Ne c. N d. NO'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p70-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 70, 2, 'Give the answer to the question no. 2 and 3 according to the following stem: [Table: Matter | Symbol | Formula — 1: — | Cl₂; 2: Al | —; 3: — | O₃; 4: — | Br₂; 5: — | NH₃; 6: — | NaOH; 7: Cu | —] 2. Which are the substances of same properties shown through symbols and formula in the above table? a. 2,4 b. 1,3 c. 1,4 d. 2,6'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p70-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 70, 3, 'Give the answer to the question no. 2 and 3 according to the following stem: [Table: Matter | Symbol | Formula — 1: — | Cl₂; 2: Al | —; 3: — | O₃; 4: — | Br₂; 5: — | NH₃; 6: — | NaOH; 7: Cu | —] 3. Which substances have equal atomic number? a. 2,3 b. 3,4 c. 4,5 d. 3,6'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p71-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 71, NULL, 'Three matters and their atomic numbers are mentioned in the following table. [Table: Matter | Number of atoms — 1: H-2, O-1; 2: F-2; 3: C-1, O-2] a. What is molecule'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p71-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 71, NULL, 'Three matters and their atomic numbers are mentioned in the following table. [Table: Matter | Number of atoms — 1: H-2, O-1; 2: F-2; 3: C-1, O-2] b. Why is carbon an element? Describe.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p71-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 71, NULL, 'Three matters and their atomic numbers are mentioned in the following table. [Table: Matter | Number of atoms — 1: H-2, O-1; 2: F-2; 3: C-1, O-2] c. Explain the universality of substance number 1 as a solvent.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p71-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 71, NULL, 'Three matters and their atomic numbers are mentioned in the following table. [Table: Matter | Number of atoms — 1: H-2, O-1; 2: F-2; 3: C-1, O-2] d. Number 2 of the table is an element and Number 3 is a compound. Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, 1, 'Explain which substance is represented by the formula H2O.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, 2, 'What type of substance rust is?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, NULL, '[Figure: Bohr model of an atom, centre 6p and 6n, two shells with electron dots] a. What is atom?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, NULL, '[Figure: Bohr model of an atom, centre 6p and 6n, two shells with electron dots] b. What is the difference between O and O₂.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, NULL, '[Figure: Bohr model of an atom, centre 6p and 6n, two shells with electron dots] c. Putting the required electron in the second orbit, draw a diagram.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, NULL, '[Figure: Bohr model of an atom, centre 6p and 6n, two shells with electron dots] d. Give reasons in favour of the diagram that you have drawn.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch6-p72-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch6', 72, 3, 'Explain the position of protons within an atom.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p81-b1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 81, 1, 'Solar Energy production. Necessary equipment: Magnifying glass / Metal disc. Procedure: At first take a magnifying glass. Usually magnifying glass has convex lens. Focus sunray on a piece of paper using the lens. You will find fire flame up, if you focus the lens correctly. [Figure: magnifying glass focusing sunrays on a piece of paper setting it on fire]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p86-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 86, 1, 'Which one is the source of non-renewable energy? a) Air b) Flow of water c) Solar Energy d) Coal'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p86-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 86, 2, 'Sometimes Atish studies using a charger fan with light. In this regard he uses- i) Light energy ii) Electrical energy iii) Chemical energy Which one is correct from the following? a) i and ii b) ii and iii c) i and iii d) i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p86-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 86, 3, 'Answer the question no 3 and 4 according to the following stem: A gymnast lifts the weight of 200 kg and keeps it down. Then after taking some rest she/he is having food with listening music. 3. Which is the correct energy transformation serial from weight lifting to keeping down? a) Chemical energy → Kinetic energy → Static energy → Kinetic energy b) Kinetic energy → Static energy → Kinetic energy → Sound energy c) Static energy → Kinetic energy → Sound energy → Thermal energy d) Kinetic energy → Static energy → Kinetic energy → Static energy'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, 1, 'What is the main use of nuclearenergy?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'There is no electricity till now in Samiha''s village named Bijoynagar. That is why many of the villagers use solar electricity. She went to Kaptai with her uncle during last Eid vacation and found that electricity was being produced from water also. a) What is the main source of energy?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'There is no electricity till now in Samiha''s village named Bijoynagar. That is why many of the villagers use solar electricity. She went to Kaptai with her uncle during last Eid vacation and found that electricity was being produced from water also. b) Why is natural gas non-renewable energy? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'There is no electricity till now in Samiha''s village named Bijoynagar. That is why many of the villagers use solar electricity. She went to Kaptai with her uncle during last Eid vacation and found that electricity was being produced from water also. c) Explain the method of generating electricity from water seen by Samiha at Kaptai.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'There is no electricity till now in Samiha''s village named Bijoynagar. That is why many of the villagers use solar electricity. She went to Kaptai with her uncle during last Eid vacation and found that electricity was being produced from water also. d) Discuss the suitability of the energy as mentioned in the stem used in Samiha''s village.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, 2, 'What type of energy source is biogas? Explain.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'Now a days Mr. Mumin is producing one kind of gas from the excrement of animal firms. He can sell extra gas after fulfilling the demand of his own firm. a) What is power?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'Now a days Mr. Mumin is producing one kind of gas from the excrement of animal firms. He can sell extra gas after fulfilling the demand of his own firm. b) Describe the necessity of energy transformation.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'Now a days Mr. Mumin is producing one kind of gas from the excrement of animal firms. He can sell extra gas after fulfilling the demand of his own firm. c) Explain what type of energy source the gas produced in the stem.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, NULL, 'Now a days Mr. Mumin is producing one kind of gas from the excrement of animal firms. He can sell extra gas after fulfilling the demand of his own firm. d) Analyze the importance of activities of Mr. Mumin regarding energy conservation.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, 3, 'Mention the reasons of energy crisis.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch7-p87-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch7', 87, 4, 'Answer the question no 3 and 4 according to the following stem: A gymnast lifts the weight of 200 kg and keeps it down. Then after taking some rest she/he is having food with listening music. 4. Which two of the energy are related to having food and listening music of the weight lifter? a) Heat and Sound b) Heat and Electricity c) Chemical and Sound d) Static and Heat'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p89-b1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 89, 1, 'To identify tuneful and tuneless sound. Process: Divide into groups of 5 or 6. Discuss among yourselves and decide which of the various sounds you hear are melodious and which are unmelodious. Make a list of tuneful and tuneless sounds from your discussion. Then anyone of each group present it to the class.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p89-b2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 89, 2, 'To know the cause of sourse of the sound. Required equipment: A metallic pot, some ropes and a stick. Process: Hang the metallic pot (it may be steel or aluminium) with a rope at a suirtable place. Keep it in mind that it does not touch anything. Now strike the pot with a stick. Touch the pot with your finger softly. Do you feel the vibration of the pot? Strike the pot with a stick again and instantly hold the pot tightly. Are you hearing the sound yet? No, you can''t hear. Strike the pot again, you''ll hear the sound. Touch the pot when the sound is stopped. Is the pot vibrating yet? No, it is not vibrating. [Figure: a boy striking a hanging metallic pot]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p90-b3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 90, 3, 'To know the cause of source of sound. Required equipment: A metalic (steel) plate, a spoon, and some water. Process: pour water on the plate. Strike the one edge of the plate with the spoon. Are you hearing sound? Strike the plate once again and touch the plate instantly. Do you feel that the plate is vibrating? Are you hearing the sound yet? No, you don''t hear. Strike the plate again and look at the water. Do you see any wave on water? Do you see any waves in the water? As a result of the plate''s vibration, the water is vibrating, and waves have been created in it. [Figure: steel plate on books with water, struck by a spoon]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p91-b4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 91, 4, 'To know sound does not transmit without medium. Required equipment: A metallic musical instrument, a stick with small diameter, a wide mouthed bottle and a cork. Process: Tie up a musical instrument with thread at one end of the stick. Push the other end of the stick through the cork. Now the full arrangement is pushed into the bottle in such a way that the cork works as a stopper. Tie the rattle to one end of the stick with a thread. Make sure the rattle does not touch the side of the bottle. You will hear the sound of musical instrument from outside. Now open up the cork and keep it at a little height. Now heat the bottle with a burning candle. A lot of air will escape from the bottle for heating. Then tight up the cork of the bottle. Shake the bottle when it is cool. Can you hear a sound? You can hear a little sound. If all the air in the bottle was gone, no sound would be heard. What does it mean? It means sound that cannot be transmitted without medium. [Figure: bottle with a musical instrument inside, heated by a candle]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p91-b5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 91, 5, 'Transmission of sound through liquid. Required equipment: A balloon and some water. Process: Fill the balloon with water. Give your ear to one side of a balloon and scratch the other side of the balloon softly. Are you hearing the scratching sound? You can hear the scratching sound loudly and clearly. [Figure: boy holding a water-filled balloon to his ear]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p92-b6', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 92, 6, 'Circulation of sound through solid. Required equipment: A metallic scale and a long metallic rod. Process: Put an end of scale or rod to your ear and ask your friend to scratch the other end slowly. Are you hearing the sound of scratching? Ask your friends who are standing beside you whether they are hearing sound or not? [Figure: boy holding a metallic rod to his ear while a friend scratches the other end]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p93-b7', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 93, 7, 'How sound vibrations cause the eardrum to vibrate. Required equipment: A tin pot (you can take a piece of soft drink can) and a rubber balloon. Process: Cut the both end of the can. Close one end of the can with the balloon which is tied up tightly with thread or rubber band. Put 4 or 5 grains of wheat or rice on the tightly tied up balloon. Ask your friend to make a sound ''hurrah'', ''hurrah'' in front of the open end of the can. Ovserve carefuully of what happens to the wheat or rice. Why does the wheat or the rice jump up and down? The vibration of sound created by your friend vibrates the balloon. That''s why wheat or rice was jumping. [Figure: tin can with a balloon stretched over one end, grains on top; a boy shouting into the open end]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p94-b8', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 94, 8, 'Point out the causes of sound pollution in your area and note down the causes after discussion. You can make a group of 5-6 persons to do the work.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p95-b9', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 95, 9, 'Observing the variation in sound with the length of an open tube. Required equipment: a straw or tube which is used in drinking, a scissors. Process: Make that tube flat, cut the one end of that tube which will be pointed, blow the cutting end with your mouth. Observe what kind of sound produces. Now cut the other end of the tube and make it shorter. Can you hear the difference of intensity of sound? The intensity of sound is more of the shorter tube. [Figure: boy blowing a straw or tube]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p96-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 96, 1, 'Which medium was a higher velocity of sound? a. Vacuum medium b. Solid medium c. Gaseous medium d. Liquid medium'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p97-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 97, 2, 'Which instrument produces sound with the help of its inside vibration? a. Sitar b. Monochord instrument c. Guitar d. Flute'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p97-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 97, 3, 'Read the passage given below attentively and answer the question no. 3 and 4. The explosions on the surface of the moon and shooting a gun on the surface of the earth, in both cases the flashes of light are seen. 3. To hear the sound of explosion on the surface of the moon from the earth- i. The distance of moon will be less ii. The medium must be in between the earth and the moon iii. The limit and audibility will be 20 to 20000 Hz. Which one is correct? a. i b. ii c. iii d. ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p97-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 97, 4, 'Read the passage given below attentively and answer the question no. 3 and 4. The explosions on the surface of the moon and shooting a gun on the surface of the earth, in both cases the flashes of light are seen. 4. Which one will be observed last if both the incidents take place at a time? a. The sound of gun fire b. The light produced by gun fire c. The sound of explosion d. The light of explosion'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, 1, 'What are the differences between audible and inaudible sound?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The velocity of sound is 330 m/sec (air). The velocity of sound in sea water is 1500m/sec. The man standing on the sea shore and the diver are 3300 meters away from the place of the bomb explosion. [Figure: a person standing on the sea shore, a bomb explosion in the sea, and a diver under water] a. What is sound?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The velocity of sound is 330 m/sec (air). The velocity of sound in sea water is 1500m/sec. The man standing on the sea shore and the diver are 3300 meters away from the place of the bomb explosion. [Figure: a person standing on the sea shore, a bomb explosion in the sea, and a diver under water] b. Why do we hear the sound of railway movement from a distance if you put the ear on the rail?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The velocity of sound is 330 m/sec (air). The velocity of sound in sea water is 1500m/sec. The man standing on the sea shore and the diver are 3300 meters away from the place of the bomb explosion. [Figure: a person standing on the sea shore, a bomb explosion in the sea, and a diver under water] c. After how much time will the man standing on the shore hear the sound from the place of the bomb explosion?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The velocity of sound is 330 m/sec (air). The velocity of sound in sea water is 1500m/sec. The man standing on the sea shore and the diver are 3300 meters away from the place of the bomb explosion. [Figure: a person standing on the sea shore, a bomb explosion in the sea, and a diver under water] d. Will the diver hear the sound of the explosion of the bomb at the same time as well? Give reason in favour of your answer.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, 2, 'What is meant by pre- auditory and post- auditory sound?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The sound of school bell was not heard for a long from Tapan''s house. Recently the shape of the bell has been changed keeping the weight as before. As a result now he can hear the sound of the school bell from his house. a. What is pleasing audible sound?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The sound of school bell was not heard for a long from Tapan''s house. Recently the shape of the bell has been changed keeping the weight as before. As a result now he can hear the sound of the school bell from his house. b. What change will come to the flute if the length of the tube of the flute is lesser?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The sound of school bell was not heard for a long from Tapan''s house. Recently the shape of the bell has been changed keeping the weight as before. As a result now he can hear the sound of the school bell from his house. c. Describe the techniques of reaching sound to Tapan''s ear from the school bell.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, NULL, 'The sound of school bell was not heard for a long from Tapan''s house. Recently the shape of the bell has been changed keeping the weight as before. As a result now he can hear the sound of the school bell from his house. d. What kind of change has been made to the bell for which Tapan can hear the sound from his house? Explain this with appropriate causes.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, 3, 'What are the differences between noise and pleasing sound?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch8-p98-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch8', 98, 4, 'Why cannot hear sounds of all frequencies?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p100-b1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 100, 1, 'First take two glasses. Touch the glasses and feel how cold or hot they are. Now pour hot water into one glass and put pieces of ice in another one. Wait for two minutes. Among the five senses, heat can only be felt by the skin. Now hold and touch the two glass-es by turns. How do you feel of the glasses? One is hot, another is cold. Now you discuss yourself, what does the hot glass contain for which it is hot? Why does the other glass feel cold? What does it have in it or does not have in? Caution: Pour hot water in such a way so that it does not fall on your body. Never touch the hot water pot or glass with your bare hand.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p100-b2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 100, 2, 'Touch a steel glass with your hand. Whether it is hot or cold, keep it in your mind. Now fill the glass with hot water. Now touch the glass after two minutes. You will feel that the glass is becoming hotter gradually. Now empty the water from the glass and touch the glass after a minute. The glass is getting cold. Caution: Pour hot water in such a way so that it does not fall on your body. Never touch hot water pot or glass with your bare hand. You will not hold the glass which is filled up with hot water for a long time.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p101-b3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 101, 3, 'Determination of fever by using thermometer. The normal temperature of human being is 98.4° Fahrenheit. It is called fever when temperature goes beyond that. Measure the temperature of five learners of your class using clinical thermometer and write down them. Decide from these whether anyone feels feverish.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p103-b4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 103, 4, 'Take a Celsius Scale and a Fahrenheit Scale which are used to measure fever. Measure the temperature of your five friends in your class using the Fahrenheit Scale. Using the formula transform the measured temperature into Celsius Scale and fill up the table given below. [Table: columns — Name of learners, Temperature in Fahrenheit Scale, Temperature in Celsius Scale, Remarks; rows — 1., 2.]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p104-b5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 104, 5, 'Proof of expansion of solids. Required equipment: A brass ball, ring, fire and stand. A brass ball and a ring are so made that the ball can simply pass through the ring when it is cold. Insert ring and ball to stand as shown in the figure. Now try to pass the ball through the ring. You will see that the ball has passed through the ring. Now take the ball and heat it. Try to pass the ball through the ring. Is the ball going to pass through the ring? No, it is not passing. Caution: Be careful while working with the hot matters/objects. [Figure: brass ball and ring on a stand]'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p105-b6', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 105, 6, 'Equipment: A glass bottle, two water tubs, hot and cold water, balloon, thread. Take a strong and empty glass bottle. Tie a balloon with a thread to the neck of the bottle. Take boiling water in one tub and cold water in another tub. Now dip the bottle in hot water cautiously. What do you see? The balloon has blown away a little. Now dip the bottle in cold water. Has the balloon soaked? Why is it happening? Caution: Be careful in using boiling water.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p108-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 108, 1, 'Which acts as a well absorber of atmosphere? a. Nitrogen b. Water vapour c. Oxygen d. Dust'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p108-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 108, 2, 'Characteristic of temperature is that it- a. Can be felt b. Can be measured c. Is a kind of energy d. Resists while force is applied'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q1a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Sharmin reads in class seven. One evening she feels feverish. The temperature measured in Celsius Scale is 37°C. Sharmin can understand Fahrenheit Scale temperature instead of Centigrade Scale. Being anxious she goes to a doctor to measure the temperature. The doctor measuring thermometer and finds no fever. a. What is temperature?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q1b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Sharmin reads in class seven. One evening she feels feverish. The temperature measured in Celsius Scale is 37°C. Sharmin can understand Fahrenheit Scale temperature instead of Centigrade Scale. Being anxious she goes to a doctor to measure the temperature. The doctor measuring thermometer and finds no fever. b. Explain the advantage of mercury thermometer.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q1c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Sharmin reads in class seven. One evening she feels feverish. The temperature measured in Celsius Scale is 37°C. Sharmin can understand Fahrenheit Scale temperature instead of Centigrade Scale. Being anxious she goes to a doctor to measure the temperature. The doctor measuring thermometer and finds no fever. c. What was the temperature in Fahrenheit Scale at Sharmin''s body?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q1d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Sharmin reads in class seven. One evening she feels feverish. The temperature measured in Celsius Scale is 37°C. Sharmin can understand Fahrenheit Scale temperature instead of Centigrade Scale. Being anxious she goes to a doctor to measure the temperature. The doctor measuring thermometer and finds no fever. d. If the temperature increases by 50° on the celsius scale, how much will it increase on the Fahrenheit scale? Explain with reasoning.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q2a', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Anika observes daily activities that happen in his life very carefully. One day he saw that the lid of the cooking pot fell down due to heat. On the other hand she noticed some gaps in their door in winter season where he found no gap in the summer. Both the incidents made her thoughtful. a. Which matter expands more due to heat?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q2b', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Anika observes daily activities that happen in his life very carefully. One day he saw that the lid of the cooking pot fell down due to heat. On the other hand she noticed some gaps in their door in winter season where he found no gap in the summer. Both the incidents made her thoughtful. b. Why is a gap kept between two consecutive rails of a rail line?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q2c', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Anika observes daily activities that happen in his life very carefully. One day he saw that the lid of the cooking pot fell down due to heat. On the other hand she noticed some gaps in their door in winter season where he found no gap in the summer. Both the incidents made her thoughtful. c. Explain the cause of incidents which Anika observed while cooking was going on.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q2d', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, NULL, 'Anika observes daily activities that happen in his life very carefully. One day he saw that the lid of the cooking pot fell down due to heat. On the other hand she noticed some gaps in their door in winter season where he found no gap in the summer. Both the incidents made her thoughtful. d. Analyze the cause of the two behaviour of wooden door which Anika observed during winter and summer season.'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, 3, 'Observe the picture below carefully and answer the questions number 3 and 4: [Figure: Fig. 1 — beaker of liquid with thermometer, 32°C; Fig. 2 — beaker of liquid with thermometer, 86°F] 3. Thermometer as shown in figure 2: (i) Freezing point 32°F (ii) Fundamental division 200°F (iii) Melting point 232°F Which one of the following is correct? a. i b. ii c. i and ii d. i, ii and iii'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p109-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 109, 4, 'Observe the picture below carefully and answer the questions number 3 and 4: [Figure: Fig. 1 — beaker of liquid with thermometer, 32°C; Fig. 2 — beaker of liquid with thermometer, 86°F] 4. In figure 1 and Figure 2 what will happen to liquid with the thermal touch? a. The flow of heat will be from 1 to 2 b. The flow of heat will be from 2 to 1 c. The flow of heat will be continued d. Both temperatures will increase'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p110-q1', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 110, 1, 'What is the difference between heat and temperature?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p110-q2', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 110, 2, 'Why is a gap kept between two consecutive rails of a rail line?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p110-q3', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 110, 3, 'We feel warm by the side of a fire. We feel warmer or hot if we keep our hand over fire. Why does that happen?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p110-q4', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 110, 4, 'Why do we not hold cooking hot pot with bare hand? Why do we use a piece of cloth?'),
  ('class7-science-en-ch9-p110-q5', 'class7-science-en', 'class7-science-en-ch9', 110, 5, 'Why does the pressure of atmosphere decrease when temperature increases?'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p2-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 2, NULL, 'কায়িক শ্রম প্রয়োজন হয় এমন আরও ৫টি উদাহরণ নিজের খাতায় লিখ এবং উদাহরণগুলো বন্ধুদের সাথে মিলিয়ে নাও। প্রয়োজনে শিক্ষকের সাহায্য নিতে পারো।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p5-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 5, NULL, 'প্রথম পর্ব
শিক্ষক কায়িক শ্রমে নিয়োজিত একজন ব্যক্তিকে অতিথি হিসেবে শ্রেণিকক্ষে নিয়ে আসবেন। কায়িক শ্রমে নিয়োজিত ব্যক্তি হতে পারেন—
➢ একজন রিকশাচালক বা ভ্যানচালক
➢ ইট ভাঙা শ্রমিক বা নির্মাণশ্রমিক
➢ খেতমজুর কিংবা দিনমজুর
➢ কায়িক শ্রমে নিযুক্ত অন্য কেউ
শিক্ষার্থীরা তার কাছ থেকে তার জীবনের কথা শুনবে। তিনি কী কাজ করেন, কী খাওয়া-দাওয়া করেন, কোথায় থাকেন, কীভাবে এই কাজে এলেন, তার স্বপ্ন কী ইত্যাদি বিষয় শুনবে। প্রয়োজনে শিক্ষার্থীরা কায়িক শ্রমে নিয়োজিত অতিথিকে বিভিন্ন বিষয়ে প্রশ্ন করবে। শিক্ষক সঞ্চালক হিসেবে শিক্ষার্থীদের প্রশ্ন করতে সাহায্য করবেন। কাজ শেষে শিক্ষক অতিথির উপস্থিতিতেই শিক্ষার্থীদের বুঝিয়ে বলবেন— যদি তিনি তার কাজে কঠোর কায়িক শ্রম না দিতেন তবে আমাদের সামাজিক জীবন কী রকম ঝুঁকির মুখে পড়ত। এভাবে শিক্ষক শিক্ষার্থীদের নিকট কায়িক শ্রমের গুরুত্ব তুলে ধরবেন।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p5-t2', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 5, NULL, 'দ্বিতীয় পর্ব
ক্লাস শেষ করার পূর্বে শিক্ষক শিক্ষার্থীদের কয়েকটি দলে ভাগ করে দিবেন। তবে যদি শিক্ষক মনে করেন তাহলে কাজটি শিক্ষার্থীদের এককভাবেও দিতে পারেন। শিক্ষার্থীদের কেউ কেউ কায়িক শ্রমে নিয়োজিত অতিথির পেশা নির্দেশ করে ছবি আঁকবে, কেউ কেউ গল্প লিখবে, কেউ কেউ কবিতা বা গানও লিখতে পারে। এসব লেখা ও ছবি একসাথে করে একটি দেয়াল পত্রিকা বানিয়ে শ্রেণিকক্ষে প্রদর্শন করতে হবে।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p7-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 7, NULL, '‘মানবসভ্যতা বিকাশে মেধাশ্রমের ভূমিকাই মুখ্য’—এ বিষয়ে বিতর্ক আয়োজন।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p8-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, 'কাজ: ছবি দেখে বলা
নিচের ছবিটি লক্ষ করো। তোমরা কি বলতে পারবে ছবিটি কোন সময়ের? কী ঘটনার পরিচয় বহন করে, কবে ও কোন দেশের এবং ছবিটি দেখে তোমার অনুভূতি কী? তোমার নিজের খাতায় এ প্রশ্নের উত্তর লেখো। শিক্ষক সবার লেখার পর ছবিটির পেছনে যে মেধাশ্রম দেওয়া হয়েছে তার গুরুত্ব ব্যাখ্যা করবেন। ছবিটি থেকে আমরা কী জানতে পারি, ছবিটি না থাকলে আমরা কী জানতে পারতাম না ইত্যাদি ব্যাখ্যা করে শিক্ষার্থীদের বোঝাবেন। (যেমন— ছবিটি না থাকলে আমরা জানতে পারতাম না যে কিশোরেরাও মুক্তিযুদ্ধ করেছে)
[চিত্র: নদীর ধারে তিন তরুণ মুক্তিযোদ্ধার সাদা-কালো ছবি; একজন দাঁড়িয়ে হাত তুলে নির্দেশ দিচ্ছেন, অন্য দুজন রাইফেল হাতে বসে ও হাঁটু গেড়ে আছেন]'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p8-t2', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 8, NULL, 'ছবিটি সম্পর্কে সংক্ষিপ্ত একটি বর্ণনা দাও।
[চিত্র: নদীর ধারে তিন তরুণ মুক্তিযোদ্ধার সাদা-কালো ছবি; একজন দাঁড়িয়ে হাত তুলে নির্দেশ দিচ্ছেন, অন্য দুজন রাইফেল হাতে বসে ও হাঁটু গেড়ে আছেন]'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p9-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 9, NULL, 'তোমার এলাকার/পরিচিত কোনো ব্যক্তির মেধাশ্রমের ব্যাপারে একটি অনুচ্ছেদ লেখো এবং তা শিক্ষককে দেখাও। তোমার লেখা অনুচ্ছেদ তোমার সহপাঠীদের পড়তে দাও, তাদের লেখাটিও তুমি পড়।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p12-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 12, NULL, 'প্রত্যেকে নিজের পরিচিত একজন আত্মবিশ্বাসী মানুষ সম্পর্কে ২-৩ মিনিট কথা বলবে।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p16-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 16, NULL, 'আমরা তো সবাই কমবেশি আত্মবিশ্বাসী, তাই না? এসো আজ আমরা প্রত্যেকে আমাদের নিজেদের জীবন থেকে একটি করে গল্প/ঘটনা লিখব যেখানে আত্মবিশ্বাসের পরিচয় পাওয়া যায়। আমরা কিন্তু আত্মমর্যাদাবান, আর যারা আত্মমর্যাদাবান তারা অন্যের লেখা দেখে লেখে না। যারা নিজে নিজে লেখার চেষ্টা করে না তারা কিন্তু আত্মমর্যাদাবান নয়। লেখা শেষ করে আমরা সবাই মিলে শান্ত হয়ে বসব। শিক্ষক আমাদের একজন একজন করে নিজের লেখা পড়ে শোনাতে বলবেন। আমরা সবাই শিক্ষকের কথা শুনব এবং সে অনুযায়ী কাজ করব। লেখা শেষে আমরা সবাই মিলে আমাদের লেখাগুলো দিয়ে খুব সুন্দর দেয়াল পত্রিকা তৈরি করব। অথবা আমরা আমাদের লেখাগুলো আলাদা আলাদা পৃষ্ঠায় লিখে সেলাই করে বইও বানাতে পারি। শক্ত কাগজের মলাট বানিয়ে তার উপর গমের নাড়া বা রং দিয়ে বইয়ের নাম লিখতে পারি। বইয়ের নাম দিতে পারি— ‘আত্মবিশ্বাসী আমরা’। বিশেষ দ্রষ্টব্য: দেয়াল পত্রিকা তৈরি বা বই বানানোর কাজটি আমরা সবাই মিলে শ্রেণিতে বসে করব। বাড়ির কাজ হিসেবে নেব না বা একজন শিক্ষার্থীর উপর দায়িত্ব দিয়ে সবাই নিজেকে আলগা প্রমাণ করব না।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p19-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 19, NULL, 'এসো প্রত্যেকে ছোট্ট করে একটা অনুচ্ছেদ লেখি। লেখার বিষয়: সৃজনশীল হয়ে আমি কী করতে চাই? লেখা শেষ হলে সবাই নিজের লেখা সবার উদ্দেশে পড়ে শোনাই। সবার লেখা একত্র করে আমরা একটা বইও বানাতে পারি। কীভাবে বই বানাবে: ক্লাসে যাদের হাতের লেখা সুন্দর তারা প্রত্যেকের লেখা আলাদা কাগজে লিখবে, যারা সুন্দর আঁকতে পারে তারা লেখার কাহিনি অনুযায়ী তাতে সুন্দর করে অলংকরণ করবে। এরপর সবগুলো কাগজ এক সাথে করে শক্ত কাগজের মলাট দিয়ে বাঁধাই করে নিবে। মলাটের উপর বইয়ের নাম দিয়ে সুন্দর প্রচ্ছদও এঁকে দিতে পারো।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p20-t1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 20, NULL, 'উপরের ছবিগুলো থেকে যেকোনো একটি ছবি বেছে নাও। ছবির বস্তুটি সম্পর্কে নিজ নিজ খাতায় ১০-১২টি বাক্যের একটি অনুচ্ছেদ লেখো। অনুচ্ছেদের নিচে তুমি ঐ বস্তুর ছবি আঁকো এবং তাতে রং করো।
[চিত্র: বাম কলামে একটি পাতা, একটি টেবিল ল্যাম্প, একটি গাড়ি ও একটি বালিশ; ডান কলামে একটি বৈদ্যুতিক বাল্ব, একটি খাট, একটি গাছ ও একটি টায়ার]'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q1', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, 1, 'কোনটি মেধাশ্রমের উদাহরণ?
ক. চীনের মহাপ্রাচীর নির্মাণ
খ. আগ্রার তাজমহল তৈরি
গ. সাইকেল-রিকশা চালানো
ঘ. মোটরগাড়ি আবিষ্কার'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q1a', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, NULL, 'পোলিও রোগে আক্রান্ত শিশু খলিলুর রহমানকে কবিরাজ দেখায় তার মা বাবা। কবিরাজের ভুল চিকিৎসায় শারীরিক প্রতিবন্ধী হয়ে যায় দুই বছরের শিশু খলিল। প্রতিবেশী ও আত্মীয়স্বজনের অনেকেই তাকে বোঝা হিসেবে মনে করত এবং তাকে ভিক্ষাবৃত্তিতে লাগিয়ে দেওয়ার পরামর্শ দিত। কিন্তু তার মা বাবা তাদের পরামর্শ না শুনে তাকে স্কুলে পড়ালেখা শুরু করালেন। খলিল পড়ালেখায় আনন্দ খুঁজে পায় এবং চেষ্টা অব্যাহত রাখে। সকল বাধা অতিক্রম করে খলিল আজ বিশ্ববিদ্যালয়ের হিসাববিজ্ঞান বিভাগের শেষ বর্ষের শিক্ষার্থী।
ক. মেধাশ্রম কী?'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q1b', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, NULL, 'পোলিও রোগে আক্রান্ত শিশু খলিলুর রহমানকে কবিরাজ দেখায় তার মা বাবা। কবিরাজের ভুল চিকিৎসায় শারীরিক প্রতিবন্ধী হয়ে যায় দুই বছরের শিশু খলিল। প্রতিবেশী ও আত্মীয়স্বজনের অনেকেই তাকে বোঝা হিসেবে মনে করত এবং তাকে ভিক্ষাবৃত্তিতে লাগিয়ে দেওয়ার পরামর্শ দিত। কিন্তু তার মা বাবা তাদের পরামর্শ না শুনে তাকে স্কুলে পড়ালেখা শুরু করালেন। খলিল পড়ালেখায় আনন্দ খুঁজে পায় এবং চেষ্টা অব্যাহত রাখে। সকল বাধা অতিক্রম করে খলিল আজ বিশ্ববিদ্যালয়ের হিসাববিজ্ঞান বিভাগের শেষ বর্ষের শিক্ষার্থী।
খ. আত্মমর্যাদাসম্পন্ন হওয়া জরুরি কেন? ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q1c', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, NULL, 'পোলিও রোগে আক্রান্ত শিশু খলিলুর রহমানকে কবিরাজ দেখায় তার মা বাবা। কবিরাজের ভুল চিকিৎসায় শারীরিক প্রতিবন্ধী হয়ে যায় দুই বছরের শিশু খলিল। প্রতিবেশী ও আত্মীয়স্বজনের অনেকেই তাকে বোঝা হিসেবে মনে করত এবং তাকে ভিক্ষাবৃত্তিতে লাগিয়ে দেওয়ার পরামর্শ দিত। কিন্তু তার মা বাবা তাদের পরামর্শ না শুনে তাকে স্কুলে পড়ালেখা শুরু করালেন। খলিল পড়ালেখায় আনন্দ খুঁজে পায় এবং চেষ্টা অব্যাহত রাখে। সকল বাধা অতিক্রম করে খলিল আজ বিশ্ববিদ্যালয়ের হিসাববিজ্ঞান বিভাগের শেষ বর্ষের শিক্ষার্থী।
গ. সামনে এগিয়ে যেতে খলিলুর রহমানের ক্ষেত্রে যে বিষয়টি কাজ করেছে তা বর্ণনা করো।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q1d', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, NULL, 'পোলিও রোগে আক্রান্ত শিশু খলিলুর রহমানকে কবিরাজ দেখায় তার মা বাবা। কবিরাজের ভুল চিকিৎসায় শারীরিক প্রতিবন্ধী হয়ে যায় দুই বছরের শিশু খলিল। প্রতিবেশী ও আত্মীয়স্বজনের অনেকেই তাকে বোঝা হিসেবে মনে করত এবং তাকে ভিক্ষাবৃত্তিতে লাগিয়ে দেওয়ার পরামর্শ দিত। কিন্তু তার মা বাবা তাদের পরামর্শ না শুনে তাকে স্কুলে পড়ালেখা শুরু করালেন। খলিল পড়ালেখায় আনন্দ খুঁজে পায় এবং চেষ্টা অব্যাহত রাখে। সকল বাধা অতিক্রম করে খলিল আজ বিশ্ববিদ্যালয়ের হিসাববিজ্ঞান বিভাগের শেষ বর্ষের শিক্ষার্থী।
ঘ. প্রতিবেশীদের পরামর্শ না শোনার বিষয়ে খলিলুর রহমানের মা-বাবার সিদ্ধান্তের যৌক্তিকতা ব্যাখ্যা করো।'),
  ('class7-worklife-bn-ch1-p21-q2', 'class7-worklife-bn', 'class7-worklife-bn-ch1', 21, 2, 'যাঁরা আত্মবিশ্বাসী তাঁরা—
